# Backend Full-Gate Diagnosis: `q15-trip-financial-governance`

Date: 2026-08-02
Scope: diagnose only; no code changes

## Executive Summary

`backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts` still hangs at current `HEAD` in isolation. The file's 9 subtests all pass, then the Node/`tsx` test worker stays alive and the file is reported as failed at file level. This is not only the earlier full-suite shared-database contention issue from 2026-08-02; I reproduced the same stuck state with a single-file run.

Root cause: the test exercises route paths that spawn unawaited out-of-band audit enrichment work (`backend/src/services/audit.service.ts:619-645`). That work keeps shared backend resources alive after the last assertion. At hang time, the isolated worker still held 3 Postgres sockets to `localhost:5441` and 1 Redis socket to `localhost:6391`. The test teardown does call `disconnectRedis()` and `client.end()` (`backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts:222-287`), so the blocker is not a missing teardown import; it is unfinished background work racing/overlapping with teardown of shared clients.

Concurrent local backend runs were an environmental amplifier for the earlier 12-minute broad-suite stall because they locked the same cleanup surfaces, but they are not the sole cause. Current `HEAD` still hangs in a single-file repro.

## Symptom

- Expected:
  `cd backend && ./node_modules/.bin/tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts`
  should exit after reporting the 9 passing q15 subtests.
- Actual:
  all 9 q15 subtests pass in about 1.7s to 2.5s, then the worker remains alive until externally terminated. The file is shown as:
  `✖ .../q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts`
  followed by
  `Interrupted while running:`
  `⚠ src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts`

## Evidence

### 1. Prior QA artifacts already isolated the file-level hang

- `qa/2026-08-02_chatbot-ocr-settings_backend-test.log`
  - Broad run note: backend run stopped making progress for more than 12 minutes at q15 while other full backend suites were also active.
  - Isolated rerun note: all 9 q15 subtests passed, but the runner did not exit.
- `qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_backend-test-final.log`
  - Again shows file-level failure at `q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts`.

### 2. Current `HEAD` isolated repro still hangs

Reproduced on 2026-08-02 with:

```bash
cd backend
./node_modules/.bin/tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts
```

Observed output tail before termination:

```text
✔ Q15 trip financial governance (1765.146334ms)
✖ /Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts (19.018958ms)
```

The process was still alive 30 seconds later and had to be terminated by the wrapper.

### 3. Live-hang resource capture shows open backend sockets after the last assertion

I ran the isolated test with a non-persistent runtime probe that dumps active handles after 5 seconds if the worker is still alive. That probe reported:

```text
ACTIVE_HANDLES [{"name":"Socket","localPort":59048,"remotePort":5441,"localAddress":"::1","remoteAddress":"::1",...},
{"name":"Socket","localPort":59053,"remotePort":5441,"localAddress":"::1","remoteAddress":"::1",...},
{"name":"Socket","localPort":59056,"remotePort":5441,"localAddress":"::1","remoteAddress":"::1",...},
{"name":"Socket","localPort":59057,"remotePort":6391,"localAddress":"::1","remoteAddress":"::1",...}]
```

Meaning: after the q15 assertions completed, the hung worker still held 3 PostgreSQL connections and 1 Redis connection.

### 4. The old “missing disconnectRedis” theory is false at current `HEAD`

Current source:

- `backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts:286`
  `await disconnectRedis();`
- `backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts:287`
  `await client.end();`

So the live bug is not “`disconnectRedis` imported but never called”.

### 5. Proven unawaited background DB work exists in the exercised path

`backend/src/services/audit.service.ts:619-645`:

- `scheduleAuditEnrichment(...)` launches `void auditEnrichmentHandler(...)`
- default handler is `defaultAuditEnrichment`
- `defaultAuditEnrichment(...)` performs additional database reads/writes (`backend/src/services/audit.service.ts:392-591`)

This is fire-and-forget work on the same shared `db` client imported by the test (`backend/src/db/index.ts:6-7`), and q15 hits many audited route paths:

- `auditLogMiddleware` mounted in test app: `backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts:211`
- Route mounts:
  - `../routes/trips`
  - `../routes/financial/payments.routes`
  - `../routes/financial/governance-actions.routes`

Those routes also touch Redis-backed invalidation paths, which explains the live Redis socket.

## Hypotheses Tested

### Hypothesis A: missing teardown call leaves Redis open

Result: eliminated.

Why: current `HEAD` teardown explicitly calls both `disconnectRedis()` and `client.end()` at `backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts:286-287`.

### Hypothesis B: only prior concurrent full-suite sessions caused the hang

Result: eliminated as sole cause.

Why: single-file isolated repro at current `HEAD` still hangs after all 9 q15 subtests pass.

### Hypothesis C: out-of-band background work keeps shared sockets alive past the last assertion

Result: confirmed.

Why:

- source proves fire-and-forget audit enrichment on shared DB (`backend/src/services/audit.service.ts:619-645`)
- runtime probe captured still-open Postgres and Redis sockets after q15 finished
- test teardown depends on shared singleton clients (`backend/src/db/index.ts:6-7`, `backend/src/lib/redis.ts:4-28`)

## Timeline

- 2026-08-02 earlier QA artifacts:
  broad backend suite stalled around q15 while other suites were also active against the same local services.
- 2026-08-02 current investigation:
  read current q15 test, teardown, audit service, Redis client, prior QA logs, and git history for q15.
- 2026-08-02 isolated repro 1:
  `pnpm exec tsx --test ... q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts`
  timed out after 45s; output showed all q15 subtests passed before hang.
- 2026-08-02 isolated repro 2:
  direct `./node_modules/.bin/tsx --test ...`
  timed out after 30s; same behavior.
- 2026-08-02 runtime-handle probe:
  confirmed live Postgres and Redis sockets after the suite body had completed.

## Why Now

`q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts` was recently changed by commit `099abde` on 2026-08-02 for the O2C completed-state work, but that diff only added POD/photo setup in `createInTransitTrip()`. It does not explain the open-handle behavior by itself.

The hang is exposed now because q15 drives multiple audited and cache-invalidating close/change/cancel flows through real route handlers, so the file is a high-volume stress case for shared out-of-band work. Concurrent local backend runs on the same DB/Redis made the earlier broad-suite stall much worse by locking cleanup concurrently, but the isolated repro proves the underlying leak remains even without those competing sessions.

## Root Cause

Confirmed root cause:

- `backend/src/services/audit.service.ts:619-645` schedules asynchronous audit enrichment with `void ...catch(...)` and does not provide a completion barrier for tests.
- `backend/src/tests/q15-trip-financial-governance.test.ts` uses real audited route handlers and shared singleton DB/Redis clients, then attempts teardown of those singletons in `after()` (`:222-287`).
- At runtime, after the test body completed, the worker still held 3 PostgreSQL sockets and 1 Redis socket.

So the repository-wide backend gate blocker is not an assertion failure inside q15; it is an open-handle/unfinished-background-work teardown bug exposed by q15.

## Blast Radius

- Any backend test that:
  - mounts audited route handlers,
  - uses the shared `db` singleton,
  - triggers Redis cache invalidation,
  - and tears down immediately without waiting for out-of-band work,
  can hang or flake similarly.
- Full backend runs are higher risk because shared local DB/Redis contention makes the cleanup race slower and more visible.

## Recurrence Prevention

1. Add a deterministic test-only barrier for audit enrichment completion, or disable audit enrichment explicitly in tests that do not assert it.
2. Avoid fire-and-forget background work against shared singleton clients during test teardown without a flush/join mechanism.
3. Keep backend full-suite runs serialized against one local DB/Redis instance, or isolate them per run, because concurrent sessions amplify cleanup lock contention.
4. Add a focused regression test around “all assertions pass, process exits cleanly” for q15-class governance suites.

## Unresolved Questions

- The evidence is sufficient to identify the open-handle class and root cause family. I did not run a patched validation that disables audit enrichment to measure whether that alone restores a clean exit, because this task was diagnosis-only.
</file>

