# UI/UX implementation specification

## Outcome and guardrails

Implement the approved operating chain inside the existing Silversea routes and shells:

`Lô hàng -> Điều vận -> Chi phí thu hồi -> Giấy báo nợ -> Phải thu / Phải trả -> Sổ quỹ / ngân hàng -> Lợi nhuận -> Tổng quan điều hành`

This report specifies responsive information architecture, component composition, interaction states, copy, accessibility, and frontend acceptance criteria. It does not authorize product-code work. Phase 1 decisions D1-D4 remain blocking for the affected actions and data states. Until accepted, implementation may build no UI that implies legal-invoice issuance, reconciled bank balance, customer-message authority, or complete dispatcher/salesperson attribution.

Scope boundary:

- Preserve `/dashboard`, `/shipments`, `/dispatch`, `/expenses`, `/debt`, `/payables`, `/finance`, `/profit`, and `/portal/*`.
- Preserve the internal `Layout` and separate `CustomerPortalLayout`; no new shell or `/finance/*` duplicate route tree.
- CUS is the existing `CLERK` role and uses live row scope. UI capability is an affordance only, never authorization.
- Preserve the flat emerald Silversea system: no shadows, no gradients, no nested decorative card stacks, no new component library.
- Display every financial amount with full `vi-VN` digits and tabular numerals. Never use `k`, `tr`, `tỷ`, `M`, or `B` on finance/executive surfaces.
- Database pagination/filtering remains authoritative. The UI must not compensate for unbounded endpoints by slicing a full response.

## Source and library decisions

### Existing Silversea primitives to reuse

- Canonical: `DataTable`, `Pagination`, `EmptyState`, `Tabs`, `TextField`, `SelectField`, `NumberField`, `CrudFormModal`, `useTableQueryState`, `useDebouncedValue`.
- Existing shell and page primitives: `Layout`, `CustomerPortalLayout`, `PageHeader`, `Breadcrumbs`, `Button`, `Modal`, `Drawer`, `Panel`, `Banner`, `Skeleton`, `Toast`, `Money`.
- Existing page patterns: `/shipments` desktop table + mobile manifest cards, `/dispatch` bounded split workbench, portal list/detail shell, AR/AP responsive cards, URL-backed month/filter patterns.
- Existing tokens: Be Vietnam Pro for interface text, JetBrains Mono for numerics, emerald primary, semantic status colors, `--control-h: 44px`, 4/8px spacing rhythm, no elevation.

### UI catalog inputs

- Untitled UI consulted: `table`, `sidebar-section-dividers`, `sidebar-dual-tier`, `filters-menu`, `charts-base`, `tabs`, `pagination`, `empty-state`. Reuse anatomy and interaction discipline only.
- Tailkit consulted: `a-l-dark-sidebar-06`, `a-c-navigation-08`, `a-c-page-headings-04`, `a-c-statistics-11`, `a-c-tables-14`. The dual-rail shell is rejected because Silversea already has a compact/collapsible sidebar; retain only grouped navigation, compact headings, statistics, and dense table ideas.
- Shadcn MCP was not callable in this session. Use the local Radix/daisyUI-style primitives as the compatible baseline. Do not install Shadcn or Untitled UI packages for this work.
- UI Pro Max recommendations used: flat/data-dense logistics dashboard, bounded large lists, 44px controls, clear state feedback, `vi-VN` typography. Its blue/orange palette and exaggerated-minimalism recommendation are rejected because they conflict with the canonical emerald, compact operational design.

## Canonical responsive frame

| Viewport | Shell | Workspace behavior | Primary action |
|---|---|---|---|
| `>= 1200px` | Existing 248px/collapsed 48px sidebar | Bounded two-pane queue/detail where the task benefits; each pane scrolls independently | Page header or sticky detail footer |
| `1024-1199px` | Existing collapsible sidebar | One primary pane; detail opens as route or right drawer; compact KPI strip | Header; never hidden in overflow |
| `768-1023px` | Drawer sidebar + topbar | Queue/detail becomes accessible tabs or full-width sheet; table only when all critical columns fit | Sticky section footer where action is transactional |
| `320-767px` | Drawer/topbar; customer keeps bottom nav | Card-first list; filter summary + full-height filter sheet; route-based detail | Bottom safe-area action bar, maximum two visible actions |

Shared dimensions:

- Page content gutters: 16px mobile, 20-24px tablet, 24-34px desktop.
- Workspace maximum usable height: `calc(100dvh - shell header - page header - gutters)`. Do not hard-code a viewport height that hides browser chrome.
- Queue row: 52-64px desktop depending on evidence density. Mobile card: content-driven, minimum 92px.
- Controls: minimum 44x44px, 8px gap between adjacent targets. Mobile input font is at least 16px.
- Bounded queue defaults: 25 rows; allow 25/50 only where the endpoint supports it. Never render 500 rows as one DOM list. Virtualize only when a deliberate non-paginated sub-list exceeds 50 visible rows.
- Page-level `overflow-x` is prohibited. Wide tables scroll only inside a labeled table region and must have a mobile card alternative for primary workflows.
- Preserve URL state for filters, tabs, sort, page, period, dimension, and selected row when practical. Back navigation restores queue scroll and selection.

## Role navigation and homes

Navigation must be projected from the same server capability envelope used by route guards and global search. Section headings are stable; item presence and order are capability-derived.

| Role | Home | Navigation priority | Explicit exclusions |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ADMIN` | `/dashboard` | Tổng quan; Vận hành; Tài chính; Dữ liệu; Hệ thống | None beyond separately guarded destructive actions |
| `MANAGER` | `/dashboard` | Tổng quan; Vận hành; Tài chính & phê duyệt; Báo cáo | Admin-only configuration and identity mutation |
| `ACCOUNTANT` | `/debt` | Phải thu; Phải trả; Chi phí; Tạm ứng; Sổ quỹ / ngân hàng; Lợi nhuận; shipment read paths | Dispatch controls, treasury administration, executive dashboard unless explicit capability says otherwise |
| `CLERK` | `/shipments` after row-scope gate; otherwise current create route | Lô hàng được giao; Tạo lô hàng; Hồ sơ; Chi phí cần kiểm tra | Global shipment count/list, Giấy báo nợ approval, AR/AP, treasury, profitability, dashboard |
| `CUSTOMER` | `/portal/shipments` | Lô hàng; Giấy báo nợ; Sao kê | Entire internal shell |
| `DRIVER` | Current driver home | Unchanged driver portal | Entire internal shell |
| `FORWARDER` | Current forwarder home | Unchanged forwarder portal | Entire internal shell |

Internal sidebar order for operations remains the approved Vietnamese sequence where those capabilities exist: `Đội xe`, `Phân xe`, `Sổ chuyến đi`, `Lô hàng`. Finance-first ordering for `ACCOUNTANT` is an intentional role override, not a global reorder.

Navigation behavior:

- Active destination: solid emerald-tinted state, visible 3x20px status strip, text weight change; never color alone.
- Counts show actionable work, not total records. Label count semantics in accessible text.
- A destination not available in the current rollout mode is absent. If previously deep-linked, show a page-level unavailable state with route back; do not render a dead disabled nav item.
- Global search uses the same capability-filtered catalog and preserves route semantics. No static finance destinations for unauthorized roles.
- Route change moves focus to `<main>`/page heading. Drawer/menu close restores focus to its opener.

## Shared workspace composition

### `BoundedWorkspace` pattern

Create a shared primitive only if the third page repeats the same shell. Until then, compose locally from existing primitives.

Desktop anatomy:

1. Page header: breadcrumb, one-line purpose, one primary action.
2. Compact metric strip: maximum 4 items; metrics support decisions on this page only.
3. Sticky filter/action bar.
4. Queue pane with result count, bounded scroll, stable skeleton rows, pagination.
5. Detail pane with heading, status, evidence sections, audit timeline, sticky action footer.

Tablet/mobile anatomy:

1. Page title + single primary action.
2. Two or three summary facts; additional metrics behind `Xem thêm`.
3. Search + filter trigger showing active-filter count.
4. Card list.
5. Detail is a route by default. Use a sheet only for short, reversible inspection or filter selection.

Interaction contracts:

- A page transition or filter request makes stale mutation controls non-interactive and shows stable-size skeletons. Never allow actions against stale rows.
- Query error remains in place with `Thử lại`; do not present it as an empty list.
- `409` conflict: keep entered data, show `Dữ liệu đã thay đổi. Tải lại để xem bản mới nhất.`, and offer `Tải lại` as the primary recovery.
- Destructive/reversal actions require a confirmation dialog stating financial consequence. Governance submission buttons show pending state and cannot double-submit.
- Empty states distinguish no records, no filter match, no assignment, unavailable authority, and denied/revoked scope.

## Surface 1 — CUS shipment coordination

### `/shipments`: assigned operating queue

Page title stays `Lô hàng`. CLERK subtitle is `Lô hàng trong phạm vi được giao`; office read users see `Theo dõi hồ sơ và tiến độ lô hàng`.

Queue controls:

- Search: shipment code, B/L, booking, container, customer; reuse Vietnamese diacritic-insensitive normalization.
- Filter groups: `Trạng thái`, `Mức độ hoàn thiện hồ sơ`, `Sẵn sàng điều vận`, `Cần khách hàng xác nhận`, `Người phụ trách`, `Khoảng ngày`.
- Quick segments: `Cần xử lý`, `Đang chờ`, `Đã sẵn sàng`, `Tất cả`. Counts are server-scoped and query-consistent.
- Row/card priority: shipment code + customer; next operational milestone; route/container summary; readiness warning; acknowledgement/delivery state; status.
- CLERK no-assignment state: `Bạn chưa được giao lô hàng nào` + `Liên hệ quản lý để được phân công.` No global fallback and no total count leak.

At `>=1200px`, optional detail preview may occupy 40-44% of the workspace. It must deep-link to `/shipments/:id`, preserve keyboard row selection, and never replace the canonical detail route. Below 1200px, use list/detail routes rather than nested horizontal panes.

### `/shipments/:id`: operational hub

Desktop layout: 8/4 grid with the operational record on the left and `Việc cần làm` on the right. Tablet/mobile is a linear document with sticky in-page section tabs.

Section order:

1. `Tóm tắt`: status, customer, route, cargo, container count, accepted dispatcher, salesperson attribution state.
2. `Việc cần làm`: missing dossier facts, readiness warnings, customer acknowledgement, unresolved change request. Advisory warnings use `Cảnh báo`, never a false blocking label.
3. `Hồ sơ lô hàng`: B/L, booking, declarations, documents, containers. Never expose raw `storageKey` in customer-facing views.
4. `Điều vận`: readiness evidence, handoff accepted by/time, linked trip, reassignment/supersession.
5. `Phối hợp khách hàng`: internal operational event list and separately classified customer-visible delivery/acknowledgement state.
6. `Lịch sử`: immutable status and change-request timeline.

Customer communication is not a chat UI. Use a vertical event timeline with explicit labels:

- `Nội bộ` — visible only internally.
- `Đã gửi khách hàng` — immutable allowlisted snapshot.
- `Đã chuyển giao` — delivery evidence, not acknowledgement.
- `Khách hàng đã xác nhận` — acknowledgement tied to event version.
- `Gửi thất bại` — show retry/recovery state to authorized operator.

### Customer portal shipment detail

Extend the existing portal detail, not the shell. Order: current status, next milestone, shipment summary, customer-visible timeline, documents allowed for customer display, acknowledgement action. Hide internal actor, notes, raw diffs, pending changes, contact data, and storage keys.

Mobile acknowledgement uses a sticky safe-area footer with one action: `Xác nhận đã nhận thông tin`. Confirmation dialog repeats the event title/version and clarifies that it acknowledges receipt, not acceptance of charges.

## Surface 2 — recoverable-cost queue and Giấy báo nợ

### `/expenses`: role-composed workbench

Do not create a second expense authority or a separate CUS app. Add role-aware tabs from the existing route:

- CLERK: `Cần kiểm tra`, `Đã gửi duyệt`, `Đã xử lý`.
- ACCOUNTANT/MANAGER/ADMIN: `Chi phí`, `Chi phí thu hồi`, `Cần phê duyệt`, subject to capability.

The recoverable queue uses database-backed filters: customer, shipment/trip, business date, evidence state, approval state, billed state. Row/card content:

- Expense type and amount in full digits.
- Customer + shipment/trip source.
- Evidence: `Đủ chứng từ`, `Thiếu chứng từ`, `Được phép không hóa đơn`.
- Governance state: `Chờ kiểm tra`, `Đã trả lại`, `Đã duyệt`, `Từ chối`.
- Billing eligibility: `Có thể lập Giấy báo nợ`, `Đã được ghi nhận`, `Chỉ điều chỉnh`.
- One specific blocked reason supplied by server.

Desktop: 56-60% queue + detail panel. Mobile: cards open a full detail route/sheet; evidence and reason appear before actions. Primary CLERK action is `Gửi kiểm tra`; `Trả lại bổ sung` is secondary. No CLERK control may say `Duyệt Giấy báo nợ`.

### Billing builder/panel

Use a flat, three-part composition:

1. `Nguồn chi phí`: selectable eligible lines with evidence/provenance and one-claim state.
2. `Nội dung Giấy báo nợ`: separate `Khoản thu hộ/chi hộ` principal from `Phí dịch vụ`; show subtotal, tax, and total in full digits.
3. `Kiểm tra & phát hành`: maker/checker/approver timeline, due date, source lock, expected version, and issue status.

Selection summary stays visible in a sticky footer. On mobile, it reads `Đã chọn X khoản · 123.456.789 ₫` and opens a review step before submit. Never silently disable a source: keep it visible with its block reason when useful for recovery.

### Legal invoice reference

Present `Giấy báo nợ` and `Hóa đơn pháp lý` as separate labeled facts. Under reference-only D1, allowed states are:

- `Chưa có tham chiếu hóa đơn pháp lý`
- `Đang ghi nhận tham chiếu`
- `Đã ghi nhận hóa đơn pháp lý` + external reference
- `Không xác định — cần kiểm tra`
- `Ghi nhận thất bại` + authorized recovery

Never label a Giấy báo nợ number as invoice number. Invoice reference status never changes the displayed AR total.

### `/portal/debit-notes`

Keep current list route. Add status, original/processing due dates, total, legal-invoice reference state, and clear `Xác nhận` / `Phản hồi` actions. Replace immediate dispute mutation with a dialog/sheet containing a required labeled reason, character count, expected-version handling, and unsaved-dismiss confirmation. On success, return focus to the originating row/action.

## Surface 3 — AR, AP, and book balances

### `/debt`: accounts receivable queue

Header KPIs: `Phải thu`, `Quá hạn`, `Tiền chưa phân bổ`, `Khách hàng chạm hạn mức`. Keep one row, not a decorative hero.

Queue columns desktop: customer, outstanding, overdue, oldest due date, dispute, credit utilization, reminder state, last receipt. Mobile card priority: customer, outstanding, overdue/due state, credit warning, next action.

Filters: due/aging bucket, dispute, reminder, credit band, unapplied cash, customer, `asOf`. Drill-down must preserve filters in URL.

### `/debt/:id`: AR detail

Use tabs: `Nghĩa vụ`, `Thu tiền & phân bổ`, `Nhắc nợ`, `Lịch sử`. The overview displays a clear equation: opening + new obligations - allocations - non-cash offsets = closing. Each obligation links to its shipment/trip/Giấy báo nợ authority.

Receipt flow is a focused multi-section form, not a wizard modal:

- Treasury account (required after cutover), value date, physical/external reference.
- Gross receipt amount.
- Optional explicit allocation instructions; otherwise show `Hệ thống sẽ phân bổ từ khoản đến hạn cũ nhất`.
- Allocation preview with outstanding cap and `Tiền chưa phân bổ` remainder.
- Governance submission summary and immutable result links.

Label balances precisely: `Số dư công nợ`, `Tiền đã nhận chưa phân bổ`, and `Số dư ghi sổ tài khoản` are different values.

### `/payables` and `/payables/:id`: accounts payable

List tabs: `Nhà cung cấp`, `Đơn vị vận tải`. Filters: aging, due, category, evidence, payment state, duplicate reference. Row/card shows payable source, contractual/processing due dates, outstanding, paid, and evidence warning.

Detail tabs: `Nghĩa vụ`, `Thanh toán`, `Chứng từ`, `Lịch sử`. Fuel allocation displays actual slips/logs per vehicle; never an equal split. Payment flow mirrors the AR receipt form but uses outbound terminology and keeps overpayment explicit.

Debt offset appears in AR and AP histories as `Bù trừ công nợ · Không dùng tiền mặt`. It never appears in cash/bank movement lists.

### `/finance`: source-linked book-balance summary

This phase does not create a full treasury workspace. Add a compact read-only section above or alongside the existing P&L:

- `Tiền mặt — Số dư ghi sổ`
- `Ngân hàng — Số dư ghi sổ`
- `Cập nhật đến <asOf>`
- Status: `Đầy đủ`, `Một phần`, or `Chưa khả dụng` with text + icon.

Account rows show account name/code, type, opening balance date, inflow, outflow, book balance, freshness, and source-link coverage. `Một phần` must explain the unsupported activity. Never use `Số dư ngân hàng` without the qualifier `ghi sổ`, and never imply statement reconciliation.

## Surface 4 — profitability and executive dashboard

### `/dashboard`: MANAGER/ADMIN executive view

Use progressive disclosure, not all 12 KPIs as equal cards.

1. Decision strip: `Doanh thu hôm nay`, `Doanh thu tháng`, `Chi phí tháng`, `Lợi nhuận tháng`, `Phải thu`, `Quá hạn`.
2. Liquidity strip: `Tiền mặt — ghi sổ`, `Ngân hàng — ghi sổ`, each preserving partial/unavailable state.
3. `Việc cần xử lý`: overdue AR, partial treasury, reconciliation mismatch, missing attribution, governance queue.
4. Analysis: revenue/profit trend, top customers, top debtors, cost by type, profit by vehicle.

Every group shows `Cập nhật đến`, definition version, and a keyboard-reachable `Cách tính`. Do not render unavailable sources as zero. A partial dashboard has a persistent scoped banner and marks affected cards only; unaffected data stays usable.

Charts:

- Trend: line/area for revenue vs profit, accessible legend and table alternative.
- Ranking: horizontal bars for top 10, direct full-digit labels on desktop; mobile shows ordered rows, not cramped bars.
- Cost breakdown: horizontal bars; no donut when more than five categories.
- Profit by vehicle: sortable table/list with margin and full amount; bar is supplementary.
- Chart tooltips must work by keyboard/focus, not hover only. Use the canonical semantic palette and never red/green as the only distinction.

### `/profit` and `/finance` profitability drill-down

Preserve routes and put dimension/period/asOf in query parameters. Dimension selector values use natural Vietnamese labels: `Khách hàng`, `Tuyến đường`, `Đầu xe`, `Điều vận`, `Kinh doanh`, `Tháng`, `Năm`, `Container`.

Top strip: revenue, direct cost, shared overhead, profit, missing attribution. Detail table/card includes stable source link, revenue, direct cost, allocated/unallocated state, profit, margin, coverage. Keep `Chi phí chung chưa phân bổ`, `Thiếu thông tin phân bổ`, and `Lợi nhuận chưa chia theo chủ xe` as three distinct rows/states.

For mobile, show dimension + period controls first, then reconciliation status, then cards. Definitions and `asOf` remain reachable without horizontal scroll.

## State and copy contract

| State | Visual treatment | Required copy/action |
|---|---|---|
| Loading | Stable skeleton matching final geometry; `aria-busy` | `Đang tải…`; no stale actions |
| Empty | Flat bordered section, no decorative illustration required | Specific reason + next valid action |
| No match | Preserve filters | `Không có kết quả phù hợp` + `Xóa bộ lọc` |
| Partial | Amber icon + text + affected scope | Explain missing authority; never substitute zero |
| Stale/conflict | Amber banner in detail/action region | `Dữ liệu đã thay đổi` + `Tải lại` |
| Denied/revoked | Neutral blocked state without record counts | `Bạn không còn quyền xem dữ liệu này` + safe route back |
| Error | Red icon + concise cause/recovery | `Thử lại`; preserve user input |
| Success | Inline result + polite toast | State what was recorded and provide source reference |

Approved terminology:

- `Lô hàng`, `Phân xe`, `Sổ chuyến đi`, `Đội xe`.
- `Chi phí thu hồi`, `Khoản thu hộ/chi hộ`, `Phí dịch vụ`.
- `Giấy báo nợ`; `Hóa đơn pháp lý` only for the separate reference.
- `Công nợ phải thu`, `Công nợ phải trả`, `Tiền chưa phân bổ`, `Bù trừ công nợ`.
- `Số dư ghi sổ`, `Một phần`, `Chưa khả dụng`; do not use `Đã đối soát ngân hàng` without statement authority.
- Use `Dự án`, never `Công trường`, on any downstream reused label.

## Accessibility and interaction acceptance

- Semantic `<button>`, `<a>/<Link>`, `<table>`, `<label>`, headings, lists, and definition lists before ARIA.
- All icon-only buttons have Vietnamese `aria-label`; decorative icons use `aria-hidden`.
- Visible `:focus-visible` state on rows, cards, tabs, filters, chart points, and sticky actions.
- Tabs implement roving focus with Arrow/Home/End and connect tab to panel with `aria-controls`/`aria-labelledby`.
- Sortable tables expose `aria-sort`; selectable rows use native checkboxes with one combined label/hit target.
- Async status uses `aria-live="polite"`; validation/conflict uses `role="alert"` where interruption is necessary.
- Forms have persistent labels, helper text, inline errors, first-invalid focus, and unsaved-change protection.
- Sheet/dialog: focus trap, Escape close, body scroll lock, labelled title, cancel path, opener-focus restoration, `overscroll-behavior: contain`.
- Status always includes text/icon, never color only. Normal text contrast >= 4.5:1; large/glyph contrast >= 3:1.
- Motion only for opacity/transform at 120-240ms and respects `prefers-reduced-motion`; no decorative scroll reveal in operational workspaces.
- Customer/finance identifiers and long Vietnamese labels wrap or expose the full value; truncation must have an accessible full-value mechanism.

## Frontend performance contract

- Fetch independent dashboard authorities concurrently; render partial source failures without blocking unrelated panels.
- Route-split existing heavy pages and charts; load chart modules only when the analysis section is visible/needed.
- Memoize column definitions and expensive view models; do not subscribe whole pages to state used only in callbacks.
- Keep URL/query keys isolated by role-safe filters, page, period, dimension, rollout version, capability version, and `asOf` as required by the API contract.
- Debounce search by 250-350ms. Abort/ignore stale responses and keep stale mutation controls disabled.
- Use pagination or windowing for 500+ records. Reserve geometry for skeletons/charts to avoid layout shift.
- Do not calculate financial totals, aging, eligibility, allocation, reconciliation, or profitability in React. Consume server-authoritative values.

## Proposed frontend file ownership

| Surface | Primary files | Supporting tests/styles |
|---|---|---|
| Capability navigation | `shared/src/navigation/pageCatalog.ts`, `frontend/src/App.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx`, `frontend/src/lib/routes.ts`, `frontend/src/data/searchRegistry.ts` | `Layout.test.ts`, route/search matrix tests |
| CUS shipment | `ShipmentsPage.tsx`, `ShipmentDetailPage.tsx`, portal shipment pages | Existing page CSS/tests; new coordination-focused tests |
| Recoverable/Debit Note | `ExpenseListPage.tsx`, `BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx`, `BillingDocumentsPanel.tsx`, `PortalDebitNotesPage.tsx` | Recoverable queue/builder/portal tests |
| AR/AP/book balance | `DebtListPage.tsx`, `DebtDetailPage.tsx`, `PayableListPage.tsx`, `PayableDetailPage.tsx`, `FinancePage.tsx` | Existing CSS/tests plus source-linked balance states |
| Profit/dashboard | `DashboardPage.tsx`, `FinancePage.tsx`, `ProfitPage.tsx`, dashboard hooks/client | Canonical KPI, full-digit, drill-down, partial/error tests |
| Shared only after repetition | `frontend/src/design-system/` | Isolated keyboard/responsive tests |

Do not exceed page composition responsibility: extract domain sections to `features/<domain>/components/` when a touched page would remain over approximately 200 lines. Do not create a generic abstraction until three real pages share the same behavior.

## Responsive and role QA matrix

Minimum viewports: `1440x900`, `1200x800`, `1024x768`, `768x1024`, `390x844`, `320x568`.

For each affected role/surface prove:

- Intended nav item, role home, route, direct URL, refresh, back/forward, and global-search reach.
- Forbidden route/action is absent in UI and denied by backend; page visibility and action visibility are separate assertions.
- No page-level horizontal overflow; long labels and full VND remain readable.
- Primary action visible and all touch targets at least 44px.
- Keyboard traversal, focus restoration, dialog/sheet behavior, live state feedback, and reduced motion.
- Loading, no assignment, empty, no match, partial, stale, revoked, error, and success states.
- Realistic 55-vehicle and 500+ shipment/order data with bounded queue/detail scrolling, deterministic pagination, stable interaction, and no 500-row DOM render.
- Portal remains separate and leaks no internal shell, actor, note, raw diff, storage key, or cross-customer data.

## Delivery order

1. After Phase 1 decision acceptance, freeze capability/action matrix and exact Vietnamese labels.
2. Align route/nav/search/home affordances without changing verified backend policy implicitly.
3. Implement CUS assigned shipment queue/detail and customer-visible coordination projection.
4. Implement recoverable queue and Giấy báo nợ composition.
5. Implement bounded AR/AP and source-linked book-balance read states.
6. Replace dashboard/profit client derivations with canonical APIs and this information hierarchy.
7. Run focused tests after each surface; then full role, viewport, volume, accessibility, and financial-flow QA under the plan's mandatory gates.

## Unresolved questions and implementation gates

- D1: confirm reference-only legal invoice language and the authorizing event before exposing any actionable invoice state.
- D2: confirm exact treasury read/operate/admin capability and when account selection becomes required.
- D3: approve the internal/customer-visible/delivery/acknowledgement authority matrix before implementing the coordination timeline.
- D4: approve dispatcher, salesperson, and canonical financial-version ownership before rendering those dimensions as complete.
- Resolve every `Per policy` / `Explicit capability only` role-matrix cell before navigation implementation. In particular: ACCOUNTANT dispatch visibility, ACCOUNTANT profitability reach, MANAGER AR/AP actions, and treasury administration.
- Decide whether shipment detail preview at `>=1200px` materially improves throughput after measuring with real CLERK users. The canonical route must work without it.

Status: DONE

Summary: Build-ready responsive UI/UX specification completed for the CUS-to-finance workflow, grounded in current routes, primitives, role guards, design tokens, and phase authority boundaries.

Concerns/Blockers: Product implementation remains blocked on Phase 1 D1-D4 and unresolved action-level role-policy cells. Shadcn MCP was unavailable; local primitives are the required compatible baseline.
