## Canonical Workflow

```text
Master data seed
  -> shipment / booking planning
  -> dispatch confirmation and execution
  -> debit-note / transport-summary generation
  -> invoice issuance / reconciliation
  -> AR/AP aging and reminders
  -> monthly profit / loss close
```

### Workflow Stages

1. Master data setup
   - customer / vendor / factory / route / port / vehicle / staff entities are seeded from the template books
   - this is the app's canonical reference data layer, not live transactional history

2. Planning and intake
   - customer, factory, bill/book, container, route, date, vessel / truck, and note fields are captured in the CUS planning sheet
   - the workflow splits into import/export and detailed / all modes

3. Dispatch and execution
   - transport rows record route, truck, container, weight, CBM, loading/unloading, date, and note fields
   - the debit-note template and transport summary templates aggregate line items, fees, and taxes

4. Settlement and reconciliation
   - debt sheets track invoice value, disbursements, paid amount, remaining amount, due date, actual payment date, and warning status
   - reminder text is generated from the debt sheet for email / notice workflows

5. Monthly close and reporting
   - daily and monthly P&L sheets aggregate revenue, vendor cost, fixed cost, variable cost, and financial cost
   - aging reports and profit reports support finance review, not operational dispatch

## Workbook-to-Domain Mapping

