# Phase 2: Seed Script for Customer Data

## Overview

Build a single, idempotent TypeScript seed script
(`backend/src/seed-customer.ts`) that (1) wipes all **business** data in
FK-safe order while **preserving `users` and auth/account tables**, and
(2) re-inserts the customer's real master data from
`docs/BIẾU MẪU BÁO CÁO/29.7 - DATA PM.xlsx` plus ~5-10 representative sample
trips drawn from `29.7 - DEMO KẾ TOÁN.xlsx` and `BẢNG DEMO ... CUS-ĐIỀU XE.xlsx`.

This script is the **only** seed used for both local and staging reseeds
(Phase 3 and Phase 4). It retires the stale raw-SQL pattern
(`deploy/seed-vantai*.sql`, `reset-seed.ts`) which FK-fails on today's schema.

## Requirements

- Functional:
  - Idempotent — safe to run twice (`onConflictDoNothing` / `onConflictDoUpdate`).
  - Preserves `users` (and `push_subscriptions`, `user_onboarding_*`,
    `agent_*`, `faq_entries`, `knowledge_chunks`, `idempotency_keys`).
  - Relinks existing driver **logins** to representative real driver records
    (per D3) so the driver portal still resolves `getDriverByUserId()`.
  - Inserts the customer's real master data (see Source→Target map).
  - Inserts ~5-10 sample shipments+trips in varied states (DRAFT,
    IN_PROGRESS, DELIVERED, CLOSED) so reports and the dispatch workflow demo
    realistically — but **no `LOCKED`/`COMPLETED` trips with fabricated
    ledger postings beyond what's needed for the sample** (avoid fake
    financial completion).
  - Dry-run mode (`--dry-run`) that prints the planned changes without
    writing, for the staging pre-flight (Phase 4).
  - Generated identifier maps (e.g. Excel-BKS → truckId) printed to stdout
    for audit.
- Non-functional:
  - **Drizzle ORM only — no raw SQL** (repo invariant).
  - Financial values inserted via the existing authorities
    (`round2dp()`, `computeTripTotals()`), never hand-typed VND strings that
    bypass precision rules.
  - Runs under `tsx` and through `make seed:customer` (new target).

## Architecture

```
backend/src/seed-customer.ts         ← entry: parse args, orchestrate wipe+seed
  ├─ backend/src/seed/wipe.ts        ← FK-ordered DELETE (excludes users/auth)
  ├─ backend/src/seed/customers-data.ts ← typed constants from the Excel sheets
  ├─ backend/src/seed/seed-customers.ts  ← suppliers, customers, partners
  ├─ backend/src/seed/seed-fleet.ts     ← trucks (BKS), trailers, drivers (NHÂN SỰ)
  ├─ backend/src/seed/seed-reference.ts ← routes, cargo_types, ports, container_types
  ├─ backend/src/seed/seed-pricing.ts   ← pricing_tables, fuel_config/norms, lift_pricing
  ├─ backend/src/seed/seed-debit-template.ts ← Long Minh debit-note template
  ├─ backend/src/seed/seed-samples.ts   ← ~5-10 sample shipments + trips
  └─ backend/src/seed/relink-driver-logins.ts ← map existing logins → real drivers
```

A shared `backend/src/seed/data/` folder holds the extracted, typed customer
values (not the xlsx files themselves — the values are committed as TS so the
script runs without an Excel parser and the data is reviewable in code review).
The xlsx parsing is a one-time extraction step done in this phase.

### Wipe order (FK-safe, excludes users)

Derived from the full table inventory (planning scout). Grouped leaf-first:

1. Trip children → `trips` → `trip_code_counters`
2. Shipment children → `shipments`
3. Billing/ledger children → `ledger`, `billing_documents*`, `period_locks`,
   `governance_actions`, `debit_note_templates`, `payment_*`,
   `credit_override_requests`
4. Salary/advance children → salary/advance tables, `management_fees`
5. Cap table → `truck_cap_table`, `cap_table_history`, `distributions`,
   `debt_offsets`
6. Expenses → `expense_photos`, `expenses`
7. Fleet → fuel tables, `tires`, `trailers`, `trucks`, `drivers`,
   `driver_*`
8. Customers/partners → `customer_email_logs`, `user_customer_links`,
   `user_business_unit_links`, `business_calendar_days`, `business_units`,
   `customers`, `partners`
9. Routes/pricing → `route_polylines`, `ancillary_revenue`, `lift_pricing`,
   `weight_pricing_tiers`, `road_allowances`, `pricing_tables`,
   `cargo_types`, `routes`
10. Suppliers/categories → `suppliers`, `expense_categories`, `penalty_reasons`,
    `penalties`
11. Reference → `forwarder_expense_types`, `container_types`, `seal_types`,
    `ports`, `road_config`

**Never wiped:** `users`, `push_subscriptions`, `user_onboarding_*`,
`onboarding_events`, `user_customer_links`/`user_business_unit_links` (these are
wiped under step 8 because they tie to business entities that are recreated —
they get re-linked by `relink-driver-logins.ts` and the customer-link step).

### Source → Target map (DATA PM workbook)

| Excel sheet | Target tables | Notes / normalization |
|-------------|---------------|------------------------|
| THÔNG TIN NCC | `suppliers`, `customers` (linked) | Long Minh: supplier row + customer row linked via `linkedSupplierId`/`linkedCustomerId`. Payment terms (HẠN TT CHI HỘ 25, CƯỚC 15) → `customers.paymentTermDays`. |
| THÔNG TIN KH | `customers` | (Empty in the file beyond headers — placeholder for future customers. Document, don't fabricate.) |
| NHÀ MÁY | `cargoTypes`-adjacent / reference | **Representability gap** (Phase 1). Store NEWEB/ASKEY/SUNRISE/SJ Tech/S-CONNECT as reference entries in the most appropriate existing table (decision in implementation); their rich notes (address, MST nâng hạ, GPS link) become `note`/`address`. Do not invent a new `factories` table in this plan. |
| TUYẾN ĐƯỜNG | `routes` | (Sheet lists columns but no rows.) Seed canonical routes derived from MẪU BÁO GIÁ instead (Hải Phòng–NEWEB, –ASKEY, –SUNRISE+SJ). |
| LOẠI HÌNH XE | `trucks` (BKS), `trailers` (romooc), `drivers` (named driver) | Normalize BKS punctuation (`15H-052.82` vs `15H - 052.82`). Driver name → match against NHÂN SỰ. **Note:** `trucks` has no tonnage column — tonnage (33T/29T/22T) is captured per-cargo/per-trip, so the "Loại hình xe" text (NẶNG 2 CẦU 3 GIÀN, etc.) is stored on the truck as a model/classifier only if a column exists, else documented as a gap. |
| MẪU BÁO GIÁ | `pricing_tables`, `weight_pricing_tiers`, `fuel_config`, `fuel_norms` | The fuel-surcharge formula column (`giá dầu hiện tại`, định mức dầu/KM, % chia sẻ 2/2.5/4%) maps to `fuel_config` + `fuel_norms`. Cước gốc per size × route → `pricing_tables`. **Implement the formula, don't hardcode the surcharged totals.** |
| THÔNG TIN CẢNG BÃI | `ports` | 17 ports/yards → `ports` (name, address, web portal URL in notes). |
| DS NHÂN SỰ | `drivers` (the ~28 "Lái xe" rows) | Office staff (Giám đốc/PGĐ/Kế toán/Cus/Ops) are **not** seeded as users (D4); only the ~28 driver rows become `drivers` records, MST → `drivers` has no tax column so drop or store in note. |
| MẪU DEBIT LONG MINH | `debit_note_templates` | One template matching the 20-column layout (Silver Sea issuer identity: MST 0201985011, address, bank account 0031000391518 VCB). VAT 8%. |

### Driver-login relink (D3)

After seeding the 28 real drivers:

1. List existing driver-role users (local: laixe/thu/pho/quyet; staging:
   laixe/thu/nam/tuan/duc — discovered at runtime, not hardcoded).
2. Match each to a representative real driver by a stable key. The Excel
   trucks-to-driver map (LOẠI HÌNH XE) names specific drivers (e.g.
   "Đinh Thanh Thịnh", "Nguyễn Duy Tuấn"); pick the 4-9 real drivers that the
   sample trips will use, and link the existing logins to those records.
3. Set `drivers.userId` for the chosen real drivers; clear `userId` on the
   rest (they remain records without login).
4. Update `users.driverId`-equivalent link if present in schema.

### Sample trips (~5-10)

Drawn from `DEMO KẾ TOÁN` TH VẬN TẢI rows (e.g. the 4 NEWEB/Long Minh
container trips on 25/06, 2/7, 12/7, 13/7) and the CUS-ĐIỀU XE example. Each
sample trip carries realistic: customer (Long Minh), factory, route, cont
type/number, BKS (mapped to a seeded truck), carrier (SS own vs ABC external),
receivable/payable breakdown. **Trips are seeded in CREATED/IN_PROGRESS or
DELIVERED states only** — no fabricated COMPLETED+locked-ledger entries. This
keeps the books honest while still demonstrating the workflow.

## Implementation Steps

1. Extract the customer values from the xlsx workbooks into typed TS constants
   under `backend/src/seed/data/` (one-time; commit the TS, not the xlsx).
   Normalize BKS punctuation, trim whitespace, drop the Chinese-text blocks
   from NHÀ MÁY notes (keep the Vietnamese + MST + GPS link).
2. Implement `seed/wipe.ts` with the 11-group FK-ordered wipe, gated by
   `--dry-run`.
3. Implement `seed-customers.ts`, `seed-fleet.ts`, `seed-reference.ts`,
   `seed-pricing.ts`, `seed-debit-template.ts` — each idempotent, each printing
   a row-count summary.
4. Implement `relink-driver-logins.ts` per D3.
5. Implement `seed-samples.ts` for the ~5-10 trips via the existing
   `createShipment` / `transitionShipmentStatus` services (reuse, don't
   hand-roll inserts).
6. Wire `seed-customer.ts` entry: `--dry-run` prints plan; default runs
   wipe → reference → fleet → customers → pricing → debit template → relink →
   samples.
7. Add `make seed:customer` target (`cd backend && npx tsx src/seed-customer.ts`).
8. Document the script in `HANDOFF.md` and a short section in
   `docs/customer-workflow-gap-analysis.md` (data-appendix).

## Related Code Files

- Create: `backend/src/seed-customer.ts`, `backend/src/seed/*.ts`,
  `backend/src/seed/data/*.ts`
- Modify: `Makefile` (add `seed:customer` target)
- Read (reference): `backend/src/seed.ts`, `backend/src/reset-seed.ts`,
  `backend/src/db/schema.ts`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts`,
  `shared/src/calculations/tripTotals.ts`

## Success Criteria

- [ ] `backend/src/seed-customer.ts` runs green on a fresh local DB.
- [ ] `--dry-run` prints the full wipe+insert plan without mutating.
- [ ] No `users` row is deleted or password-changed by the script.
- [ ] Existing driver logins resolve to a real `drivers` row afterward.
- [ ] Master data from all 9 DATA-PM sheets is represented (or its gap
      documented inline).
- [ ] ~5-10 sample shipments/trips exist in non-locked states.
- [ ] Script is idempotent (second run = no-op or clean refresh).
- [ ] No raw SQL; all inserts via Drizzle.

## Risk Assessment

- **Risk:** FK violations during wipe because the order is wrong or a new
  table was added. **Mitigation:** the wipe list is derived from today's
  full schema inventory; run with `--dry-run` first; CI/lint the table list
  against `schema.ts` exports.
- **Risk:** The NHÀ MÁY "factory" entity has no clean home → forced fit
  distorts data. **Mitigation:** store as reference text; flag as a gap; do
  not invent a new table in this plan.
- **Risk:** Pricing fuel-surcharge formula is mis-implemented, producing wrong
  cước. **Mitigation:** implement from the formula columns, validate one row
  against the Excel total before seeding all.
- **Risk:** Driver-login relink picks the wrong real driver. **Mitigation:**
  print the mapping to stdout for human review before the staging run.
</file>

