# End-to-End Dispatch Workflow Implementation Report

## Result

The complete business workflow is implemented and its feature-specific chain is
verified locally. Formal plan closure remains blocked by the repository-wide
backend gate described below. The delivered authority chain is:

`Master Data -> Shipment -> Fulfillment -> Dispatch -> Driver milestones -> e-POD -> Review/lock -> Shipment closure -> Long Minh Debit Note`.

The explicit product exclusions remain enforced: no Zalo integration, no GPS
live map or continuous tracking, and no backward-compatibility layer.

## Acceptance Summary

- FCL creates one independently dispatchable fulfillment per container; LCL
  creates one fulfillment/trip per shipment.
- Dispatch requires explicit carrier, truck/plate, and driver selection and uses
  bounded server pagination.
- DRIVER completion is evidence-gated; scoped operational review is first-winner,
  idempotent, and locks the trip through the canonical status authority.
- Shipment closure requires all required fulfillment trips to be locked with
  accepted e-POD.
- Long Minh export reuses billing document, template snapshot, source claiming,
  and ledger authority without inferred VAT.
- Offline commands are scoped by authenticated user and replay the same
  idempotency identity.

## Current Gates

- Shared typecheck and 162/162 tests: green.
- Backend typecheck was green before later concurrent accountant edits; 39/39
  focused workflow tests are green after the final review fixes.
- Frontend typecheck and 487/487 tests: green.
- Migration and seed are green. Lint is green with 0 errors/57 warnings. A prior
  production build was green; the final combined-checkout build is blocked by
  the concurrent accountant test type error described below.
- Persisted public API/UI workflow: 29/29 green from CUS intake through shipment
  closure and Long Minh export.
- Dispatch role/responsive E2E: 46/46 green across six roles and
  1440/1024/768/390/320 px.
- Independent final review is recorded under `qa/`.

## Formal Closure Blocker

The latest full backend run is not green: 1,952/1,966 tests pass and 14 fail in
the combined checkout. The failures are concentrated in concurrently changing
accountant/source-authority fixtures, including the two legacy direct `ADHOC`
document-update cases in `billing-document-lock.test.ts`, source-posting cleanup,
and approved-financial idempotency fixtures. A subsequent backend typecheck and
`make build` are also red on the concurrent `q15-debit-note-governance.test.ts`
draft shape. They
do not fail in the dispatch, e-POD, closure, financial-claim, seed, or Long Minh
focused paths, but `AGENTS.md` requires the repository gate to be green. Phase 6
and the umbrella plan therefore remain `in-progress`; no release/unblock claim
is made.

The supported `pnpm seed` path now installs reference masters, Long Minh customer,
Silver Sea company identity, and the assigned Long Minh template. Its initial
fix-loop run exposed an invalid route conflict target; after replacing it with a
transactionally serialized idempotent resolver, two consecutive seed runs pass.

## Delivery Boundary

No staging/production deployment and no final controller commit were performed.
The local dev/test database was reset for clean-migration verification; previous
local-only data is not recoverable.
