# Historical reporting implementation

## Scope delivered

- Added one strict Vietnam business-date authority for historical reports. A date such as `2026-08-01` resolves to `[start, 2026-08-02 00:00:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)`, represented by the UTC end-exclusive instant `2026-08-01T17:00:00.000Z`.
- Propagated `asOfDate` through customer receivable obligations, billing documents, approved adjustments, allocations, direct ledger rows, AP/AR FIFO aging, overdue-day calculation, and report caches.
- Corrected statement period filters to use the same Vietnam inclusive-start/end-exclusive bounds on both screen and export endpoints. Customer, supplier, and carrier aging now uses the requested historical closing date and excludes future entries.
- Added report evidence metadata to receivable/payable summaries, P&L, and profitability: `asOf`, timezone, definition version, consistency level, and SHA-256 checksum.
- Marked assembled multi-query reports as `BEST_EFFORT`. No repeatable-read claim was added because the services still assemble multiple reads outside a single transaction; this is intentionally truthful rather than overstating snapshot isolation.

## Files changed

- `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/aging.service.ts`
- `backend/src/routes/financial/ledger.routes.ts`
- `backend/src/services/statement.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/profitability.service.ts`
- `backend/src/tests/historical-reporting-as-of.test.ts`
- `backend/src/tests/customer-receivable-as-of.test.ts`
- `backend/src/tests/profitability-pagination.test.ts`
- `qa/2026-08-01_accountant-historical-reporting_backend-focused-test.log`
- `qa/2026-08-01_accountant-historical-reporting_lint.log`
- `qa/2026-08-01_accountant-historical-reporting_backend-typecheck.log`

`backend/src/routes/financial/reports.routes.ts` did not need a code change: it already forwards `asOfDate`; invalid dates now surface as a domain `400` from the shared cutoff authority.

## Verification

- Historical cutoff unit tests: 4 passed.
- Existing statement period tests: 12 passed.
- Customer receivable cutoff and evidence-metadata database tests: 2 passed after fixing the timestamp-expression binding found by the first run.
- Profitability pagination and report-evidence test: 1 passed.
- Focused lint on all owned service, route, and test files: passed.
- `git diff --check` for the owned slice: passed.
- Backend typecheck passed once after the historical implementation. A later repository-wide rerun became red only in concurrently edited secure billing/VAT files (`billingDocument.service.ts`, billing tests, and a shipment export); none of the reported diagnostics point to this owned slice. The controller must rerun the global gate after the concurrent billing work settles and save the final artifact.

## Review notes

- The same cutoff function owns validation, cache keys, query bounds, and aging reference time, preventing timezone drift between layers.
