# Secure billing and VAT implementation

Status: IMPLEMENTED — focused QA green; controller still owns repository-wide gates and integrated release review.

## Delivered

- Debit Note writes now accept immutable source references instead of browser-authored descriptions, amounts, overrides, exclusions, or ad-hoc rows.
- TRIP sources are bound to the active financial posting using `financialPostingId`, `financialPostingVersion`, and a SHA-256 posting checksum. Save re-locks and revalidates those sources in the transaction.
- Server-side draft derivation is authoritative. Legacy internal callers may provide source-shaped lines, but their monetary values are ignored and re-derived.
- VAT uses versioned line snapshots (`VAT-V1`) with explicit treatment and allowed rates. Existing source authority is VAT-inclusive, so gross remains unchanged while net and tax are split with integer-VND half-up rounding; issuance does not increase AR.
- Active trip claims prevent overlapping Debit Notes with a database daterange exclusion. Non-overlapping billing periods remain valid. Cancel/delete releases trip and recoverable-expense claims while retaining release time, reason, actor, and immutable evidence history.
- The transport selection contract is `selectedTripIds`. The builder filters only the authoritative TRIP lines returned by the server; any requested ID missing from that response blocks save.
- Payment Statements remain presentation-only and do not create AP postings.

## Migration

The pre-release schema was consolidated into one internally consistent migration and snapshot:

- `backend/drizzle/0174_cute_thor_girl.sql`
- `backend/drizzle/meta/0174_snapshot.json`
- `backend/drizzle/meta/_journal.json` index 174

The migration was verified by rebuilding the local Silversea database from an empty `public` and `drizzle` schema, applying all migrations, and reseeding demo data.

## Focused verification

- Backend typecheck: green.
- Backend billing/VAT/claim/PDF/recoverable-ledger tests: 47/47 green.
- Frontend typecheck and suite: 487/487 green.
- Shared typecheck and suite: 162/162 green.
- Context manifest check: green.
- Migration from an empty local database plus seed: green.

Evidence is saved under `qa/2026-08-01_accountant-secure-billing-vat_*`.

## Scope boundary

- No production deployment or backward-compatibility migration path was added; this is a pre-release clean schema.
- Repository-wide lint/build/E2E and integrated browser QA remain with the controller because other accountant workflow slices are changing concurrently.
- Unrelated shared navigation, agent, customer-service, and accounting workspace edits were preserved and are not claimed by this slice.
