## 9. Responsive behavior matrix

| Surface | Desktop ≥1024 | Tablet 768–1023 | 390px | 320px |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Page gutter | existing desktop shell | 16–20px | 10px | 10px |
| Header | title/actions one row | actions may wrap to second row | stacked | stacked, full-width actions |
| Overview metrics | single 4-cell strip | 2×2 within one section | 2 columns | compact definition list |
| Filters | inline toolbar | core filters + drawer | date/party + drawer | one control per row in sheet |
| Register | 10-column bounded table | 5-column bounded table | labeled cards | single-column labeled cards |
| Detail | right drawer | wide right drawer | full-screen sheet | full-screen sheet |
| Bulk action | sticky inside register | sticky inside register | fixed safe-area bar | fixed 2-row safe-area bar |
| Money | full digits, tabular | full digits, tabular | wrap at separators; never abbreviate | own line, `overflow-wrap:anywhere` only as last resort |
| Charts | chart + table toggle | simplified ticks | summary + horizontal bars | summary + list/table |

There must be zero page-level horizontal overflow at every viewport. A desktop
register may have an internal scroll region, but primary actions and row status
must remain visible without scrolling horizontally.

Test with long real-world forms of:

- customer/carrier names
- routes and factory names
- bill/container references
- Vietnamese eligibility and error explanations
- 12–15 digit VND amounts

## 10. Interaction and state specification

| State | Required UI |
|---|---|
| Initial loading | Stable skeleton matching final dimensions; `aria-busy=true`; no empty chart axes |
| Background refresh | Keep data; subtle `Đang cập nhật…` metadata, no blocking overlay |
| Empty default | Explain what source event creates data; link to authorized next step |
| Empty filtered | `Không có dữ liệu phù hợp bộ lọc.` + `Đặt lại bộ lọc` |
| Network error | Cause + `Thử lại`; keep last safe data visibly marked as old when available |
| Permission denied | `Bạn không có quyền xem dữ liệu này.`; no leaked counts or names |
| Partial data | Warning strip, unavailable categories listed, totals state `Chưa đối chiếu` |
| Stale source/version | Disable confirmation; `Dữ liệu nguồn đã thay đổi. Tạo lại bản xem trước.` |
| Preview expired | Same as stale; preserve filter/selection where source keys remain valid |
| Submit in progress | Disable duplicate submit; visible spinner and active-verb copy |
| Success | Inline document link + polite toast; clear only successfully consumed selection |
| Mixed failure | Persistent result panel with accepted/rejected groups, not toast-only |
| Export queued | `Đang tạo tệp…`; allow leaving page; notification when ready if durable export exists |
| Export failed | `Không thể tạo tệp. Thử lại` with retained query/snapshot identity |
| Historical cutoff | Persistent `Dữ liệu đến hết dd/MM/yyyy`; never say `vừa xong` |

Transitions: 120–200ms for color/opacity/transform only. Do not use `transition:
all`, hover lift, bounce, chart flourish or animated counters. Honor
`prefers-reduced-motion` by removing non-essential transition/slide motion.

## 11. Accessibility contract

- WCAG 2.1 AA minimum: 4.5:1 text, 3:1 large text and graphical objects.
- Every control is ≥44×44px on touch widths; inputs are ≥16px on phone.
- Use native checkbox semantics and one clickable label/hit target.
- Table sort buttons expose `aria-sort`; active filters and tabs expose selected
  state; expanding rows/drawers use `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`.
- Status is always text + icon/strip, never color alone.
- Icon-only actions require Vietnamese `aria-label` and visible tooltip on
  desktop.
- Focus order follows reading order. Drawers/dialogs trap focus, close on
  Escape when safe, warn about unsaved changes and restore the opener.
- Route changes move focus to `#main-content`/page heading; the existing route
  live region announces the page title.
- Selection, background refresh, partial failure and export completion use
  `aria-live="polite"`; blocking errors use `role="alert"`.
- Charts provide a concise screen-reader summary and keyboard-accessible exact
  values. No information is hover-only.
- Use semantic `<Link>` for navigation and `<button>` for actions. Avoid
  clickable table rows as the only affordance.
- Preserve browser zoom and system back navigation.

## 12. Component reuse and modular frontend structure

### Reuse without duplication

- `PageHeader`, `Breadcrumbs`, `Toolbar`, `FilterPill`, `StatusPill`
- `Drawer`, `Modal`, `DropdownMenu`, `Select`
- `DataTable`, `Pagination`, `EmptyState`, `Skeleton`, `Alert`, `Toast`
- `PeriodFilter`, `PeriodSummaryCards`
- `BillingDocumentsPanel`, refactored `BillingDocumentBuilder`
- `RevenueTrendChart`, with exact-value alternative
- `usePrefersReducedMotion`, query-key conventions, React Query

### Do not install

- Shadcn UI
- Untitled UI runtime/templates
- Tailkit package/components
- a second chart library
- a second form or table framework

### Feature boundary

Recommended new files:

```text
frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx       # lazy route adapter only
frontend/src/features/accounting/
  AccountingWorkspace.tsx                           # view/tab composition
  accounting-workspace.css                          # scoped flat layout
  accounting-query-state.ts                         # URL parse/serialize contract
  AccountingOverview.tsx                            # summary composition
  TransportRegister.tsx                             # filters/table/cards/selection
  TransportRowDetails.tsx                           # shared detail semantics
  TransportPreviewDrawer.tsx                        # immutable preview/submit
  accounting-api.ts                                 # client calls + query keys
```

Keep API response types in the shared schema. Do not redefine DTOs inside
components.

### Existing files to modify

- `shared/src/navigation/pageCatalog.ts`
- `frontend/src/lib/routes.ts`
- `frontend/src/App.tsx`
- `frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx` and its route/nav tests
- current debt/payables/finance/profit pages and scoped CSS
- `frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx/.css`
- `frontend/src/components/finance/ProfitabilityReportPanel.tsx`
- `frontend/src/api/financialClient.ts`, query keys/hooks

### Shared primitive changes

- Do not force selection-specific complexity into the basic `DataTable`.
  `TransportRegister` may use the already-installed TanStack Table directly,
  while reusing project table tokens and `Pagination`.
- Add a generic URL-state adapter around `useTableQueryState` or create one
  small `useUrlTableQueryState` primitive. Do not hand-roll different parsing
  in AR, AP, transport and profitability screens.
- Harden shared `Drawer`/`Modal` focus trapping, inert background, accessible
  title linkage, safe-area padding and opener restoration before using it for
  financial confirmation.

## 13. React and performance rules

- Lazy-load `/accounting` at route level like current pages.
- Start independent overview requests in parallel, but prefer the accepted
  single repeatable-read overview response when cross-widget reconciliation is
  required.
- One query-key factory includes canonical query params, `asOf`, scope and
  returned/selected source version where applicable.
- Keep previous page data during filter/page transitions; mark it as refreshing.
- Debounce search at 300ms; do not debounce checkbox or date apply actions.
- Use server pagination. Default 50 and maximum 100 transport rows.
- Memoize column definitions and expensive row formatting. Use `Set`/`Map` for
  selected and rejected key lookup.
- Never subscribe every row to the whole selection object. Derive row-selected
  booleans by immutable key and isolate checkbox rows/components.
- Do not serialize entire 500+ result sets into the URL or browser storage.
- Dynamically load heavy chart detail only when `/finance` or `/profit` is
  visited; do not include it in the `/accounting` overview bundle.
- Use `Intl.NumberFormat('vi-VN')` and `Intl.DateTimeFormat('vi-VN',
  { timeZone: 'Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh' })` through existing shared format helpers.
- Avoid current-time rendering for historical reports; always use response
  metadata.

## 14. Approved Vietnamese copy

| Purpose | Copy |
|---|---|
| Home title | Kế toán |
| Home description | Đối chiếu vận tải, công nợ và báo cáo tài chính |
| Overview tab | Tổng quan |
| Register tab | Đối chiếu vận tải |
| Customer party | Khách hàng |
| Carrier party | Nhà xe |
| Customer document action | Tạo giấy báo nợ |
| Carrier statement action | Xác nhận bảng kê nhà xe |
| Preview | Xem trước |
| Reconciliation pending | Cần đối chiếu |
| Ready | Đủ điều kiện |
| Not ready | Chưa đủ điều kiện |
| Frozen source | Đã chốt nguồn |
| VAT unknown | Chưa xác định |
| Unavailable source | Chưa có nguồn dữ liệu |
| Historical metadata | Dữ liệu đến hết {date} |
| Stale preview | Dữ liệu nguồn đã thay đổi. Tạo lại bản xem trước. |
| Empty register | Chưa có chuyến đủ điều kiện trong kỳ đã chọn. |
| Filtered empty | Không có dữ liệu phù hợp bộ lọc. |
| Export Excel | Xuất Excel |
| Export PDF | Xuất PDF |
| Retry | Thử lại |
| Reset filters | Đặt lại bộ lọc |

Avoid mixed English labels such as `Closing time`, `Aging`, `Statement`,
`Revenue` or `Margin` in user-facing UI. Technical IDs may be exposed only as
secondary provenance with a Vietnamese label.

## 15. QA and acceptance matrix

### Route and navigation

- `ACCOUNTANT` login and `/` land on `/accounting`.
- Sidebar label and browser title are `Kế toán`.
- `/debt`, `/payables`, `/finance`, `/profit` remain direct drill-downs.
- No compatibility redirect from `/debt` to `/accounting`.
- Direct URLs enforce server and route capabilities for all roles.

### Functional coverage

- overview counts/totals share `asOf` and checksum
- URL reload/copy preserves view, period, filters, sort, page and row detail
- transport page/current-filter selection behaves deterministically
- customer and carrier selections never mix
- stale/expired preview blocks confirmation
- carrier statement does not present itself as a new AP posting
- normal billing cannot edit authoritative amounts, exclude source rows or add
  ad-hoc money
- AR/AP list/detail/export share period and `asOf`
- P&L and profitability totals reconcile to their drill-downs
- unavailable tax/cost categories are explicit, not zero-filled

### Responsive coverage

Test at 1440, 1024, 768, 390 and 320 CSS pixels with 500+ matching transport
rows, 50 visible rows, long Vietnamese copy and full-digit currency.

At every width verify:

- no page-level horizontal overflow
- no content hidden under sticky selection/footer bars
- all actions remain visible and ≥44px on touch widths
- filter sheet/drawer is operable and dismissible
- focus restoration and keyboard-only completion
- mobile and desktop feature parity within role capability
- no clipped money, date, status or party names

### Accessibility coverage

- axe or equivalent automated pass
- keyboard: skip link, tabs, filters, table links, selection, drawer, submit
- screen reader: table headers, selection announcements, errors, export state
- 200% zoom and browser text enlargement
- reduced-motion enabled
- contrast audit for all semantic states

### Visual acceptance

- no decorative shadows, floating layers, glass cards or hover lift in touched
  Accountant surfaces
- no decorative hero illustration
- exact currency uses tabular figures and full digits
- one consistent status-strip treatment
- consistent PageHeader, toolbar, table/card and drawer language across routes
- actual screenshots saved under `qa/` for desktop, tablet, 390px and 320px

## 16. Implementation sequence

1. Route/catalog/home/nav contract and tests.
2. Shared URL-state and overlay accessibility hardening.
3. `/accounting` overview composition against the accepted overview response.
4. Transport register, selection and preview drawer.
5. Billing builder server-owned-money refactor.
6. `/debt` and `/payables` bounded list/detail deltas.
7. `/finance` and `/profit` presentation/reconciliation deltas.
8. Responsive, accessibility, role and visual QA loop.
9. Update canonical `docs/design-guidelines.md` and all required QA artifacts.

## 17. Unresolved implementation concerns

1. Shadcn MCP is unavailable; do not block implementation or install Shadcn.
   Re-verify availability immediately before UI coding if the controller's
   environment differs.
2. `docs/design-guidelines.md` is missing and must be created/updated by the
   controller because this report-only subtask cannot write outside its report.
3. The exact capability names for prepare/approve/export/payment actions must
   come from the accepted role/action matrix. Never infer them from role labels.
4. Bundled multi-report export remains deferred. Every implemented export is
