# Accountant workspace UI implementation re-review

**Reviewed:** 2026-08-01
**Scope:** static re-review of the updated Accountant workspace, its customer-draft handoff, and `transport-preview-integration-assessment.md`
**Verdict:** **DONE_WITH_CONCERNS — the explicit current-page customer draft flow is acceptable for the initial slice; remaining gaps are bounded follow-ups or intentionally deferred capabilities**

## Executive result

The controller fixes resolve most safety and responsive issues from the first review:

- `/accounting` remains the canonical Accountant home; `/debt` remains a separate `Công nợ phải thu` drill-down.
- `view`, `from`, `to`, applied search, page, ownership and readiness are URL-owned and preserved through navigation.
- Period defaults use `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh`; displayed dates are Vietnamese day/month/year.
- Overdue money now comes from the server response instead of browser bucket arithmetic.
- The overview visibly identifies its cutoff and source checksums.
- Search has a real label, name, `type="search"`, autocomplete policy and example placeholder.
- Register error/empty states provide retry/reset actions; loading exposes `aria-busy` and a polite status.
- Main controls are 44px high; monetary table columns are right-aligned with tabular figures.
- At widths below 1024px the wide table is removed in favor of bounded cards, eliminating the previous tablet horizontal-overflow failure.
- Phone/tablet cards now include selection, service date, route, container, exact amounts and readiness status.
- Only `READY` rows can be selected. Selection is current-page, one customer at a time, and the action copy correctly says `Tạo bản nháp giấy báo nợ` rather than implying financial confirmation.
- Filter-wide select-all, immutable preview tokens, mixed-customer orchestration and carrier confirmation are correctly deferred by `transport-preview-integration-assessment.md`; the UI does not claim those capabilities.

The explicit current-page customer flow is now architecturally and functionally acceptable for the initial slice: select visible `READY` trips for one customer, generate the canonical server draft, retain selected `TRIP` lines, save immutable server-returned source references, and leave issue/approval to governance.

## Primary current-page customer flow assessment — acceptable

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:348-365` enables selection only for `READY` rows and keeps one customer group at a time.
- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:367-372` passes `selectedTripIds` plus the selected completion-date span to the customer billing route.
- `frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx:55-63` consumes the same `selectedTripIds`, `from` and `to` URL contract.
- `frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx:141-168` generates the customer draft from server authority, retains only selected `TRIP` lines and reports selected trips that are no longer eligible.
- `frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx:231-259` saves debit notes using only server-returned `sourceRefs`, financial posting versions and checksums.
- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:444-450` accurately labels the next action `Tạo bản nháp giấy báo nợ`; it does not call save or issue “financial confirmation.”

This matches the narrow flow approved in `transport-preview-integration-assessment.md`. Trip IDs are acceptable selection inputs here because generation and save reload and revalidate the authoritative posting/e-POD/source evidence. The register does not attempt to manufacture posting checksums or money.

No UI blocker remains for this initial slice. One verification improvement remains: `AccountingWorkspacePage.test.tsx:108-111` proves the outgoing URL, but a builder-level integration test should also prove that a selected subset filters the authoritative draft and that a missing selected trip blocks save. Parsing at the route boundary and passing typed props would be cleaner than reading `window.location.search` inside the editor, but the current matching contract works.

## Accepted deferrals

The following are **not blockers for the initial explicit customer freight flow**, provided the product labels remain narrow:

- filter-wide selection across unloaded pages;
- mixed-customer batch document orchestration;
- immutable preview token/checksum binding;
- automatic ancillary-cost attachment without an authoritative trip reference;
- carrier/vendor confirmation and `Xác nhận bảng kê nhà xe`;
- a dedicated transport-preview endpoint.

The assessment correctly requires those capabilities to wait for a thin server orchestration adapter. The current UI offers only a customer debit-note draft and does not mislabel saving as approval.

## Remaining high-priority findings

### 1. Selection does not clear on every filter/period mutation

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:352` clears selection only when `page` or the live search input changes.
- Changes to `from`, `to`, `ownership` or `readiness` do not explicitly invalidate the selected set.

Because `selectedRows` is intersected with the current page, many changes appear to clear selection incidentally, but an ID surviving a filter/date change remains selected without confirmation. Include the canonical filter fingerprint or every applied filter in selection invalidation. For this current-page slice, clearing with a polite announcement is sufficient; the filter-wide confirmation model remains deferred.

### 2. Checkbox hit areas remain smaller than 44px

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.css:88-90` renders the native checkbox at 18px and does not give `.accounting-row-check` a 44px minimum hit area.
- The surrounding label is clickable, but its own box can remain roughly one text line high; table-cell/card padding outside the label is not part of the hit target.

Give the label at least `min-height: 44px`, align it centrally where appropriate, and keep the disabled reason visible in the row/card. The 44px fix for tabs, dates, search, selects, pagination and selection-bar actions is otherwise resolved.

### 3. Phone inputs do not guarantee a 16px text size

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.css:24,63` use `font: inherit` for date/search inputs.
- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.css:82` fixes selects at 13px.

At phone widths, set date/search/select controls to at least 16px to prevent mobile browser zoom. Height alone does not satisfy this requirement.

### 4. Overview is safer but still not the accepted repeatable-read work queue

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:105-138` still makes three independent overview requests rather than consuming one repeatable-read overview projection.
- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:192-227` still shows separate `Phải thu / Quá hạn / Phải trả / Lợi nhuận kỳ` cards, not the accepted `Cần đối chiếu / Chờ phát hành / Sắp đến hạn / Quá hạn` strip.
- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:232-280` still has six large route tiles and no bounded `Việc cần xử lý` queue, conditional reconciliation panel or explicit `/profit` row.
- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:228-230` displays three independent checksums. This is truthful provenance, but it is not proof of a cross-widget repeatable-read snapshot.

The authority violation is resolved—overdue is server-provided—but the exact overview composition remains a planned follow-up. Do not describe the three-source page as one reconciled snapshot until the combined endpoint exists.

### 5. Loading and partial-error presentation is improved but incomplete

- Register retry/reset and `aria-busy` are resolved.
- KPI values now say `Không khả dụng`, but their metadata can still show zero counts from fallbacks (`AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:193-225`), producing combinations such as unavailable value plus `0 khách hàng`.
- Overview partial failure has no per-source retry, and loading uses text rather than stable-dimension skeletons.

Suppress unavailable metadata, list the failed source, and add focused retry actions. Skeletons remain desirable to avoid content shift but do not block the explicit customer draft slice.

## Remaining medium-priority findings

### 6. Tablet behavior is usable but diverges from the five-column contract

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.css:99-111` switches 768–1023px directly to cards rather than the specified five-column tablet table.

This resolves horizontal overflow and remains usable, so it is no longer a blocker. If dense tablet accounting is important, implement the compact table later; otherwise document cards as the accepted tablet variant.

### 7. Card content is richer, but eligibility explanation and row provenance remain shallow

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx:491-502` shows readiness text, date, route, container and exact values.
- It does not show the underlying eligibility explanation/evidence, posting version/short ID, bill/reference details or a URL-owned row-detail drawer.

The visible status is enough to gate the initial selection. A row-detail/provenance surface remains necessary before claiming full compliance with the workbench specification.

### 8. The page remains monolithic

- `frontend/src/pages/AccountingWorkspacePage.tsx` now exceeds 550 lines and owns URL parsing, queries, overview, selection, register, table rows, mobile cards, KPIs and workflow links.
- Receivable/payable/profitability DTOs remain locally defined.

Move query-state parsing, API/query keys, overview and transport register into the planned `features/accounting` boundary. This is a maintainability concern, not a reason to block the narrow current-page customer flow.

### 9. The builder still exposes misleading normal-flow controls

- `frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx:191-219` retains add/remove/exclusion behavior.
- `frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx:231-259` correctly saves debit notes through server-owned `sourceRefs`, so browser-authored money is not persisted.

For a selected-source debit-note flow, hide `Thêm dòng trình bày`, amount-altering controls and source exclusion affordances, or make them presentation-only with unambiguous copy. The strict save contract protects money, but the current controls can mislead the Accountant about what will be saved.

## Responsive and accessibility matrix

| Area | Re-review result | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Desktop ≥1024 | Pass with follow-up | Bounded 25-row table, sticky header, right-aligned money; no full 500+ render |
| Tablet 768–1023 | Usable divergence | Bounded cards replace wide table; no page-level horizontal overflow, but not the specified five-column table |
| Phone 390 | Partial pass | Two-column value grid, full exact amounts, selection bar actions wrap; checkbox/input sizing follow-ups remain |
| Phone 320 | Partial pass | Dates and key values stack; Vietnamese content can wrap; input font and checkbox hit-area follow-ups remain |
| 500+ result safety | Pass for initial slice | Server limit 25 + bounded scroll; no filter-wide claim or client array of all results |
| URL persistence | Pass for implemented filters | View, period, applied search, page, ownership and readiness are reload-safe |
| Selection semantics | Partial | READY + same customer + current page is correct; filter invalidation incomplete |
| Async accessibility | Partial pass | Register busy/live/error retry resolved; selection live region exists; overview retries/skeletons incomplete |
| Navigation semantics | Pass | Tabs are now real links with `aria-current`, appropriate for URL navigation |
| Exact Vietnamese money/dates | Pass | Full VND digits and Vietnam business dates are visible |

## Resolved findings from first review

1. Destructive `setSearchParams({ view })` replacement — resolved with merged URL state and link navigation.
2. Browser-derived overdue aging amount — resolved through `overdueAmount` response authority.
3. Browser-local timezone cutoff — resolved with `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh` date construction.
4. Raw ISO period display — resolved to `dd/MM/yyyy`.
5. 38–42px main controls — resolved to 44px, except checkbox label hit areas.
6. Unlabeled table action header — resolved as `Thao tác`.
7. Left-aligned money — resolved.
8. Search field metadata/example — resolved.
9. Transport retry/empty reset/`aria-busy` — resolved.
10. Tablet horizontal desktop table — resolved by bounded card composition.
11. Thin mobile transport cards — substantially resolved with date, route, container, exact amounts and AP value for external transport.
12. No selection path — resolved for explicit current-page, same-customer READY trips, including the matching builder handoff.

## Required closeout checks

1. Add a subset-selection integration test through the builder, including missing/stale selected-trip recovery.
2. Clear selection on all applied period/filter mutations and announce the reset.
3. Verify actual 1024/768/390/320 rendering, long Vietnamese names/routes and 12–15 digit amounts in a browser.
4. Verify checkbox and input sizing, keyboard traversal, focus visibility and live announcements.
5. Preserve the accepted deferral labels: no filter-wide, carrier-confirmation or financial-confirmation claim.

## Review limitation

This is a static code and contract re-review. It does not claim browser screenshots, measured contrast, screen-reader output or completed end-to-end billing issuance. The current-page customer draft flow is acceptable by code inspection; full closed-loop proof still requires the focused builder integration test and browser QA listed above.

Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS
Summary: URL state, server-owned overdue totals, Vietnam dates, provenance, bounded responsive cards, retry states, 44px main controls and narrow READY/same-customer selection are materially improved. The matching `selectedTripIds` builder flow securely filters server-generated lines and is acceptable for the initial customer draft slice.
Concerns/Blockers: No blocker for the initial explicit customer flow. Remaining concerns are filter-driven selection invalidation, checkbox/input accessibility, browser QA, overview composition and a focused builder integration test; filter-wide selection and carrier confirmation remain intentionally deferred.
</file>

