# New workflow as the only runtime

## Outcome

Remove the customer-service-to-finance rollout compatibility layer. A normal
backend start always executes the canonical posting, milestone, treasury,
profitability, customer-event, and Accountant flow without an environment flag.

## Acceptance criteria

- Completing an in-transit trip always creates one ACTIVE financial posting and
  records the corresponding ledger authority.
- Canceling a completed trip requires and retires its active posting.
- Workflow routes are governed by authentication, role, and Casbin only; no
  `503` rollout response remains.
- Capabilities are derived only from role/Casbin, and the browser no longer
  receives or branches on `workflowRolloutMode`.
- Executive finance, profitability, treasury, customer milestones, and shipment
  coordination render when their capability allows them.
- Default local development and E2E pass without `WORKFLOW_ROLLOUT_MODE`.

## Scope

### Remove

- `WORKFLOW_ROLLOUT_MODE` configuration and `.env.example` documentation.
- `workflow-rollout` middleware and all route guards using it.
- OFF/SHADOW branches in posting, milestone, Debit Note, capability, and
  dashboard services.
- `workflowRolloutMode` from auth responses and frontend user state.
- Browser rollout checks and OFF/SHADOW-only regression cases.

### Preserve

- Existing Casbin and role permissions.
- Financial-posting version/checksum, source-claim, idempotency, and governance
  invariants.
- Unrelated `SHIPMENT_FIRST_CREATE` behavior and user-owned worktree changes.

### Out of scope

- Deployment, staging mutation, data backfill for old local rows, and unrelated
  Accountant or dispatch features.

## Phases

1. Remove backend rollout configuration, middleware, and conditional behavior.
2. Remove the rollout field and conditionals from frontend auth/navigation/pages.
3. Replace compatibility tests/docs with single-flow contracts.
4. Run focused tests, then full affected lint/typecheck/test/build/E2E gates,
   independent review, plan sync, and handoff.

## QA matrix

- Backend focused: capabilities, trip completion/cancellation, driver
  fulfillment, customer events, Debit Note confirmation, treasury/report routes.
- Frontend focused: auth route redirects, Layout navigation, Dashboard, Profit,
  shipment detail, portal shipment detail.
- Repository gates: shared/backend/frontend typechecks and tests, root lint,
  production build, full E2E, `pnpm context:check`, and `git diff --check`.

## Risks

- Old local COMPLETED trips without postings remain historical data; this task
  prevents new missing postings but does not invent a backfill.
- Removing the browser field is an intentional API contract break authorized for
  this new product.

## Completion evidence

- [x] Backend rollout configuration, middleware, and compatibility branches removed.
- [x] Auth and frontend contracts use capabilities only.
- [x] Trip completion/cancellation and customer milestones use the canonical posting path.
- [x] Auth contract, touched backend regressions, frontend, shared, lint, typecheck, and build are green.
- [x] Default full E2E is green without the rollout environment variable: 293 pass, 0 fail.
- [x] Independent review and QA artifacts saved under `qa/`.
- [x] Review findings closed: cancellation governance records the exact
  cancellation posting, portal event failures degrade locally, and executive
  treasury aggregation is capability-scoped and batched.
- [x] Post-review backend/frontend suites, typechecks, lint, build, and focused
  portal/persisted-chain E2E are green.
- [x] Shared financial writes invalidate both base and executive dashboard cache
  variants, covered by a Redis integration regression.
</file>

