The plan's "No backward-compatibility layer / forward-only / reset DB" strategy (plan.md:110-111, 217-219) is internally consistent only if Phases 1, 2, 3 land together. As written, each phase can ship independently (per the Dependencies section, lines 169-178), but Findings 2, 3, 4, 5 each show a service that hard-breaks at Phase 1 and isn't repaired until Phase 2 or 3. Either collapse Phases 1-3 into a single atomic PR, or explicitly enumerate the inter-phase breakage in the Risk section.
