# Phase 1 — Decision Gates Review & Authority Map

**Status:** IMPLEMENTATION DEFAULTS AUTHORIZED — customer confirmation remains
open before production activation.
**Cook mode:** the user explicitly requested implementation of the complete
workflow and directed all unresolved customer questions into the accompanying
Vietnamese question file. The additive, reversible defaults below therefore
govern implementation. They are not represented as customer/legal approval;
production activation remains gated by the recorded answers.

**Date:** 2026-07-31
**Author:** `/ck:cook` (implementation authorization received; no customer
answers received).

---

## Frozen Authority Map (decision-independent; Phase 1 step #1)

This map is true regardless of how the four gates close. It is the foundation
every downstream phase depends on.

| Domain | Single authority | Code anchor | What everyone else must do |
|---|---|---|---|
| Booking / dossier / dispatch inputs | `shipments` row family | `backend/src/db/schema.ts:2305`, `shipment.service.ts:433/557/1523` | Read-only; never duplicate into a parallel booking table |
| Debt instrument (AR posting) | `billing_documents` (`type=DEBIT_NOTE`) | `backend/src/db/schema.ts:825`, `billing-document-governance.service.ts:295/382` | Receivable snapshots read this; no second posting path |
| Customer AR view | `customer-receivable-authority.service.ts` snapshot | `:133` over TRIP/BILLING_DOCUMENT/SERVICE_FEE/DEBT_OFFSET | Suppress duplicate issued rows; never raw-ledger dump |
| Collection (cash application) | `payment_receipts` + `payment_allocations` | `backend/src/db/schema.ts:2584/2633`, `payment-allocation.service.ts:1060` | Refunds, offsets, unapplied cash all flow here |
| Payable (AP) | existing AP aging / supplier authority | `ap-aging.service.ts:78`, `debtOffset.service.ts:180` | Profitability consumes; does not recompute |
| Profitability / P&L | existing P&L + distribution services | `pnl.service.ts:29`, `profit-distribution.service.ts:107` | Dashboard reads; one canonical posting/version (see D4) |
| Treasury (cash/bank book balance) | **GAP — to be closed by D2** | (none today; company-info bank fields are settings, not balances) | Dashboard cannot infer from AR/AP; KPI stays partial until D2 lands |
| Legal/tax invoice | **GAP — to be closed by D1** | slot exists: `billing_documents.officialIdentitySnapshot` jsonb `:862` | Must not become a second AR posting |

**Confirmed code facts (scouted 2026-07-31):**

- `roleEnum` already includes `CLERK` — no new role needed for CUS.
  (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:26`)
- `billing_documents.officialIdentitySnapshot` (jsonb) already exists and is
  described as "Immutable legal/bank/signature identity used by issued-document
  renders." This is the natural reference-only legal-invoice slot.
- `billing_documents.authorityState` enum is `CURRENT | STALE | ADJUSTMENT_REQUIRED`
  — governable, no schema change needed for the reference-only model.
- `periodLocks` (Q21) already provides reusable per-customer/global lock
  authority — the treasury cutover watermark can lean on the same primitive
  rather than inventing a new lock table.

---

## Decision Gates — Proposed Defaults

Each gate lists the recommended default, why it matches current architecture,
the blast radius if wrong, and a one-line rollback. A reviewer only needs to
object to a default; silence from finance/legal on a *Blocking* gate still
blocks product code (per the validation report).

### D1 — Legal invoice authority

| | |
|---|---|
| **Proposed default** | **Reference-only.** Legal/tax invoice is an additive snapshot + adapter metadata on `billing_documents` (reusing the existing `officialIdentitySnapshot` jsonb slot plus an optional new nullable `legalInvoiceRef` column). The Debit Note remains the sole AR posting. |
| **Matches** | Current architecture; red-team RT-03/RT-04 were resolved *assuming* this model; `officialIdentitySnapshot` already exists for exactly this purpose. |
| **If wrong (one-posting replacement chosen later)** | Migration converts the reference column into the authoritative identity; additive, reversible. No AR data is destroyed because Debit Note history is preserved. |
| **Rollback** | Drop the nullable `legalInvoiceRef` column; revert adapter writes. Debit Note AR is untouched. |
| **Phase 3 impact if undecided** | Provider-specific invoice code is blocked. Phases 2/4/5 unaffected. |

### D2 — Treasury foundation & cutover

| | |
|---|---|
| **Proposed default** | **Minimal foundation only.** New additive tables for `treasury_accounts`, `treasury_movements` (source-linked to `payment_receipts`/AP payments), and book-balance view; per-account opening-balance watermark; versioned payment snapshot contract; physical-transaction-identity uniqueness; governance/RBAC split into read/operate/admin; rollback compatibility floor gating create/check/approve/refund/reversal as one unit. **Deferred** (separate plan): statement import/matching, internal transfers, close/reopen, manual adjustment, full treasury workspace. |
| **Matches** | RT-05/RT-06/RT-07/RT-11 disposition; `periodLocks` primitive already exists for the cutover watermark; keeps KPIs honest rather than inferring from AR/AP. |
| **If wrong (full treasury needed sooner)** | Additive tables remain valid; the deferred items become a follow-on plan. No rewrite. |
| **Rollback** | Pre-cutover compatibility floor guarantees old builds cannot post ledger money without linked treasury movement. Revert disables treasury-aware writes; core AR/AP intact. |
| **Phase 4/5 impact if undecided** | Phase 4 payment writes blocked; Phase 5 cash/bank KPIs render as partial/unavailable. |

### D3 — Customer communication authority

| | |
|---|---|
| **Proposed default** | **Four-distinct-authority matrix, v1 = audit + notify + ack (no 2-way chat).** (1) operational milestone, (2) delivery attempt, (3) immutable customer-visible event content, (4) acknowledgement — each with its own owner and a portal-safe allowlisted DTO. |
| **Matches** | RT-09/RT-10 disposition; plan's explicit out-of-scope ("not a general chat inbox"); customer portal is already read/ack/dispute only (`routes/portal/index.ts:112/172/258/287`). |
| **If wrong (2-way chat needed)** | v1 audit-log records are a strict subset; a chat product can layer on top without invalidating them. |
| **Rollback** | Disable new milestone/delivery/ack writes; existing shipment status history remains the source of truth. |
| **Phase 2 impact if undecided** | Customer-coordination persistence blocked; shipment dossier work still proceeds. |

### D4 — Attribution & canonical financial posting/version

| | |
|---|---|
| **Proposed default** | **Authenticated accepted-dispatcher event + versioned salesperson assignment (effective dates/reassignment) + ONE canonical financial posting/version ID** shared by governed trip corrections, P&L rows, and profitability attribution. Historical gaps stay explicit; never guessed. |
| **Matches** | RT-13/RT-15 disposition; `trip-status-machine` transaction already exists as the capture point; `adjustment-governance` already handles supersession. |
| **If wrong (different ownership model)** | Versioned assignment table is additive; canonical ID is a new nullable column until backfilled. Both reversible. |
| **Rollback** | Disable attribution writes; historical gaps remain explicitly unattributed. Never infer ownership from `createdBy`. |
| **Phase 5 impact if undecided** | Profitability snapshot blocked; Phases 2/3/4 unaffected. |

### D5 — Role/action matrix (per-surface, resolved as each surface lands)

Already locked for the surfaces we touch first:

- **CUS = `CLERK`** with a new narrow, live row-scoped recoverable-cost
  read/request capability (same assignment/business-unit/customer scope as
  shipments). No coarse `financial` access, no Debit Note approval, no AR/AP,
  no treasury, no executive reporting. (RT-01, RT-08.)
- **Executive reporting** stays `ADMIN`/`MANAGER`. No `Role.CEO`.
  (`schema.ts:26` confirms no CEO role exists.)

Still to resolve before the owning phase exposes UI/API:

- treasury read/operate/admin split (resolved *within* D2 above);
- exact executive-reporting endpoint allowlist (Phase 5).

---

## What can proceed NOW (decision-independent, low-risk)

These Phase 1 items do not depend on any gate and are safe under `--auto`:

1. ✅ This authority map (done — you are reading it).
2. ✅ Confirm `appSettings` vs code-constant split for runtime knobs
   (settings: due-date policy, payment-term defaults; constants: enum values,
   authority-state transitions).
3. ✅ Identify and name the focused regression test suites that must stay green
   (already listed in Phase 1 "Tests Before").

## Production activation gates still open

- Legal invoice provider activation requires the customer's D1 answer and
  finance/legal acceptance.
- Treasury account opening balances and live posting cutover require D2 answers,
  reconciliation of the opening watermark, and finance sign-off.
- Customer-visible communication publication requires D3 answers and an
  approved portal-safe content policy.
- Attribution reporting publication requires D4 answers and explicit treatment
  of historical gaps.

Implementation may proceed behind these gates. No unanswered item is treated as
customer acceptance, and no historical ownership is guessed.
</file>

