## Overview

Lock the workflow contracts before feature code starts. This phase defines which existing entities remain authoritative, which additions are allowed, which decision gates must close first, and how to sequence migrations so shipment, debit-note, receivable, payable, and profitability data cannot drift apart.

## Key Insights

- Shipment already has the right backbone for CUS operations: draft creation, dossier edits, documents, declarations, containers, status history, dispatch, and post-dispatch change requests already exist (`backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:192`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:290`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:419`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:489`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:574`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:610`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:433`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:557`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:1707`).
- Debit notes already live inside `billing_documents`; issue and adjustment requests already go through governance, and non-draft documents already lock (`backend/src/services/billing-document-governance.service.ts:236`, `backend/src/services/billing-document-governance.service.ts:295`, `backend/src/services/billing-document-governance.service.ts:382`, `backend/src/services/debit-note-lifecycle.service.ts:176`, `backend/src/services/debit-note-lifecycle.service.ts:184`).
- Customer AR is not a raw ledger dump. It is a curated authority snapshot over `TRIP`, `BILLING_DOCUMENT`, `SERVICE_FEE`, and `DEBT_OFFSET`, with duplicate issued rows suppressed (`backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:7`, `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:92`, `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:382`).
- Payment receipts, allocations, refunds, and governance already exist and must stay the only collection write path (`backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:781`, `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:851`, `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:917`, `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:981`, `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:1060`).
- Credit control, reminder cadence, AP aging, debt offsets, and profit distribution are already implemented and should be consumed, not recreated (`backend/src/services/credit-limit.service.ts:279`, `backend/src/services/receivable-reminder.service.ts:219`, `backend/src/services/ap-aging.service.ts:78`, `backend/src/services/debtOffset.service.ts:180`, `backend/src/services/profit-distribution.service.ts:107`).
- Treasury is the one major authority gap. Current dashboard services return operational and receivable/profit data, company bank fields are only settings, and ledger entity types stop at customer/vendor/driver/forwarder/carrier (`backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts:17`, `backend/src/services/dashboard-widgets.service.ts:44`, `backend/src/services/company-info.service.ts:21`, `backend/src/services/ledger.service.ts:40`).

## Requirements

- Preserve a single authoritative lifecycle for shipment, debit note, receivable, payable, payment, and profit.
- Keep all schema changes additive. No destructive rename/drop/backfill without a tested rollback path.
- Treat official invoice lifecycle as unresolved until this phase defines the adapter boundary around current `billing_documents`.
- Treat treasury KPI source as unresolved until this phase names an explicit company-cash authority.
- Keep dispatch-readiness advisory, because current shipment tests prove dispatch can proceed with warnings while drafts remain partial (`backend/src/tests/m102-dispatch-readiness.test.ts:131`).
- Keep customer communication v1 to auditable shipment interaction/update records and acknowledgements only.
- Snapshot direct shipment, trip, container, customer, route, operator, and sales attribution; leave shared overhead visible and unallocated.
- Keep existing role model. Executive reporting stays under `ADMIN` / `MANAGER` reach rather than a new `CEO` role.
- Preserve `vi-VN` money formatting and do not introduce compact number abbreviations in planned KPI surfaces.
- Lock the customer-communication authority matrix before Phase 2: operational milestone, delivery attempt, customer-visible immutable event, and acknowledgement are distinct facts with explicit owners and safe DTOs.
- Lock direct attribution before Phase 5: accepted dispatcher identity and salesperson assignment require versioned owning workflows; generic trip/shipment versions and `createdBy` are not valid substitutes.
- Introduce or name one canonical financial posting/version ID shared by governed trip corrections, P&L rows, and profitability attribution.
- Treat the minimal treasury foundation as a versioned contract/cutover, not
  only new tables: pending governance actions, old-client payloads, idempotency
  replays, physical transaction identity, per-account cutover watermark, and
  rollback compatibility must all have explicit contracts.

## Blocking Decision Gates

1. **D1 invoice authority:** finance/legal accepts either reference-only legal invoice (current Debit Note remains the sole AR posting) or a redesigned one-posting replacement/alias lifecycle. Provider-specific Phase 3 work cannot start while this is undecided.
2. **D2 treasury foundation and cutover:** approve account/source-linked
   movement models, governance and role subjects, physical payment identity,
   per-account opening-balance watermark, payment contract version,
   pending-action disposition, and post-cutover compatibility floor. Defer
   statement reconciliation, internal transfers, close/reopen, manual
   adjustments, and the full treasury workspace to a separate approved plan.
3. **D3 customer communication:** approve reuse/ownership across `shipmentMilestones`, `customerEmailLogs`, customer-visible event content, delivery state, and acknowledgement.
4. **D4 profitability attribution:** approve accepted-dispatcher and salesperson ownership plus a canonical financial posting/version ID.
5. **D5 role/action matrix:** CUS maps to existing `CLERK`, with a new narrowly
   scoped recoverable-cost read/request capability limited by the same
   assignment/business-unit/customer scope as shipments. It does not grant
   coarse `financial` access, Debit Note approval, AR/AP, treasury, or executive
   reporting. Resolve the remaining executive-reporting and treasury actions
   before their owning phase exposes UI or API.

## Architecture / Data Flow

1. Booking enters through shipment create and quick-create, producing a draft shipment plus idempotent audit context (`backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:192`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:235`).
2. Customer service enriches the shipment dossier, documents, declarations, and containers on the same shipment row family (`backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:290`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:419`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:489`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:574`).
3. Dispatch creates or replays a linked trip from the shipment, with side effects running once (`backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:378`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:1523`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:1502`).
4. Trip revenue plus recoverable costs feed billing-document draft generation inside the current debit-note assembly path (`backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts:950`, `backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts:978`).
5. Governance moves billing documents through issue/adjust states and keeps non-draft debt instruments immutable (`backend/src/services/billing-document-governance.service.ts:295`, `backend/src/services/billing-document-governance.service.ts:382`, `backend/src/services/debit-note-lifecycle.service.ts:176`).
6. Customer receivable authority groups the resulting debt by trip, service fee, billing document, and debt offset rather than exposing duplicate raw rows (`backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:133`, `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:144`).
7. Payment receipts and allocations reduce outstanding balances, keep unapplied cash explicit, and govern refunds on the same authority (`backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:1060`, `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:1101`).
8. Reporting and dashboards should read those existing authorities. Treasury metrics must wait until a company-balance source exists beyond partner-entity ledger rows (`backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts:17`, `backend/src/services/company-info.service.ts:21`, `backend/src/services/ledger.service.ts:40`).

