4. Close D3-D5: customer communication ownership, operational/profitability attribution, financial posting version, and exact role/action matrix.
5. Define additive schema changes only after the applicable gate is accepted.
6. Write failing tests for any new contract edges before changing services.
7. Implement the smallest additive guards needed to keep the chosen contract true.
8. Re-run the focused finance and shipment suites, then the repo QA gates.
9. Hand downstream implementers an approved contract checklist, not a vague narrative.

