# Phase 3: Recoverable costs Debit Note and invoice handoff

## Context Links

- [Plan index](./plan.md)
- [Current code authority](./research/codebase-domain-map.md)
- [Accounting and dependency research](./research/accounting-and-plan-dependencies.md)
- [Role and UI research](./research/role-ux-and-ui-patterns.md)
- [`docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md`](../../docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md) — accepted Q12-Q23 evidence, role, lock, period, and concurrency rules
- [`docs/regression-testing/03-module-03-cus.md`](../../docs/regression-testing/03-module-03-cus.md) — Debit Note lifecycle and customer response cases
- [`docs/regression-testing/04-module-04-disbursement-recovery.md`](../../docs/regression-testing/04-module-04-disbursement-recovery.md) — recoverable-cost and no-invoice evidence cases
- [`plans/260727-1230-approved-business-rules/plan.md`](../260727-1230-approved-business-rules/plan.md) — accepted authority baseline
- [`plans/260729-1248-customer-portal-overhaul/plan.md`](../260729-1248-customer-portal-overhaul/plan.md) — existing portal interaction boundary

## Overview

Deliver one governed handoff from verified recoverable cost to customer receivable:

`approved expense -> Debit Note draft -> independent accounting approval -> issue -> customer confirm/dispute -> legal-invoice handoff/reference -> AR authority`

This phase composes existing expense evidence, `billingDocuments`, governance, ledger, and portal authorities. It does not introduce a second expense-verification state machine, billing lifecycle, ledger, or receivable model.

### Scope boundary

In scope:

- named CUS verification as a queue/read-model and action orchestration over existing expense evidence and governance;
- selection of approved recoverable costs into Debit Note drafts;
- independent accountant/checker/approver issue flow;
- customer confirmation/dispute using the current portal boundary;
- a decision gate and adapter boundary for a legal/tax invoice;
- explicit AR-source handoff and chi hộ linkage without double billing;
- desktop, tablet, and mobile task surfaces for the affected roles.

Out of scope:

- choosing a tax authority/provider or inventing legal invoice numbering without a recorded business decision;
- cash/bank balances and reconciliation, which belong to Phase 4;
- AP payment execution, profitability, CEO dashboards, and a new app shell;
- two-way customer messaging beyond the existing confirm/dispute and notification contract.

## Key Insights

1. `requestTripExpenseDecision` and `applyTripExpenseGovernanceAction` already own evidence-backed expense decisions, optimistic version checks, first-winner semantics, and source propagation. “CUS kiểm tra” is a task label and UI orchestration, not a new persisted approval status.
2. `generateDraft`, `saveDocument`, `requestBillingDocumentIssue`, `applyBillingDocumentGovernanceAction`, and `transitionDebitNoteStatus` already own the Debit Note authority path. Extend these contracts; do not fork them.
3. `buildExpenseDraftLineTx`, `propagateExpenseApproval`, source-version tokens, source drift checks, source locks, and period locks are the durable link between expense evidence and issued documents.
4. The current customer portal already exposes row-scoped `confirm` and `dispute` actions. Preserve legal-entity scoping and never accept a customer/document ID outside the authenticated scope.
5. No separate legal/tax invoice authority was found. A Debit Note is not silently re-labeled as a tax invoice. Implementation must pass Decision Gate D3-INV before any provider-specific schema or code is created.
6. Chi hộ is not one money bucket. Cash disbursement, supplier payable, recoverable customer receivable, service-fee revenue, and settlement are separate authorities connected by immutable source references.
7. The existing accounting obligation is created from the issued Debit Note; the later confirmed legal-invoice handoff/reference completes the requested workflow presentation but enriches that same obligation and never creates a second AR posting.

## Requirements

### Functional

- Show CUS users a recoverable-cost queue sourced from current `tripExpenses`/expense evidence and governance state, with explicit reasons an item is blocked, returnable, approved, already billed, or adjustment-only.
- Require invoice data where `assertInvoiceRequiredForExpense` says it is mandatory; for allowed no-invoice categories, require the accepted substitute evidence and Q12-Q14 thresholds.
- Preserve maker/checker/approver separation. The maker cannot check or approve their own cost decision or Debit Note issue.
- Use `expectedExpenseVersion`, billing-document version, idempotency key, and first-approve-wins semantics on every material write.
- Include only `APPROVED` recoverable sources in a Debit Note draft. `PENDING`, returned, rejected, canceled, deleted, wrong-customer, or incomplete-evidence sources are ineligible.
- Prevent one recoverable source from contributing value to more than one non-canceled Debit Note, including concurrent draft/save/issue attempts and retries.
- Snapshot source version, evidence reference, customer/legal-entity scope, period, due dates, and line calculation when the document is issued.
- Lock issued/confirmed sources. Later corrections use `requestBillingDocumentAdjustment`, reversal, or a linked open-period adjustment; never mutate the issued record in place.
- Preserve the current lifecycle: `DRAFT -> SENT -> PENDING_CONFIRM -> CONFIRMED -> PARTIAL_PAID -> PAID`, with `REJECTED`/`CANCELED` outcomes only through legal transitions.
- Keep customer confirm/dispute row-scoped through `/portal/debit-notes/:id/confirm` and `/portal/debit-notes/:id/dispute`.
- Require customer dispute reason, idempotency key, and expected document version. Persist immutable dispute evidence with actor, customer/legal-entity scope, reason, source version, and timestamp; do not rely on a bare `REJECTED` transition.
- Make the AR source explicit: an issued/eligible Debit Note and its adjustments feed `getCustomerReceivableSnapshot`; a tax-invoice reference must not post a second receivable.
- Preserve customer-cycle locks, completion/event business dates, original and processing due dates, and Q19 next-business-day behavior.
- Keep full-VND display and approved Vietnamese labels; do not abbreviate financial amounts.

### Chi hộ accounting invariants

For every recoverable chi hộ source, persist or expose five separately reconcilable links:

1. cash disbursement or employee/forwarder settlement source;
2. supplier/carrier payable when a third party is owed;
3. customer recoverable receivable created by the issued Debit Note;
4. service-fee/revenue line, when charged, separate from reimbursable principal;
5. customer receipt, AP payment, and/or non-cash offset settlement references.

Rules:

- reimbursable principal is not service-fee revenue;
- a supplier payable is not proof that cash was paid;
- a cash disbursement is not proof that the customer was billed;
- a customer receipt is not proof that the supplier was paid;
- only approved recoverables enter `billingDocumentLines`;
- debt offset remains a later manual, non-cash settlement and never creates another Debit Note line;
- all linked amounts reconcile under `round2dp()` with no hidden remainder and no double billing.

### Non-functional

- Drizzle ORM only; financial transitions occur in one database transaction with row/advisory locks where current services already require them.
- No write endpoint is accepted without its canonical idempotency key and expected version.
- Queue/list endpoints apply database filters, deterministic order, and page
  bounds before detail hydration; no unbounded or in-memory full-scan customer,
  expense, or document list.
- Desktop uses a bounded queue/detail workspace; tablet collapses detail to tabs/sheet; mobile uses cards, 44px controls, readable wrapping, and no horizontal overflow.
- Audit evidence records actor, role, source version, before/after/delta, evidence references, reason, and resulting document/ledger reference.

## Decision Gate D3-INV — legal/tax invoice authority

This gate is blocking for provider-specific implementation and must be recorded in an accepted product/finance decision before Step 7.

Required answers:

1. Is “hóa đơn” a legal e-invoice governed by an external provider/tax authority, or only an external/manual reference captured after Debit Note confirmation?
2. Which event authorizes handoff: `SENT`, `PENDING_CONFIRM`, or `CONFIRMED`? The phase default is `CONFIRMED` because the requested outcome orders customer response before invoice handoff.
3. Who owns numbering, signature, issue date, tax treatment, correction/cancellation, and immutable rendered artifact?
4. Can a disputed Debit Note be invoiced? Default: no.
5. Does the external invoice replace the Debit Note as the AR document, or is it a reference on the same receivable? Default: reference only; never post AR twice.
6. What is the replay key and provider recovery behavior for timeout, duplicate response, correction, and cancellation?

Allowed outcomes:

- **Provider authority selected:** implement the adapter and durable handoff/reference records described below.
- **Manual external authority selected:** store a governed, immutable external invoice reference and artifact metadata; do not generate a legal invoice in Silversea.
- **Decision deferred:** ship no provider call and show “Chưa tích hợp hóa đơn pháp lý”; Phase 3 remains incomplete if the accepted scope requires actual legal invoice issuance.

Binding consequence:

- The current plan default is **reference-only**, because `billing_documents` remains the sole AR posting authority. This is not approved product truth until finance/legal records D3-INV.
- If finance/legal decides that the tax invoice replaces the Debit Note as the legal debt instrument, stop Phase 3 and redesign the one-posting transition/alias, correction/cancellation lifecycle, numbering/artifact authority, AR snapshot, and migration tests. Do not reuse the reference-only adapter unchanged.

Adapter boundary (proposed, provider-neutral):

```ts
export interface LegalInvoiceAdapter {
  issue(request: LegalInvoiceIssueRequest): Promise<LegalInvoiceIssueResult>;
  getStatus(reference: LegalInvoiceReference): Promise<LegalInvoiceStatusResult>;
  cancel(request: LegalInvoiceCancelRequest): Promise<LegalInvoiceStatusResult>;
}
```

The request carries the issued Debit Note ID/version, immutable identity snapshot, tax/customer identity, currency, totals, line snapshots, and an idempotency key. The result carries provider/reference IDs, status, issued timestamp, artifact checksum/location metadata, and raw-provider payload hash only. It never receives permission to write AR or mutate a Debit Note directly.

## Architecture and Data Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A["Expense evidence / tripExpenses"] --> B["requestTripExpenseDecision"]
  B --> C["Governance check + approve"]
  C --> D["applyTripExpenseGovernanceAction"]
  D --> E["propagateExpenseApproval"]
  E --> F["generateDraft / saveDocument"]
  F --> G["requestBillingDocumentIssue"]
  G --> H["Independent check + approve"]
  H --> I["applyBillingDocumentGovernanceAction"]
  I --> J["Debit Note issued + source locked"]
  J --> K["Portal confirm or dispute"]
  K -->|confirmed| L["Legal-invoice adapter/reference gate"]
  K -->|disputed| M["Review / adjustment workflow"]
  J --> N["Customer receivable authority"]
  L -. reference only; no second posting .-> N
```

### Authoritative write sequence

1. CUS submits a decision request with evidence, reason, `expectedExpenseVersion`, and idempotency key.
2. Governance independently checks/approves; `applyTripExpenseGovernanceAction` wins once and propagates approved source state.
3. Draft generation reads only eligible approved sources, source versions, customer scope, and business dates.
4. Save acquires the customer/period/source guards and rejects an already claimed recoverable source.
5. Issue request captures source diffs and immutable snapshots. Independent approval calls `applyBillingDocumentGovernanceAction`, posts the existing ledger delta once, and locks sources/period authority.
6. Portal confirmation/dispute transitions the same document with scoped authentication and optimistic state checks.
7. On confirmed handoff, the same transaction enqueues a versioned legal-invoice effect through the existing durable-effect authority. AR continues to originate from the existing Debit Note/ledger authority under the accepted reference-only outcome.
8. Any post-lock correction creates an adjustment/reversal linked to the original source and period.

