## Success Criteria

- [ ] A verified recoverable cost can be traced from evidence and governance through one issued Debit Note and one AR obligation.
- [ ] Unapproved, stale, wrong-customer, locked, or already-billed sources cannot enter a new document.
- [ ] CUS verification is visibly named but persists no duplicate approval authority.
- [ ] Accountant issue follows maker/checker/approver, expected-version, idempotency, and first-winner rules.
- [ ] Customer confirmation/dispute is scoped, auditable, and usable on desktop and mobile.
- [ ] Debit Note and legal/tax invoice meanings are visibly separate; D3-INV is accepted before provider work.
- [ ] Legal-invoice handoff/reference can never double-post AR.
- [ ] Chi hộ cash, AP, recoverable AR, fee/revenue, and settlements remain independently traceable and reconcile.
- [ ] All post-lock changes are linked adjustments/reversals, never in-place edits.
- [ ] All affected QA gates and independent review are green with artifacts in `qa/`.

## Risks, Security, and RBAC

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Duplicate billing of one recoverable | Transactional source locks, active-document uniqueness, expected versions, idempotency, concurrency tests |
| Debit Note mistaken for legal tax invoice | D3-INV, separate labels/types, provider-neutral adapter/reference, no shared numbering |
| Duplicate AR on legal-invoice handoff | Adapter has no ledger capability; invariant test asserts one receivable |
| Self-approval or first-winner race | Governance policy, maker/checker/approver separation, locked apply transaction |
| Cross-customer portal access | Authenticated legal-entity scope on every read/write/export |
| Sensitive evidence/provider data leak | Store storage-key hash/reference and provider payload hash only; never credentials/raw payload in audit |
| Post-lock silent correction | Immutable issued snapshot plus governed adjustment/reversal |
| Client-only eligibility enforcement | Server revalidates all sources in save/issue transactions |

RBAC minimum:

- CUS/maker is existing `CLERK`: view only recoverable costs linked to shipments
  inside the live CLERK assignment/business-unit/customer scope and request an
  evidence/cost decision or draft handoff; no general `financial` permission,
  Debit Note issue approval, AR/AP, or treasury access.
- Add a dedicated recoverable-cost resource/action and row-scoped service/route
  boundary for CLERK. This phase does not add a `CUS` role enum and must not
  mount CLERK actions behind the coarse `financial` permission.
- ACCOUNTANT checker/maker: build/review documents and request issue; cannot approve own action.
- MANAGER/ADMIN configured approver: check/approve according to governance policy.
- CUSTOMER: view/export and confirm/dispute only records in the authenticated legal-entity scope.
- Legal-invoice integration worker: service identity limited to outbox/reference updates; no general ledger/portal permissions.

## Migration, Backfill, Rollback, and Next Steps

### Migration/backfill

- Reuse existing `tripExpenses`, `billingDocuments`, `billingDocumentLines`, governance, period-lock, ledger, and payment authority.
- Before adding a constraint, audit existing non-canceled duplicate `EXPENSE` source claims. Do not auto-delete or silently choose a winner; emit a reviewed remediation report.
- Backfill source-version/evidence/reference metadata only from authoritative existing rows. Unknown historical data remains explicitly `UNKNOWN`, never fabricated.
- If D3-INV selects invoice references, create the provider-neutral table/columns through `schema.ts` and a Drizzle-generated migration. Existing documents start with `NOT_REQUESTED`/no reference.
- Do not backfill a legal-invoice reference from a Debit Note number or export filename.

### Rollback

- Feature-flag the CUS queue and invoice handoff UI independently from core billing.
- Disable new adapter dispatch first; retain outbox/reference rows for audit and recovery.
- Roll application reads back to current document/portal views without deleting issued documents, source links, governance, or ledger entries.
- Reverse financial mistakes through existing adjustment/reversal services; never delete or rewrite ledger history.
- A schema rollback must preserve external invoice references already issued; destructive down migration is prohibited after first production handoff.

### Next steps

- Phase 4 consumes the explicit Debit Note AR authority, but owns receipts, allocation, AP payments, offsets, and treasury.
- Phase 5 consumes settled/authoritative revenue and cost links; it must not infer profit from invoice-reference status.
- Phase 6 aligns role navigation, final responsive workspaces, training copy, rollout, and production QA.
