- [ ] Vendor and carrier invoices/evidence, AP aging, payments, due balances, and overpayments remain separately traceable.
- [ ] Q06 fuel allocation uses actual slips/logs with deterministic rounding.
- [ ] Debt offset remains manual, same-entity, VND-only, capped, governed, reversible, and non-cash.
- [ ] Every post-cutover receipt/payment creates exactly one linked treasury movement in the same transaction.
- [ ] Pending governance actions and pre-cutover idempotency keys have an explicit versioned disposition; none can bypass or become silently stranded at activation.
- [ ] Cash/bank balances come only from explicit accounts, opening balances, posted movements, and reversals.
- [ ] Unsupported internal transfers/statement activity cannot enter through a
  manual shortcut and makes the affected book balance partial/unavailable.
- [ ] AR/AP/treasury workspaces are role-correct, bounded, responsive, accessible, and use full VND.
- [ ] All mandatory gates, E2E, migration checks, manual QA, and independent review are green with artifacts in `qa/`.

## Risks, Security, and RBAC

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Treasury balance inferred from receivables/payables | Dedicated account/entry tables and balance service with no aging-service dependency |
| Double cash posting on payment retry | Source uniqueness, idempotency payload hash, first-winner governance, same-transaction insert |
| Ledger succeeds but cash link fails | Owning ledger and treasury writes share one transaction; failure rolls both back |
| Offset incorrectly affects cash | Service-level prohibition plus zero-entry invariant test |
| Book balance mistaken for reconciled bank balance | Explicit balance kind/status and separate treasury-operations prerequisite |
| Unauthorized account/payment mutation | Casbin/role middleware plus service-layer policy and maker/checker/approver |
| Historical mapping fabricates balances | Evidence-only backfill; explicit opening balance; unmapped report |

RBAC minimum:

- ACCOUNTANT maker: create receipt/payment requests and view AR/AP/source-linked
  book balances; cannot approve own action or administer treasury accounts.
- MANAGER/ADMIN approver: check/approve within governance policy; account creation/opening-balance/close is ADMIN or separately configured treasury authority.
- CUSTOMER: view only own Debit Notes/statements/payment application; no treasury account or AP visibility.
- CUS/dispatch: see credit warning/override status needed for service decisions; no treasury balance or payment mutation.
- Background reminder worker: read scoped receivable authority and emit notifications only.

## Migration, Backfill, Cutover, Rollback, and Next Steps

### Migration

- Add the proposed treasury tables and constraints through `backend/src/db/schema.ts` and a generated Drizzle migration.
- Keep currency explicit even though initial scope is VND.
- Use immutable `sourceType + sourceId` linkage and a separate linked reversal instead of mutable status-only correction.
- Do not reuse `ledger.balance`, customer/vendor balances, `companyInfo.bankAccount`, or statement closing balance as treasury opening balance.

### Backfill

1. Produce a read-only inventory of historical customer receipts and vendor/carrier payments with authoritative references.
2. Map a historical movement to a treasury account only when bank/cash evidence identifies the account and amount.
3. Leave ambiguous history in an `unmapped` migration report; exclude it from account balance.
4. Enter each account opening balance/date through reviewed governance so it bridges the chosen historical cutover.
5. Reconcile the first imported statement to the opening balance and new entries before enabling account-required writes.

### Cutover

- Stage 1: deploy read-only account/entry schema and backfill report.
- Stage 2: configure/approve accounts and opening balances; enable shadow invariant checks without changing existing writes.
- Stage 3: atomically link all new receipt/payment writes and require `treasuryAccountId`.
- Stage 4: expose the source-linked book-balance read model with explicit
  freshness/partial status; reconciled treasury operations remain deferred.
- Stop the cutover if ledger-to-treasury source count or amount invariants fail.

### Rollback

- Before Stage 3, disable treasury UI/writes and retain harmless empty/read-only tables.
- After Stage 3, never run a build or mode that allows ledger-only direct-money writes. Rollback gates create/check/approve/refund/reversal together, or restores only a compatibility-floor build that contains the treasury dual-write and epoch check.
- Preserve all posted account/movement/reversal authority for audit; do not
  drop populated tables.
- Correct financial errors with linked ledger/treasury reversal, not deletion or balance overwrite.
- Rehearse rollback by attempting a receipt and supplier payment against an incompatible build/mode and proving early rejection before ledger mutation.

### Next steps

- Phase 5 reads AR/AP settlement and explicit treasury balance for profitability/cash reporting, keeping forecasts labeled and separate from actual cash.
- Phase 6 finalizes role navigation, rollout/training, responsive coverage, production data checks, and release evidence.
</file>

