# Phase 5: Profitability and CEO dashboard

## Context Links

- [Master plan](./plan.md)
- [Phase 4: AR AP and treasury controls](./phase-04-ar-ap-and-treasury-controls.md)
- [Accounting and plan dependencies](./research/accounting-and-plan-dependencies.md)
- [Codebase domain map](./research/codebase-domain-map.md)
- [Role UX and UI patterns](./research/role-ux-and-ui-patterns.md)
- [`CONTEXT.md`](../../CONTEXT.md)
- [`docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md`](../../docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md)
- Existing reporting authorities:
  [`pnl.service.ts`](../../backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts),
  [`profit-distribution.service.ts`](../../backend/src/services/profit-distribution.service.ts),
  [`dashboard-stats.service.ts`](../../backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts),
  and [`dashboard-widgets.service.ts`](../../backend/src/services/dashboard-widgets.service.ts)

## Overview

Build one canonical profitability read model and executive dashboard over the
existing shipment, trip, expense, billing, AR, AP, treasury, P&L, and profit
distribution authorities. The dashboard remains a read surface, never a ledger,
allocation engine, or second source of truth.

The phase captures immutable direct-attribution snapshots when a trip reaches
the financially reportable state, exposes reconciled profitability by customer,
route, vehicle, dispatcher, salesperson, month, year, and container, and
publishes the agreed executive KPI set with explicit definitions and an
`asOf` timestamp. Shared overhead stays in a visible unallocated bucket until a
separately governed allocation policy is approved.

“CEO dashboard” describes the audience and information hierarchy. It does not
add `Role.CEO`; the existing `MANAGER` and `ADMIN` roles receive the executive
reporting capability.

## Scope Boundary

### In scope

- Reuse the current P&L, profit-distribution, dashboard, AR, AP, and Phase 4
  treasury authorities.
- Snapshot direct attribution for shipment, trip, container, customer, route,
  vehicle, dispatcher, and salesperson at the reportable financial boundary.
- Add canonical profitability query contracts, reconciliation diagnostics,
  pagination, drill-down identifiers, metric definitions, and `asOf` metadata.
- Replace frontend-derived or estimated dashboard values with backend report
  results.
- Render every monetary value with full `vi-VN` digits.
- Keep shared overhead, ownerless-truck distribution, and missing attribution
  as three different concepts.

### Out of scope

- A new ledger, a new P&L engine, or a parallel profit-distribution lifecycle.
- Allocating shared overhead without an approved allocation policy.
- Inferring cash or bank balance from AR, AP, payment method, or company bank
  account metadata.
- Equal-splitting a trip's profit across containers when direct line/container
  provenance is absent.
- Historical mutation of completed trips to make new dimensions appear filled.
- A new CEO role, a new application shell, or new dashboard-only permissions.
- Compact currency (`k`, `tr`, `tỷ`, `M`, `B`) in any executive or finance KPI.

## Key Insights

1. `getPnlReport()` already owns period P&L and uses
   `tripCompletionBusinessDateSql`; it should feed profitability instead of
   being reimplemented.
2. `getDashboardStats()` already composes P&L and receivables, while
   `getDashboardWidgets()` has period logic that must be aligned to the official
   completed-trip business date before either is treated as canonical.
3. `useDashboardData()` currently derives route profit in the browser and can
   fabricate a `55/25/20` cost allocation. Those fallbacks must be deleted once
   the canonical report is available; missing data must be visible, not
   estimated.
4. `distributeTruckProfit()` governs owner-level profit distribution.
   `undistributedProfit` means ownerless-truck distribution and must not be
   reused for unallocated shared overhead.
5. Customer, route, and vehicle identities can be traced today. Dispatcher and
   salesperson are not yet production-grade authorities: accepted dispatcher
   identity is not durably owned on the active command path, and salesperson
   has no authoritative field. Phase 1/2 must introduce versioned ownership,
   effective dates/reassignment history, RBAC, and capture timing; neither
   dimension may guess from `createdBy`, assigned handler, or current display
   state.
6. A trip may reference multiple shipment containers. Store container identity
   in child snapshot rows; do not duplicate the trip financial amount for each
   container. Container profitability requires direct line/container
   provenance, otherwise the amount stays in the missing-attribution bucket.
7. Phase 4 must provide an explicit source-linked treasury **book-balance**
   contract. Phase 5 labels it accordingly and shows `PARTIAL`/unavailable when
   unsupported transfer/statement activity exists; it never claims bank
   reconciliation or invents cash/bank numbers.

## Requirements

### Functional requirements

- A reportable trip uses the official completed/locked financial state and
  completion business date already enforced by P&L.
- The attribution snapshot is immutable for a specific trip/source version and
  idempotent under retries.
- The snapshot and P&L row share one canonical financial posting/version ID.
  Generic trip version is not sufficient. Active/superseded selection is
  explicit, and unrelated operational edits cannot change the joined
  financial snapshot.
- Historical reports read snapshots rather than mutable display names or
  current assignments.
- Profitability filters support:
  - `CUSTOMER`
  - `ROUTE`
  - `VEHICLE`
  - `DISPATCHER`
  - `SALESPERSON`
  - `MONTH`
  - `YEAR`
  - `CONTAINER`
- Every report response includes requested period, resolved period, `asOf`,
  timezone, definition version, source coverage, reconciliation totals, and
  missing-attribution counts.
- `asOf` is enforced by one consistent-read protocol: either one read-only
  `REPEATABLE READ` transaction passed through all database-backed authorities,
  or per-authority committed watermarks captured before/after with retry on
  change. Cached components must carry compatible watermarks; a mixed snapshot
  is returned as partial/error, never as reconciled.
- Drill-down rows carry stable source identifiers sufficient to open the
  existing shipment, trip, customer, vehicle, debt, or finance surface.
- Shared overhead is reported as `SHARED_OVERHEAD` and remains unallocated.
- Missing dimension data is reported as `MISSING_ATTRIBUTION`, with no fallback
  to creator, dispatcher, owner, equal split, or “Unknown” silently mixed into
  a real entity.
- Ownerless-truck profit distribution remains `undistributedProfit` in the
  existing distribution contract.
- The executive dashboard returns the authoritative KPI list below and no
  client-side monetary derivation is required.

### Metric contract

| KPI | Canonical definition and source | Drill-down |
|---|---|---|
| Revenue today | Sum `recordedTripRevenue` for reportable trips whose completion business date is today in the configured Vietnam business timezone | Existing trip/shipment register filtered to the resolved date |
| Revenue month | Sum `recordedTripRevenue` for the current official reporting month | `/finance` or `/profit` with period query |
| Monthly cost | P&L direct trip cost plus approved shared/company expense totals for the month; allocation status remains explicit | `/profit` cost/category detail |
| Monthly profit | P&L revenue less the canonical monthly cost; must equal the report reconciliation total | `/profit` period detail |
| Accounts receivable | Phase 4/current customer receivable closing balance as of the dashboard timestamp | `/debt` with `asOf` |
| Overdue accounts receivable | Same receivable authority, filtered by authoritative due date earlier than `asOf` and unpaid balance greater than zero | `/debt` overdue filter |
| Cash | Phase 4 source-linked book balance for cash-classified accounts as of the dashboard timestamp; partial/unavailable when unsupported activity exists | `/finance` book-balance detail |
| Bank | Phase 4 source-linked book balance for bank-classified accounts as of the dashboard timestamp; not a reconciled statement balance | `/finance` book-balance detail |
| Top 10 customers | Canonical recorded revenue by snapshotted customer for the selected period, descending with deterministic tie-break | `/finance?dimension=CUSTOMER` |
| Top 10 debtors | Receivable closing balance by customer as of the timestamp, descending with deterministic tie-break | `/debt` |
| Cost by type | Canonical direct trip cost types plus approved shared expense categories; allocated/unallocated status visible | `/profit` category detail |
| Profit by vehicle | P&L revenue and direct vehicle costs by snapshotted vehicle, preserving external/unassigned buckets | `/profit?dimension=VEHICLE` |

### Non-functional requirements

- Monetary calculations remain decimal-safe and use existing rounding helpers;
  no JavaScript floating-point recomputation of totals in the UI.
- List endpoints are bounded and paginated. Top lists are limited server-side to
  10; drill-downs use deterministic sort plus cursor or page/limit.
- Query filters are allowlisted and parameterized through Drizzle; no raw SQL
  application path is introduced.
- Report results are cacheable only with a versioned key containing period,
  dimension, `asOf`, source version, and rollout mode. Mutation events that
  change an authority invalidate the relevant cache.
- Empty, partial, stale, and failed states remain distinguishable and
  accessible.
- Dashboard and profitability responses remain compatible during rollout;
  additive fields land before frontend consumption.
- Database filter/order/page bounds apply before detail hydration for AR/AP and
  profitability inputs. Volume acceptance records query plan/scanned rows,
  query count, response bytes, p95 latency, and memory; slicing an in-memory
  full scan does not pass.

## Architecture And Data Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  S["Shipment and dispatch authorities"] --> A["Immutable attribution snapshot"]
  T["Completed or locked trip financial snapshot"] --> A
  E["Expense and direct-cost authorities"] --> P["Existing P&L service"]
  B["Billing, AR, AP, and Phase 4 treasury"] --> D["Executive reporting read model"]
  A --> R["Profitability query service"]
  P --> R
  P --> D
  R --> D
  G["Existing profit distribution governance"] --> D
  D --> API["Existing financial report routes"]
  API --> UI["Dashboard, Finance, and Profit pages"]
```

### Write boundary

1. The trip completion/lock transaction creates or selects a canonical
   financial posting/version ID and calls the attribution snapshot builder.
2. The builder resolves shipment and source version, customer, route, vehicle,
   current accepted dispatch handoff, salesperson authority, and child
   containers.
3. The header and child rows are inserted with a unique source/version key.
   Retrying the same event returns the same snapshot.
4. A later correction creates a new governed source version; it never updates a
   historical snapshot in place.

### Read boundary

1. `getPnlReport()` supplies canonical revenue, costs, profit, and the shared
   financial posting/version identifier for the resolved reporting period.
2. `getProfitabilityReport()` joins those reportable financial rows to the
   matching attribution snapshot and groups only by the requested dimension.
3. `getExecutiveDashboard()` composes canonical P&L, profitability, receivable,
   payable, and Phase 4 treasury read models under the accepted consistent-read
   protocol and one compatible watermark set.
4. Routes authorize the request using the existing financial resource and
   return definitions, coverage, reconciliation, and `asOf`.
5. The frontend formats and displays returned values; it does not invent
   allocations or recompute accounting totals.

### Attribution snapshot model

`profitability_attribution_snapshots` **Create (proposed)**:

- unique `source_trip_id` + `source_financial_version`
- completion business date, reporting month, reporting year, timezone
- shipment ID/version
- customer ID and display-name snapshot
- route ID and route-label snapshot
- vehicle ID and plate snapshot
- dispatcher user ID and name snapshot
- salesperson user ID and name snapshot
- source fingerprint, captured timestamp, capture reason

`profitability_attribution_containers` **Create (proposed)**:

- snapshot ID
- shipment container ID
- trip/container-line provenance ID when available
- container number/type snapshot
- directly attributable revenue/cost/profit fields only when the source
  authority provides those values

The header owns trip-level money once. Child container rows never repeat a full
trip amount. If direct container financial provenance is unavailable, the
container report places that money in `MISSING_ATTRIBUTION`.

### Reconciliation invariants

- Total grouped direct revenue equals canonical reportable revenue.
- Total grouped direct cost equals canonical direct cost.
- Total grouped direct profit plus shared overhead treatment equals P&L net
  profit according to the selected report definition.
- `SHARED_OVERHEAD`, `MISSING_ATTRIBUTION`, external vehicle, unassigned
  vehicle, and `undistributedProfit` remain separately labeled.
- Rounding residual is zero at report precision; a non-zero residual makes the
  response diagnostic/partial and emits an operational alert.
- Top 10 lists are projections of the same reconciled full result, not separate
  calculations.

