## Dependency Map

- **Phase 1**: financial state/version and invoice/treasury authority decisions.
- **Phase 2**: stable shipment/customer interaction and dispatcher handoff
  history.
- **Phase 3**: recoverable cost, debit-note, and invoice handoff outcomes.
- **Phase 4**: canonical AR, overdue AR, AP, payment application, cash, and bank
  read models.
- **Phase 5 output consumed by Phase 6**: stable report APIs, role-safe
  drill-downs, feature-switch behavior, migration/backfill status, and
  reconciliation fixtures.
- If the Phase 4 treasury contract is not implemented and green, cash and bank
  cards remain explicitly unavailable and Phase 5 cannot be marked done.
- New reportable work cannot mark the salesperson/dispatcher dimensions
  complete until Phase 1/2 supplies canonical versioned ownership. Historical
  rows with no evidence remain visible `MISSING_ATTRIBUTION`; they are never
  guessed or silently excluded.

## Tests Before Implementation

Capture characterization tests before altering behavior:

1. Freeze current `getPnlReport()` totals and Q20 completion-business-date
   behavior for representative own-truck, external-truck, unassigned-truck,
   direct-expense, and company-expense cases.
2. Freeze `getDashboardStats()` and `getDashboardWidgets()` response behavior,
   including any current date-basis divergence.
3. Prove the browser-derived route profit and `55/25/20` fallback with a focused
   `useDashboardData()` test, then make that test fail only when the fallback is
   removed in favor of the server result.
4. Prove current distribution behavior for ownerless trucks so it cannot be
   conflated with shared overhead.
5. Add fixtures with:
   - one shipment and one trip;
   - multiple containers;
   - changed customer/route/vehicle labels after completion;
   - accepted and superseded dispatcher handoffs;
   - absent salesperson attribution;
   - direct and shared costs;
   - unapplied receipt and overdue receivable;
   - Phase 4 cash and bank balances.
6. Record baseline API timings and response sizes for the chosen realistic
   period so pagination/index changes can be evaluated.

## Implementation

### 1. Lock report definitions and versioning

- Write one versioned metric registry shared by dashboard and profitability
  responses.
- Use the official business timezone and completion-date period functions.
- Define the accounting relationship between direct cost, shared overhead,
  gross profit, and net profit in tests before exposing UI.
- Treat metric-definition changes as contract changes requiring a version bump,
  regression fixtures, and release note.

### 2. Add attribution snapshots

- Generate additive Drizzle schema and migration.
- Wire accepted dispatcher identity and salesperson ownership in their owning
  operational workflow first, including reassignment/supersession and effective
  dates. Snapshot only the accepted source version.
- Add uniqueness, foreign-key behavior, source fingerprint, and indexes for
  period plus each dimension.
- Capture snapshots in the same transaction or canonical event path as the
  reportable financial-state transition.
- Exercise the real status-machine and governed-adjustment callers in P0 tests;
  prove retries, completion/lock, reopen, and correction select one active
  version without double capture.
- Store display snapshots for historical labels while retaining stable IDs for
  drill-down.
- Keep child containers normalized and store financial values only with direct
  source provenance.

### 3. Backfill safely

- Implement a Drizzle-based script with `--dry-run`, `--batch-size`,
  `--after-id`, `--status`, and deterministic resume.
- Build snapshots from historical source versions without changing shipment,
  trip, ledger, billing, receipt, or distribution rows.
- Classify absent dispatcher, salesperson, container provenance, or legacy
  source version as missing attribution.
- Produce counts and reconciliation by period before any activation.
- Stop activation if duplicate sources, financial mismatch, or orphan rate
  exceeds the explicit release threshold.

### 4. Build the profitability read model

- Query only reportable source versions for the requested period.
- Join canonical P&L amounts to immutable attribution.
- Group by one allowlisted dimension per request.
- Return explicit external, unassigned, shared-overhead, and
  missing-attribution buckets.
- Add bounded pagination and deterministic ordering.
- Include source IDs and filters for existing-route drill-downs.

### 5. Compose the executive dashboard

- Extend the existing dashboard authority rather than creating a competing
  service.
- Compose all twelve KPIs from canonical services and include source watermark,
  definition, and freshness.
- Use the same profitability result for top customers, cost by type, and profit
  by vehicle.
- Use the same receivable result for AR, overdue AR, and top debtors.
- Use only the Phase 4 source-linked book-balance contract for cash and bank,
  preserving its balance kind, freshness, and partial/unavailable status.
- Execute all authority reads under the accepted consistent-snapshot protocol
  and reject/retry mixed watermarks; `asOf` is not presentation-only metadata.
- Keep source-specific failures visible as partial data; never substitute zero
  for unavailable authority.

### 6. Publish additive APIs

- Validate dates, dimension, page size, sort, and `asOf`.
- Add endpoint-level `ADMIN`/`MANAGER` enforcement (or a dedicated executive
  reporting resource) for dashboard/widgets and executive drill-downs.
- Add cache keys and invalidation tied to financial source versions.
- Return machine-readable diagnostic codes for stale source, partial coverage,
  reconciliation mismatch, and missing treasury authority.

### 7. Replace frontend derivations

- Consume canonical dashboard and profitability responses.
- Delete estimated cost allocation and client-side accounting calculations.
- Render full digits using current format helpers.
- Add compact information hierarchy using existing design-system primitives:
  Untitled UI `table`, `filter-bar`, `filter-dropdown-menu`, and chart patterns;
  Tailkit statistics/page-heading/table composition patterns; existing local
  Shadcn-style primitives. Adapt patterns without adding a second component
  library.
- Use a bounded desktop table and mobile summary cards with an explicit
  drill-down action. Keep definitions and `asOf` reachable by keyboard and
  screen reader.

### 8. Add observability and reconciliation

- Emit structured metrics for capture failures, backfill coverage,
  missing-attribution rate, stale watermarks, report latency, and
  reconciliation mismatch.
- Add an operations-only reconciliation endpoint or script output; do not expose
  internal diagnostics to customer or portal roles.
- Make a mismatch block report activation and Phase 6 rollout.

## Tests After Implementation

### Automated backend

- Snapshot retry creates one header and the correct child containers.
- Historical names and assignments remain stable after source records change.
- A governed correction creates a new source version without mutating history.
- Financial correction and later unrelated operational edit still select the
  exact P&L-linked attribution version once.
- Salesperson absence is `MISSING_ATTRIBUTION`; it never falls back to
  `createdBy`.
- Multi-container trip value is not duplicated or equally split.
- Every supported dimension reconciles to the same canonical totals.
- Shared overhead, missing attribution, external/unassigned vehicle, and
  `undistributedProfit` remain distinct.
- Dashboard metric definitions and `asOf` are present and versioned.
- AR, treasury, and P&L cannot be combined under one reconciled `asOf` when
  their committed watermarks differ.
- Revenue today/month use completion business date.
- AR/overdue/top-debtor values use one receivable watermark.
- Cash/bank fail visibly when Phase 4 authority is absent.
- Unauthorized roles receive `403` for report routes.
- `ACCOUNTANT` receives `403` from executive dashboard/widgets and executive
  drill-downs even though it retains authorized finance workspace access.
- Pagination, filters, and invalid dates are bounded and validated.
- Backfill dry-run writes nothing; active run is resumable and idempotent.

### Automated frontend

- No test observes `formatCompact` for finance money.
- No test observes the `55/25/20` cost fallback.
- KPI loading, empty, partial, stale, failed, and complete states render
  distinctly.
- Every KPI drill-down preserves period/`asOf` filters.
- Profitability dimension switching uses isolated query keys.
- Large values render in full `vi-VN` digits without horizontal page overflow.
- Keyboard users can reach definitions, filters, tables/cards, and drill-downs.

### Manual and E2E

- Reconcile one selected month from dashboard -> profitability -> P&L -> trip
  detail.
- Change current customer/route/vehicle/dispatcher labels and prove historical
  report labels stay snapshotted.
- Verify a multi-container shipment does not multiply totals.
- Verify realistic top-10 and long-label behavior at desktop, tablet, and
  mobile widths.
- Verify `MANAGER` and `ADMIN` can view the executive dashboard while portal
  roles cannot.

## P0 / P1 / P2 Test Matrix

| Priority | Test focus | Required evidence |
|---|---|---|
| P0 | Financial reconciliation, completion-date authority, immutable/versioned snapshots, no container duplication, treasury authority, RBAC denial, backfill idempotency | Backend tests, migration rehearsal, E2E reconciliation, exact command artifacts |
| P0 | Financial-version join and consistent `asOf` under concurrent receipt/correction | Completion/correction/operational-edit tests plus repeatable-read or watermark-retry evidence |
| P1 | All eight profitability dimensions, all twelve dashboard KPIs, full-digit formatting, pagination, partial/stale/error states, drill-down filter preservation | Backend/frontend suites plus desktop/tablet/mobile screenshots |
| P2 | Definition affordance clarity, deterministic top-list ties, chart/table usability, cache efficiency, export/read-only ergonomics | Visual review, performance sample, reviewer report |

## Regression Gate

During implementation, save every command and its exit status under `qa/` using
the repository naming convention, including red runs and the green rerun:

- `pnpm lint`
- `cd backend && npx tsc --noEmit`
- `cd backend && pnpm test`
- `cd frontend && npx tsc -b`
- `cd frontend && pnpm test`
- `make build`
- `cd e2e && ./run_all.sh`

Minimum task artifacts:

- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_lint.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_backend-typecheck.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_backend-test.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_frontend-typecheck.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_frontend-test.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_build.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_e2e.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_migration-backfill.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_reconciliation.log`
- `qa/<date>_profitability-dashboard_review.md`
- desktop/tablet/mobile screenshots named by role and viewport

The gate is red if any supported dimension fails reconciliation, any KPI uses a
fallback, any required role is untested, or an affected command is not green.

## Risks, Security, And RBAC

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Dashboard becomes a second accounting authority | Keep it as a composition/read model; tests compare every total to canonical services |
| Historical reports drift with mutable labels/assignments | Immutable versioned attribution snapshot with display snapshot and stable ID |
| Container totals are multiplied | Normalize child containers; require direct provenance or use missing-attribution bucket |
| Salesperson is guessed from creator or dispatcher | Introduce an explicit authority or surface missing attribution |
| Shared overhead is silently allocated | Keep `SHARED_OVERHEAD` visible and unallocated until governed policy exists |
| Ownerless profit is confused with overhead | Preserve existing `undistributedProfit` contract and label separately |
| Cash/bank is inferred from non-treasury data | Hard dependency on Phase 4 treasury position; visible unavailable state |
| Broad finance data leaks to portal roles | Existing financial Casbin authorization plus route tests for every role |
| Large reports create unbounded work | Server pagination, indexed dimensions, deterministic limits, bounded UI |
| Cache returns a mixed watermark | Versioned cache key and source watermark; no cross-period/dimension reuse |
| Backfill changes financial truth | Additive snapshot writes only; dry-run, batches, idempotency, reconciliation |

### RBAC contract

- `ADMIN`: executive dashboard, profitability, all authorized drill-downs.
- `MANAGER`: same reporting audience, subject to existing action-level finance
  governance.
- `ACCOUNTANT`: finance/profitability access according to current financial
  policy; do not grant executive-only mutation because the page is visible.
- `CLERK`, `CUSTOMER`, `DRIVER`, `FORWARDER`: no executive profitability
  endpoint or finance drill-down.
- Frontend visibility is convenience only; backend financial authorization is
  authoritative.

## Migration, Backfill, And Rollback

### Migration

- Add tables, indexes, unique constraints, and nullable direct-attribution
  columns first.
- Deploy capture in `shadow` mode while existing reporting remains active.
- Never drop or rewrite existing trip, shipment, billing, expense, ledger,
  payment, or distribution data.
- Verify forward migration on an empty database and a production-like copy.

### Backfill

- Dry-run all historical periods and report exact classified counts.
- Backfill newest closed periods first in bounded batches.
- Resume from a persisted cursor; reruns are no-ops for identical source
  versions.
- Require zero financial residual and an accepted missing-attribution profile
  before activating the new read model.
- Do not “repair” absent salesperson/container provenance by heuristics.

### Rollback

- Switch reporting attribution mode from `active` to `shadow`/`off`.
- Keep existing `/reports/dashboard` compatible and fall back only to its prior
  canonical fields, never to browser estimates.
- Stop new snapshot capture if necessary while preserving additive rows for
  investigation.
- Roll back application code independently; do not delete snapshot data during
  incident response.
- A destructive schema rollback requires a separately reviewed backup and
  migration procedure and is not part of routine rollback.

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Every profitability dimension returns reconciled canonical totals.
- [ ] Direct attribution is immutable, versioned, retry-idempotent, and
  backfilled without changing existing finance records.
- [ ] Shipment, trip, container, customer, route, vehicle, dispatcher, and
  salesperson coverage is visible; new dispatcher/salesperson authority is
  versioned and historical missing sources are not guessed.
- [ ] Shared overhead is visibly unallocated and distinct from
  `undistributedProfit` and missing attribution.
- [ ] All twelve authoritative executive KPIs expose metric definition,
  resolved period, source watermark, and `asOf`.
- [ ] Revenue, costs, profit, AR, overdue AR, cash, and bank reconcile to their
  named source authorities.
- [ ] One financial posting/version ID joins P&L and attribution, and one
  consistent snapshot/watermark set backs every reconciled dashboard response.
- [ ] Frontend dashboard code contains no estimated accounting fallback or
  compact financial format.
- [ ] `MANAGER` and `ADMIN` reach the executive dashboard without adding
  `Role.CEO`; unauthorized roles are rejected by the API.
- [ ] Desktop, tablet, and mobile views remain bounded, readable, keyboard
  accessible, and free of horizontal page overflow.
- [ ] Migration, backfill, cache, failure-state, and rollback behaviors are
  tested.
- [ ] Every affected QA gate is green and its complete artifact is saved under
  `qa/`.

## Implementation Todos

- [ ] Confirm the Phase 4 treasury contract name and replace the proposed
  reference without duplicating it.
- [ ] Implement and verify authoritative dispatcher acceptance and
  salesperson ownership in the Phase 1/2 operational workflow; approve
  explicit missing-attribution only for historical rows lacking evidence.
- [ ] Freeze metric definition version 1 and completion-date semantics.
- [ ] Add and rehearse additive attribution migration.
- [ ] Implement transactional snapshot capture and safe backfill.
- [ ] Implement all-dimension profitability and reconciliation.
- [ ] Extend the existing dashboard read model and routes.
- [ ] Remove browser accounting fallbacks and compact currency.
- [ ] Complete automated, E2E, responsive, migration, and reconciliation QA.
- [ ] Obtain separate reviewer/verifier evidence before Phase 6 activation.

## Next Steps

1. Phase 6 consumes only the green, versioned API contracts from this phase.
2. Keep attribution capture in `shadow` mode until the Phase 6 role and
