# Phase 1: Customer Source and Workflow Authority

## Overview

Turn the mixed workbook/contract folder into a signed, machine-readable
authority manifest and a workflow coverage matrix. Nothing is deleted or
imported in this phase.

## Requirements

- Functional: classify every sheet/range and contract rule as authoritative
  data, template, example, derived output, or rejected input.
- Functional: map each approved field to an existing authority or a confirmed
  application gap.
- Functional: bind each customer to one effective contract version and policy.
- Non-functional: never commit or log personal contacts, bank details,
  credential data, or raw sensitive workbook rows.

## Architecture

The source manifest is the only input accepted by the later importer:

```text
Customer files
  -> normalized source inventory
  -> human-approved row/rule classifications
  -> versioned cutover manifest
  -> dry-run parser (Phase 3)
```

The manifest records source fingerprint, sheet/range, row natural key,
classification, target authority, transformation, validation status, and
approval metadata. It contains references or redacted values, not copied
secrets.

Approval is bound to the source hashes, authority-manifest hash, target
