# Phase 4: Local Dry Run and Cutover

## Overview

Prove the full backup, cleanup, import, scope-remap, reconciliation, rollback,
and repeatability loop against local data before staging is touched.

## Requirements

- Functional: local backup and isolated restore both succeed.
- Functional: dry-run and apply use the exact approved manifest/source hashes.
- Functional: every role can still log in and execute its permitted workflow.
- Non-functional: all evidence under `qa/`; no sensitive rows/screenshots/logs.
- Non-functional: backups are encrypted outside the repo and live volume, with
  restricted permissions, integrity hash, named custodian, expiry, and secure
  deletion procedure.

## Architecture

Use a disposable clone restored from the local dump for the first destructive
rehearsal. Only after clone QA is green may the canonical local database be
cut over.

```text
local DB -> dump -> isolated restore -> dry-run -> apply -> QA
                                      -> rollback rehearsal
                                      -> replay (committed result, no mutation)
                                      -> approved local cutover
```

## Related Code Files

- Execute: `backend/src/scripts/customer-cutover.ts`
- Read: `docs/customer-data-cutover-runbook.md`
- Create evidence:
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-local_backup-restore.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-local_dry-run.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-local_apply.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-local_reconciliation.md`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-local_role-matrix.md`
  - redacted screenshots under `qa/`

## Implementation Steps

1. Stop local writers, enable read-only maintenance mode, and hold a
   database-enforced advisory lock or equivalent writer fence through
   verification or rollback.
2. Capture schema/migration version, table counts, safe preservation digests,
   source/manifest hashes, and uploads inventory.
3. Create encrypted timestamped DB/uploads backups outside the repository and
   live volume with restrictive permissions, integrity hashes, named custodian,
   retention deadline, and secure deletion procedure. Put only redacted backup
   metadata in `qa/`.
4. Restore into a new isolated local database and run health/migration checks.
5. Run dry-run; resolve every blocked row or unexplained delta.
6. Apply the cutover on the isolated restore.
7. Verify preserved users and mappings, imported master data, operational
   workflow, finance invariants, and scope isolation.
8. Run the importer again and prove a no-op.
9. Rehearse rollback in the explicit order documented by the runbook: keep the
   writer fence, restore DB and uploads to their matched snapshot, verify schema
   and sequences, prove no post-cutover writes occurred, then compare baseline
   counts/digests before reopening writes.
10. Repeat dry-run and apply on the canonical local DB only after clone,
    rollback, and full QA are green.
11. Record exact runtime, row counts, and high-volume behavior for the staging
    maintenance estimate.

## Reconciliation Matrix

| Area | Required proof |
|---|---|
| Users | same IDs/count/credential digest/role/status/deleted state |
| Customer scope | every active customer login resolves only approved customers |
| Driver identity | same user linkage; approved driver master attributes |
| Shipment scope | no orphan/cross-customer links; expected imported counts |
| Master data | source-approved natural keys exactly once |
| Transactions | only approved rows; no sample amounts |
| Finance | opening + activity - settlement = closing; no ledger imbalance |
| User-owned history | byte-for-byte preserved by default; named exclusion separately approved |

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Dump restores successfully to an isolated DB.
- [ ] Dry-run has zero unresolved blockers.
- [ ] Apply and second-apply no-op both pass.
- [ ] Rollback restore reproduces the pre-cutover preservation baseline.
- [ ] Writer fence excludes application jobs, rogue workers, and direct
      cutover-tool writes until acceptance or rollback completes.
- [ ] Full automated gates are green.
- [ ] Authenticated desktop/mobile role matrix is green.
- [ ] No artifact contains credentials or direct personal/financial identifiers.

## QA Gates

Run the full repository gates in `AGENTS.md`, cutover integration tests, and
authenticated E2E for all roles. Test at desktop, tablet, and narrow mobile;
verify action visibility as well as page reachability.

## Risk Assessment

The local dataset is already high-volume. Stream/chunk parsing, DB-bounded
deletes, indexed natural keys, and bounded UI validation are required.
</file>

