# Phase 5: Staging Cutover

## Overview

Perform the approved, rehearsed data cutover on `vantai.tingting.vip` with a
maintenance window, read-only gate, tested rollback, and named operator.

## Requirements

- Functional: staging inventory, backup, restore validation, dry-run, apply,
  reconciliation, and smoke checks use the reviewed tooling/source authority
  from Phase 4 plus a staging-specific target snapshot.
- Functional: all user accounts remain usable and user-owned rows remain
  byte-for-byte unchanged by default.
- Non-functional: no production access or mutation; no secret/PII output;
  rollback time and trigger are fixed before maintenance begins.

## Preconditions

- Blocking customer-service/finance decisions accepted and implemented.
- Local cutover and rollback rehearsal green.
- Source manifest frozen; hashes match the local rehearsal.
- Staging schema/migration matches the tested version.
- Staging-specific target snapshot and disposition manifest approved with exact
  account/customer/driver mappings, active/pending governance rows, expected
  counts, and permitted environment deltas.
- Approval is bound to source/manifest hashes, staging fingerprint, schema
  migration, importer commit/build digest, and disposition-manifest hash.
- Explicit user approval for the staging maintenance window and mutation.
- Named cutover owner, verifier, rollback owner, and communication channel.
- Sufficient disk capacity for DB/uploads backups and isolated restore.
- Encrypted backup destination outside the repository/live volume, permissions,
  integrity verification, custodian, retention/expiry, and secure deletion are
  approved; `qa/` will contain only redacted metadata.

## Related Code Files

- Execute only reviewed commands from `docs/customer-data-cutover-runbook.md`.
- Use current deployment context from `Makefile` and
  `deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml`, but discover live container/volume/path
  names read-only; do not trust stale `vantai`/`nepocorp` labels.
- Create evidence:
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-staging_preflight.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-staging_backup-restore.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-staging_dry-run.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-staging_apply.log`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-staging_reconciliation.md`
  - `qa/<date>_customer-cutover-staging_smoke.md`

## Implementation Steps

1. Read-only inventory the actual staging host, compose project, containers,
   database, volume mounts, uploads, schema version, and free space.
2. Freeze a staging-specific inventory and mapping/disposition snapshot, then
   compare counts/digests with reviewed expectations. Any unmapped/newly changed
   row after approval forces a new dry run and approval.
3. Reject the cutover if production endpoints/volumes are detected or the
   environment identity is ambiguous.
4. Enable maintenance/read-only mode, drain jobs/writers, and acquire a
   database-enforced advisory lock or equivalent writer fence held through
   acceptance or rollback.
5. Create encrypted DB/uploads backups outside the repo/live volume with
   restrictive permissions and integrity hashes.
6. Restore the dump to an isolated database and run schema plus representative
   account/finance checks.
7. Run dry-run with the frozen manifest and source hashes.
8. Obtain final immutable go/no-go approval bound to all source, target, schema,
   importer-build, and disposition fingerprints.
9. Apply the transactional cutover. Do not deploy unrelated code in the same
   maintenance action.
10. Run automated reconciliation and independent verification.
11. Run role-specific authenticated smoke tests, including customer scope and
    financial totals, at desktop and mobile widths.
12. Roll back immediately on any identity mismatch, stale FK/semantic
    reference, financial imbalance, cross-customer visibility, health failure,
    unexplained delta, or writer-fence breach. Restore the matched DB/uploads
    snapshot, then verify schema, sequences, and absence of post-cutover writes.
13. Re-enable jobs/writes only after green verification; monitor error logs and
    key counts for the agreed window.

## Go/No-Go Gates

| Gate | No-go condition |
|---|---|
| Environment identity | host/DB/volume cannot be proven staging-only |
| Backup | dump or uploads backup missing/unreadable |
| Restore | isolated restore fails any check |
| Identity | any preserved account/mapping mismatch |
| Source | manifest/source hash differs from rehearsal |
| Target snapshot | mapping, disposition, count, pending row, or build fingerprint changed |
| Finance | any unexplained balance or document delta |
| Scope | any customer sees another customer |
| Rollback | cannot meet the rehearsed recovery window |

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Staging-only target proven.
- [ ] Backup and isolated restore verified.
- [ ] Dry-run matches the staging-specific approved snapshot and permitted deltas.
- [ ] Apply commits once; replay returns the committed result with unchanged
      PKs, timestamps, sequences, links, and counts.
- [ ] All account, scope, workflow, and finance reconciliations pass.
- [ ] Rollback remains available through the monitoring window.
- [ ] Complete redacted evidence exists under `qa/`.

## Risk Assessment

This is destructive staging work. Approval for planning or deployment is not
approval for the cutover; a separate explicit go/no-go is mandatory.
</file>

