  - never evaluates formula cells and persists only redacted analysis results;
  - classifies rows as `ACCEPTED`, `BLOCKED`, `TEMPLATE`, or `EXAMPLE` while blocking ambiguous authorities, duplicate natural keys, inactive/deleted canonical records, and conflicting driver/trailer assignments;
  - applies accepted sites, ports, drivers, trucks, and trailers atomically without creating login accounts;
  - deduplicates analysis by source hash and parser version and enforces keyed, versioned apply/reject commands;
  - schedules abandoned `ANALYZED` sources for durable deletion after seven days;
  - restores an expired source only after an authorized Admin re-uploads the exact same hash;
  - clears terminal source ownership and enqueues durable final deletion in the same transaction, so an object-store outage cannot turn a committed apply/reject into an HTTP 500;
  - checks the actor's current Admin authority before every analyze/apply/reject replay;
  - exposes rejection actor, event time, and reason from the durable idempotency record without exposing storage keys.
- `backend/src/routes/config/master-data-import.routes.ts`
