# Phase 5: e-POD review and shipment closure

## Context Links

- [Plan](./plan.md)
- `backend/src/routes/upload.ts`
- `backend/src/services/trip-status-machine.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/milestone.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/clerk-shipment-scope.service.ts`
- `frontend/src/pages/ShipmentDetailPage.tsx`

## Overview

Review the immutable e-POD submissions created in Phase 4 with a first-winner operational decision. Accepted evidence locks the completed trip; a transactional aggregate advances the shipment to `DELIVERED` and then `CLOSED` only when every required fulfillment satisfies the approved rules.

## Requirements

### Functional

- Submitted versions are immutable. Rejection records reason and sends the driver back to the Phase 4 superseding-version flow; files from prior versions remain auditable.
- Only the owning driver uploads/submits. Scoped CLERK and MANAGER/ADMIN may review. ACCOUNTANT and CUSTOMER are read-only through explicitly allowed DTOs.
- First valid approval wins under row lock/expected version; self-review rules are unnecessary because the submitter is DRIVER, but actor separation is still audited.
- Approval rechecks trip ownership, status `COMPLETED`, required file types, required fulfillment/disposition state, and scope, then invokes the canonical transition to `LOCKED`.
- Aggregate rules:
  - no empty-set closure;
  - every required fulfillment has one linked trip;
  - all required trips are `COMPLETED|LOCKED` before shipment `DELIVERED`;
  - all required trips are `LOCKED` with accepted e-POD before shipment `CLOSED`;
  - a canceled fulfillment remains required until persisted disposition is either `REPLACED` with a valid required replacement or `NOT_REQUIRED` approved by MANAGER/ADMIN with actor, reason, and time;
  - recompute locks the shipment and relevant fulfillment/disposition rows so cancel, replace, waive, approve, and close cannot race.

### Non-functional

- MIME/signature/size checks, private storage, scoped download, retention, and no raw storage keys in browser DTOs.
- Review UI supports zoom/download, missing/rejected state, keyboard focus restoration, and 44px controls on mobile.
- Aggregate updates and status history occur in the same transaction as trip lock.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  D[Driver] --> S[e-POD submission vN]
  S --> R{CUS or Dispatcher review}
  R -->|reject| N[New version required]
  R -->|approve| L[Trip COMPLETED to LOCKED]
  L --> A[Recompute shipment aggregate]
  A -->|all completed| V[Shipment DELIVERED]
  A -->|all locked and POD accepted| C[Shipment CLOSED]
```

## File Inventory

| Action | File | Purpose | Test impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| Modify | `backend/src/services/trip-pod.service.ts` | Review, supersession, download policy, aggregate integration | New tests |
| Modify | `backend/src/services/trip-status-machine.service.ts` | Evidence-approved lock command | Trip/finance |
| Modify | `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts` | Transactional aggregate closure | Shipment tests |
| Modify | `backend/src/services/milestone.service.ts` | Derived delivery/closure milestones | Milestone tests |
| Modify | `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts` | Scoped review/read endpoints | Shipment RBAC |
| Modify | `shared/src/schemas/index.ts` | POD/review contracts | Shared tests |
| Create | `frontend/src/components/shipment/TripPodReviewPanel.tsx` | CUS/dispatcher review | Frontend/a11y |
| Create | `backend/src/tests/trip-pod-workflow.test.ts` | Version/review/closure/races | Backend |

## Exact Interface Checklist

- [x] `reviewPod` requires actor, expected version, and idempotency key; it consumes the Phase 4 submission contract rather than redefining it.
- [x] POD approval performs first-winner approval, canonical lock, and aggregate recompute atomically.
- [x] Shipment completion is derived from required fulfillment/disposition/trip/POD facts.
- [x] Existing generic `tripPhotos` remain container/seal/other evidence and cannot satisfy POD requirements.
- [x] Existing billing/ledger postings are not duplicated at POD approval or shipment close.

## Implementation Steps

1. Write failing tests for missing evidence, wrong actor, version replacement, concurrent review, cancellation/replacement, and aggregate closure.
2. Extend the Phase 4 POD service with scoped review, rejection, supersession reads, and download policy.
3. Add scoped CUS/dispatcher review queue and detail panel.
4. Implement atomic approval -> trip lock -> shipment aggregate transitions/history/milestones.
5. Implement persisted replacement/`NOT_REQUIRED` disposition commands and include unresolved cancellations in the required aggregate set.
6. Verify reopen/reject/cancel paths use governed reversals or replacement versions rather than overwriting accepted evidence.

## Test Scenario Matrix

| Priority | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| P0 | Missing signed delivery note or yard receipt | Submit/complete blocked |
| P0 | Two reviewers approve | First wins; second receives conflict |
| P0 | One of four FCL tasks not locked | Shipment not CLOSED |
| P0 | All four locked with accepted POD | One CLOSED transition/history row |
| P0 | LCL task locked with accepted POD | Shipment CLOSED |
| P0 | Canceled task without replacement/approval | Closure blocked |
| P0 | Cancel races with POD approval/aggregate close | Serialized result; unresolved cancellation cannot disappear from required set |
| P1 | Rejected submission replaced | Old version immutable; new reviewable |
| P1 | ACCOUNTANT review call | 403; read remains allowed |
| P1 | Unsupported file/MIME | Rejected before persistence |

## QA and Regression Gate

- Focused upload/authz/POD/trip/shipment/milestone tests.
- Full lint, typechecks, backend/frontend tests, build, and E2E.
- Manual driver mobile and CUS/dispatcher desktop/tablet/mobile evidence review; verify no overflow and keyboard access.

## Success Criteria

- [x] e-POD has dedicated semantics, immutable versions, and required file types.
- [x] Approval permissions match the locked role matrix and live CLERK scope.
- [x] Trip lock and shipment closure are atomic, idempotent, and auditable.
- [x] Partial, rejected, canceled, and replacement cases cannot falsely close a shipment.
- [x] No duplicate AR/ledger posting occurs during review or close.

## Risks, Security, and Rollback

Risks: malicious uploads, evidence replacement, cross-customer access, and false aggregate completion. Use private storage, content validation, immutable versions, signed/scoped delivery, row locks, and database-backed predicates. Pre-release rollback is a forward correction or dev/staging reset; retained test uploads must be cleaned through the storage service.

## Next Steps

Phase 6 consumes only locked, accepted fulfillments for Debit Note export and performs complete rollout QA.
