# Consolidated Red-Team Review — Accountant Workflow Plan

## Verdict after adjudication

**PASS FOR PLANNING; IMPLEMENTATION REMAINS GATED.** All evidence-backed findings
were incorporated or explicitly deferred. Phase 1 may reconcile contracts and
decisions. Later slices start only after their named upstream contract and true
delta decision are closed.

This consolidation adjudicates the assumption-destroyer, failure-mode,
security-adversary, and scope/complexity reports in this directory. The review
covered `plan.md`, all phase files, both research reports, the upstream finance
and dispatch plans, and the cited repository authorities. It did not run product
tests because this is a plan-document review.

## Dispositions

| ID | Severity | Finding and evidence | Disposition |
|---|---|---|---|
| RT-01 | Critical | Trip financial posting already credits carrier AP (`backend/src/services/ledger.service.ts:286-297`), while `PAYMENT_STATEMENT` is presentation-only (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:825-830`). | **Accepted.** `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST` remains the sole AP obligation; carrier confirmation posts no second credit. |
| RT-02 | Critical | Billing lines lack `financialPostingId` and use operational source version despite the financial-provenance warning (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:754-780,1141-1161`). | **Accepted.** Upstream owner must persist posting ID plus immutable version/checksum and enforce an active-authority claim before this plan consumes it. |
| RT-03 | High | Billing contracts store inclusive amounts without durable VAT rate/base/tax/treatment (`shared/src/schemas/index.ts:384-421`; `backend/src/db/schema.ts:874-949,1141-1161`). | **Accepted.** Finance/Legal decision and upstream additive snapshot are required; legacy decomposition is `UNKNOWN`, never guessed. |
| RT-04 | Critical | Historical receivable/aging paths ignore or inconsistently apply `asOf` and use wall time (`backend/src/services/aging.service.ts:84,136-150,275-280,344-356`; `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:144-209,517-523`). | **Accepted.** One Vietnam end-exclusive cutoff must govern every source, cache, API, and export with historical checksum tests. |
| RT-05 | High | Statement JSON passes a date range while export drops it (`backend/src/routes/financial/ledger.routes.ts:34-49`). | **Accepted.** Upstream repair uses one strict scoped query and sentinel before/inside/after tests. |
| RT-06 | High | The first draft reopened already-approved cadence, governance, attribution, and lock rules (`docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md:63-70,179-186,228-253`). | **Accepted.** These rules are inherited; only workbook deltas remain decisions. |
| RT-07 | Critical | Current save accepts caller-authored ad-hoc/base/override/excluded money and later posts its AR delta (`shared/src/schemas/index.ts:384-417`; `backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts:158-185,1474-1482`). | **Accepted.** Normal writes become source/version references; authoritative amounts are server-derived and hostile payloads are tested. |
| RT-08 | High | Role-only checks do not define unit/customer row scope for direct IDs and exports (`backend/src/middleware/casbin.ts:19-28`; `backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts:61-75,197-243`). | **Accepted.** Role × action × field × row-scope is required everywhere, including search, counts, cache, and exports. |
| RT-09 | High | Current refunds cannot reverse applied allocations (`backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:1004-1012,1091-1127`). | **Deferred.** This plan supports unapplied-cash refunds only and exposes applied-refund/deallocation as unsupported pending a separate governed plan. |
| RT-10 | High | Manual reminder has no route/schema/caller and would collide with scheduler-only dedupe/effects (`backend/src/index.ts:83-100`; `backend/src/services/receivable-reminder.service.ts:167-180,1103-1165`). | **Deferred.** MVP shows scheduled history only; manual send needs a dedicated side-effecting contract and cannot alter approved cadence. |
| RT-11 | High | P&L/dashboard assemble independent queries/caches, so a returned timestamp cannot prove one watermark (`backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts:29-60,81-91,163-215`; `backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts:20-21,39-115`). | **Accepted.** Phase 1 selects repeatable-read or an immutable report run; exports retain its ID/checksum. |
| RT-12 | Critical | The first draft duplicated active finance/dispatch ownership across shared billing, AR/AP, reports, navigation, E2E, and rollout. | **Accepted.** A single-owner contract matrix makes this a bounded accountant-delta plan; upstream gaps return to their owning plans. |
| RT-13 | High | A new `/accounting` route could duplicate the selected `/debt` home and existing finance-first navigation (`frontend/src/lib/routes.ts:129-136`; `frontend/src/App.tsx:223-229,291-295`). | **Superseded by explicit user decision.** `/accounting` is now the dedicated pre-release Accountant home, but must remain a thin composition over existing authoritative drill-downs. No compatibility redirect is required. |
| RT-14 | High | The transport register lacked endpoint/schema/service/client/consumer definitions; existing generation/list inputs cannot represent it (`shared/src/schemas/index.ts:401-420`; `backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts:61-70`). | **Accepted.** Phase 2 now names the two routes, strict schemas/DTOs, service functions, client methods, query key, token/fingerprint, and initial consumer. |
| RT-15 | High | Profitability shared schema uses a date range while live route/service/client use month/year (`shared/src/schemas/customer-service-finance.ts:85-94`; `backend/src/routes/financial/reports.routes.ts:49-68`; `backend/src/services/profitability.service.ts:178-192`). | **Accepted.** The upstream owner reconciles one canonical contract; this plan maps workbook fields onto it and creates no second report authority. |

## Whole-plan consistency sweep

- **Authority:** one AR instrument, one existing carrier AP post, one settlement
  authority, one profitability authority, and no workbook-shaped ledger.
- **Ownership:** dispatch owns locked-source billing eligibility; customer-service
  finance owns financial provenance, finance authorities, reporting, and role
  workspace; this plan owns only workbook disposition, adapters, presentation,
  and delta QA.
- **Dates:** service, issue, due, payment, and reporting dates remain distinct;
  historical output carries one explicit cutoff and report snapshot/run.
- **Security:** money is server-derived; field and row projection occur after a
  canonical cache; direct IDs and exports use the same scope.
- **Scope:** `/accounting` is composition-only; no manual reminder send,
  applied-allocation refund, inferred VAT/tax, sample-data import, deployment,
  or production cutover.

No accepted finding remains contradictory. Open business decisions are named
gates with safe defaults, not implied implementation freedom.
