# Phase 2: Transport register adapter delta

## Context Links

- [Phase 1](./phase-01-authority-and-requirement-contract.md)
- Revised workbook: `TH VẬN TẢI!A1:AG66`
- Dispatch completion authority: `plans/260801-0942-end-to-end-dispatch-workflow/`

## Overview

Compose the transport register and governed bulk confirmation flow from accepted
trip financial postings. Produce customer Debit Note drafts or carrier/vendor
payment statements without directly mutating balances from UI selection or
double-posting carrier AP.

## Requirements

- Functional:
  - Server-side date, customer, carrier/owner, T-period, status, search, sort,
    and bounded pagination filters.
  - Row evidence: service/confirmation date, customer, factory, route,
    container type/direction/weight/CBM, bill/book, container, carrier, plate,
    AR/AP components, `financialPostingId`, immutable posting version/checksum,
    and posting readiness reason; never use operational `trip.version` as
    financial provenance.
  - Independent customer and carrier selection; select-all applies only to the
    current server filter and reports excluded/ineligible rows.
  - Confirmation preview freezes source/version, totals, approved VAT treatment,
    actor, period, and document template before maker/checker governance.
  - Customer branch extends the current Debit Note draft/issue path. Carrier
    confirmation freezes a presentation statement over the AP already posted by
    `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST`; it creates no second ledger credit.
  - Write requests contain source identities/versions and governed adjustment
    references only. The server reloads sources and derives amounts inside the
    approval transaction; caller-authored ad-hoc/base/override/excluded money is rejected.
  - Persist immutable VAT decomposition only after Phase 1 approves its model:
    rate authority/effective date, inclusive/exclusive basis, taxable base, tax,
    zero/exempt/unknown semantics, VND residual allocation, treatment version,
    and correction/reversal behavior. Legacy documents remain `UNKNOWN`.
  - Existing PDF/XLSX exports use the same frozen snapshot shown in preview.
- Non-functional:
  - Idempotent requests and optimistic version checks; first approved writer wins.
  - No N+1 query per row; page limits and response budgets are explicit.
  - A DB-enforced claim prevents one ACTIVE `financialPostingId`/version from
    contributing to multiple active obligations of the same authority.

## Architecture

```text
locked trip + active financial posting
  -> eligible transport projection
  -> selected source/version snapshot
  -> governed Debit Note (CUSTOMER) -> issue/approve posts exactly one AR obligation
  -> payment statement (CARRIER/VENDOR) -> confirms existing AP; posts no AP
```

The upstream finance/dispatch owners must first deliver the additive persistence
for `financialPostingId`, immutable version/checksum, active-authority claim, and
approved VAT snapshot. This phase consumes those contracts through one bounded
adapter; it does not reopen their schema or posting behavior.

Proposed delta contract, finalized in Phase 1 before coding:

- `GET /api/financial/billing-documents/transport-register` using
  `accountingTransportRegisterQuerySchema`; stable `(serviceDate,id)` cursor,
  strict filter fingerprint, bounded page, eligibility-reason enum, and
  `AccountingTransportRegisterResponse`.
- `POST /api/financial/billing-documents/transport-register/preview` using
  source posting IDs/versions plus filter fingerprint; returns an immutable
  preview token/checksum and per-row rejection results.
- Existing Debit Note generation/governance consumes the preview token.
  Carrier confirmation consumes the same snapshot to create presentation only.
- Service symbols: `listAccountingTransportRows()` and
  `previewAccountingTransportSelection()`; frontend symbols:
  `getAccountingTransportRegister()`, `previewAccountingTransportSelection()`,
  one query-key factory, and the existing billing component as consumer.

## Related Code Files

- Consume/verify only: upstream `tripFinancialPostings`, billing assembly,
  governance, overlap guard, AP ledger projection, VAT snapshot, and migrations.
- Create after upstream ownership closes:
  `backend/src/services/accounting-transport-register.service.ts` and its
  focused test; do not duplicate source eligibility or money calculation.
- Modify after ownership handoff: `shared/src/schemas/customer-service-finance.ts`
  for the four exact symbols above and
  `backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts` for the two routes.
- Modify: the existing customer-service finance client/query-key module and
  `BillingDocumentBuilder.tsx` as the only initial UI consumer.
- Delta tests: DTO parsing, cursor/filter fingerprint, selection drift,
  eligibility reasons, row scope, statement-no-AP, and preview/export checksum.

## Implementation Steps

1. Write failing tests for eligibility, financial-posting drift/supersede/reverse,
   mixed-entity selection, duplicate retries, concurrent approval, VAT rounding,
   and reversal. Add hostile API cases for forged amounts, overrides, exclusions,
   arbitrary ad-hoc rows, duplicate sources, and cross-scope direct IDs.
2. Verify the upstream provenance/VAT/claim contract and fail this phase if any
   dependency remains operational-version-based or caller-money-authoritative.
3. Add only the bounded transport adapter over upstream active-posting billing
   eligibility; return explicit reasons instead of duplicating eligibility rules.
4. Implement separate customer and carrier confirmation previews with approved
   VAT treatment and maker/checker governance. Prove carrier statement save and
   confirmation do not create another AP ledger entry.
5. Bind exports to the frozen preview/issued version; never requery live rows
   during historical re-export.
6. Add reconciliation diagnostics: selected total = document source total =
   posted obligation, with explicit corrections through adjustment/reversal.

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Filters and current-page/select-all behavior are deterministic at volume.
- [ ] Stale, already-claimed, unlocked, missing-evidence, and mixed-entity rows cannot post.
- [ ] Customer confirmation creates at most one governed AR obligation; carrier
  confirmation reconciles the existing AP and creates no second credit.
- [ ] Every financial line is linked to an ACTIVE `financialPostingId` and
  immutable posting version/checksum; stale/superseded/reversed sources fail safely.
- [ ] Callers cannot manufacture or suppress debt through line amounts,
  overrides, exclusions, or ad-hoc rows.
- [ ] Preview, PDF, XLSX, document, and ledger totals reconcile exactly.
- [ ] Accountant can confirm finance readiness but cannot change dispatch/e-POD state.
- [ ] The exact endpoint/schema/service/client/consumer inventory above exists;
  no second source-eligibility or billing-calculation implementation is added.

## Risk Assessment

Bulk confirmation has high financial blast radius. Mitigate with dry preview,
source/version locks, idempotency, maker/checker, immutable issue snapshots, and
reversal—not delete/edit—correction. Roll back by disabling the new projection
and actions while retaining governed documents and ledger history.
