# Phase 3: Debt and collections presentation delta

## Context Links

- [Phase 2](./phase-02-transport-reconciliation-and-posting-readiness.md)
- Revised workbook: `BÁO CÁO CÔNG NỢ THEO THÁNG!A1:Q25`,
  `BÁO CÁO TÌNH TRẠNG KH!A2:I21`

## Overview

Extend current AR/AP, receipt/allocation, aging, and reminder authorities into
the workbook-required monthly debt and customer-quality projections.

## Requirements

- Functional:
  - AR/AP rows include entity identity/tax code, account owner, source/issue
    date, applied term, original/processing due date, document references,
    invoiced amount, recoverable chi hộ, paid amount, balance, and value date.
  - Derive early, on-time, partial, at-risk, overdue, and late-paid states from
    persisted obligation and receipt/allocation timestamps; never store a
    report-only status that can drift.
  - Preserve customer, vendor, and carrier projections; do not merge identities
    by similar names or tax codes without the existing canonical linkage.
  - Show aging counts, amounts, ratios, top on-time, and top overdue entities for
    one required `asOf` business-date end-exclusive cutoff in
    `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh` and official bucket definitions.
  - Show read-only scheduled-reminder history. Manual preview/send is deferred
    until a dedicated route/schema/service/UI contract defines selection,
    recipient, collision, checksum, idempotency, row scope, and durable effects.
  - Partial/unapplied/refunded payments and disputes stay explicit. This phase
    supports refunds only from existing unapplied cash; applied-allocation
    refund/deallocation is explicitly deferred and shown as unsupported.
- Non-functional:
  - Database-bounded search/pagination and deterministic export ordering.
  - Same `asOf` and due-date authority across list, detail, dashboard, reminder,
    and XLSX export.
  - Preserve upstream scheduled-reminder dedupe, retries, terminal escalation,
    and audit evidence; do not change its approved cadence in this plan.

## Architecture

`issued obligation -> customer/carrier/vendor authority -> receipt/allocation or
payment ledger -> outstanding snapshot -> due-state/aging projection -> reminder`.

Consume the customer-service finance plan's receivable, AP-aging, payment,
reminder-history, and business-calendar contracts. The historical `asOf` repair
is an upstream authority prerequisite, not a second accountant implementation.
The UI must not recompute balances or aging.

## Related Code Files

- Upstream owner modifies: receivable authority, aging/AP aging, payment
  allocation, scheduler, and report/payment routes. This plan verifies the
  accepted versioned outputs and adds no competing money or reminder service.
- Upstream owner must include `backend/src/routes/financial/ledger.routes.ts`
  and statement export in the shared strict range/`asOf` repair.
- Modify: `frontend/src/pages/DebtListPage.tsx`, `DebtDetailPage.tsx`,
  `PayableListPage.tsx`, `PayableDetailPage.tsx`, and finance API/hooks only where
  workbook fields are absent from the upstream projection.
- Delta tests: workbook column/label mapping, historical `asOf` propagation,
  bounded statement export, row scope, scheduled-history display, and mobile cards.

## Implementation Steps

1. Require the upstream historical repair to validate one end-exclusive `asOf`
   through document issue, approved adjustments, allocation/value date,
   unapplied refunds/reversals, ledger filtering, cache keys, API metadata, and export.
2. Verify status cases for issue, due, payment, allocation, unapplied refund,
   dispute, same-day cutoff, post-cutoff events, month boundary, cache, and
   identical historical re-export checksum.
3. Map the workbook columns and aging/customer-quality labels onto the upstream
   obligation projection; expose missing identity/data state without new balances.
4. Verify the statement screen and export use one strict range/`asOf` schema,
   row scope, metadata, and sentinel transactions before/inside/after the range.
5. Add scheduled-reminder delivery history only. Return a clear unsupported
   result for manual send and applied-allocation refund/deallocation.

## Success Criteria

- [ ] AR/AP list, detail, export, and reminder totals reconcile to canonical balances.
- [ ] All supported payment states behave correctly for partial, unapplied, refunded,
  disputed, early, on-time, overdue, and late-paid cases.
- [ ] Applied-allocation refunds and manual reminder sends cannot be falsely
  recorded as supported; UI/API expose their explicit deferred status.
- [ ] Aging totals and ratios reconcile; the 61–90 bucket is not silently lost
  because the workbook omits it in one label set.
- [ ] Scheduled reminder history retains auditable delivery state without
  changing the approved cadence or introducing a phantom manual-send contract.
- [ ] UI and XLSX exclude sentinel transactions before/after the selected range
  and reproduce the same historical checksum.
- [ ] No hardcoded Gmail dependency or manual actual-payment-date override exists.

## Risk Assessment

Largest risks are double-counting issued Debit Notes versus trip debt and using
current time inconsistently. Reuse the curated receivable authority, one
business clock, and one `asOf`. Corrections use allocations/refunds/reversals;
never overwrite historical ledger rows.
</file>

