# Phase 4: Profitability workbook mapping delta

## Context Links

- Revised workbook: `BC HÀNG NGÀY!A1:AC25`, `BC LÃI LỖ!A1:N28`, `LN THÁNG!A1:D45`
- `backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts`
- `backend/src/services/profitability.service.ts`

## Overview

Build daily trip-margin and monthly financial read models that reconcile to the
accepted posting/version and expense authorities. Add unavailable/partial state
for categories that lack an approved source instead of inventing amounts.

## Requirements

- Functional:
  - Daily detail separates external and own-fleet trips and exposes customer,
    route, equipment, revenue, direct costs, profit, margin, source version, and
    reconciliation status.
  - Revised own-fleet variable costs remain distinct: trip pay, fuel, Lạch
    Huyện, toll/VETC, tire/other operating cost; only approved, non-overlapping
    sources may populate each bucket.
  - Monthly KPIs: revenue, reportable trips, total cost, profit, margin, prior-
    period change, trend series, cost mix, due and overdue summaries.
  - Monthly taxonomy separates approved revenue, vendor, fixed, variable, and
    finance-cost sources; pre-tax, tax, and after-tax output is shown only when
    authoritative tax postings exist.
  - Preserve own/external/unassigned and missing-attribution buckets.
  - Apply the Phase 1 field matrix; workbook Admin-only measures are redacted
    before serialization when the viewer lacks the capability.
- Non-functional:
  - Full `vi-VN` digits; consistent timezone, period, definition version, and `asOf`.
  - Paginated/drillable database queries; no browser-derived financial truth.
  - Summary, grouped rows, detail, dashboard, and export reconcile within the
    concrete Phase 1 consistency contract: one repeatable-read snapshot or one
    persisted immutable report-run ID/watermark/checksum.
  - Cache a canonical internal model and apply capability/row-scope projection
    after retrieval without mutating cached objects; include policy version in
    invalidation. Never cache a role-redacted payload under a shared period key.

## Architecture

`tripFinancialPostings + profitabilitySnapshots + approved expenses + AR/AP
summaries -> versioned reporting projection -> daily/monthly API -> UI/export`.

Map workbook fields onto the upstream canonical P&L/profitability authority. Do
not introduce a second P&L or allocate shared overhead/tax without an approved
method. Before presentation work, reconcile the existing public-contract split:
the shared date-range query versus the mounted month/year route/client. The
upstream owner chooses one canonical query model, response type, compatibility
policy, and caller migration. This plan consumes that result.

## Related Code Files

- Upstream owner modifies: P&L/profitability/reporting/dashboard services,
  `reports.routes.ts`, and the exact shared schema/client symbols needed to make
  `/reports/profitability` one contract. No parallel monthly-report endpoint.
- Modify: `frontend/src/pages/FinancePage.tsx`, `ProfitPage.tsx`,
  `frontend/src/components/finance/ProfitabilityReportPanel.tsx`, and dashboard
  finance components only for workbook presentation deltas.
- Reuse: `shared/src/calculations/tripTotals.ts`, `round.ts`; do not reimplement in UI.
- Tests: P&L invariants, profitability attribution/pagination, executive RBAC,
  official reporting periods, dashboard widgets, and `e2e/test_05_profit.py`.

## Implementation Steps

1. Require an upstream contract report naming the canonical profitability
   endpoint, query schema, response DTO, compatibility/retirement policy,
   service function, client method, query key, and every caller. Define daily
   detail as the existing profitability drill-down, not a second authority.
2. Write reconciliation tests for own/external trips, commissions, VAT, revised
   variable-cost buckets, expenses, missing sources, and locked corrections.
3. Publish a versioned metric/category registry mapping every workbook row to
   one current source, approved future source, or unavailable state.
4. Extend daily report presentation from the canonical financial posting snapshot;
   add server-side filters and reconciliation diagnostics.
5. Implement the accepted upstream reporting consistency mechanism across all
   component queries; exports carry the same snapshot/run ID and checksum.
6. Map monthly workbook KPI/trend/cost-mix fields onto the canonical response.
7. Add explicit tax/pre-tax/after-tax availability; never infer tax payable
   from selected Debit Note VAT or estimate corporate income tax.
8. Project capability and row-scope fields after canonical-cache retrieval.
   Test Admin→Accountant and Accountant→Admin cold/warm order, export/search
   parity, policy-version invalidation, and a correction committed mid-assembly.

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Daily details sum to monthly source totals for the same period/version.
- [ ] Each cost category is source-linked once; no trip/expense double count.
- [ ] Own, external, unassigned, missing-attribution, and unavailable states are visible.
- [ ] Tax and after-tax fields never present estimates as booked actuals.
- [ ] Unauthorized roles cannot receive restricted profit, commission, or margin fields.
- [ ] KPI/trend/cost-mix values use full digits and reconcile to drill-downs.
- [ ] Shared schema, mounted route, service, client, and query key use one
  documented profitability contract; no second monthly authority exists.
- [ ] A concurrent correction/payment/refund yields a wholly-before or wholly-
  after report snapshot, never a mixed response; re-export preserves its checksum.

## Risk Assessment

The workbook mixes management P&L and statutory tax concepts. Keep a versioned
management-report definition and explicit tax authority boundary. Rollback by
removing additive read projections/capabilities; immutable postings and snapshots remain.
