# Phase 1: Atomic Contract, Enum, and Gate Migration

## Overview

Remove `TripStatus.LOCKED` from the shared contract, the Postgres
`trip_status` enum, the governance manifest, and the central state machine —
and **move the photo / zero-revenue / e-POD gates** that today live in the
`COMPLETED → LOCKED` branch into the `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` branch. This
phase is load-bearing and **must ship atomically** with the billing/P&L/
closure rewrites it implies (listed below), because multiple services
hard-compare `status === 'LOCKED'` and break the instant the enum value is
gone.

Done == the app compiles, the dev DB accepts the four-value enum, the
completion transition carries the migrated gates, and every downstream
`=== 'LOCKED'` site is repointed at `COMPLETED` in the same PR.

## Requirements

- **Functional**
  - `TripStatus` has exactly four members: `CREATED`, `IN_TRANSIT`,
    `COMPLETED`, `CANCELED`.
  - The `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` transition carries the gates that used to
    live on `→ LOCKED`: the e-POD-acceptance binding (`podApprovalContext`),
    the photo-evidence gate (≥1 photo baseline; CONTAINER + SEAL when
    `cargoTypes.requiresPhotos`), the zero-revenue soft guard, and the
    "ADMIN/MANAGER/CLERK-with-podApprovalContext only" RBAC check.
  - The permissive driver-Hoàn Thành path (the old
    `targetStatus === COMPLETED` branch at lines 133-151 that allowed
    completion without photos, plus its `POST /trips/:id/complete` route at
    `routes/trips.ts:451`) is **removed** — the PRD's POD gate requires
    acceptance before completion. The sole completion path is the migrated
    e-POD acceptance.
  - The e-POD ACCEPT path in `shipment.service.ts:1156` is repointed from
    `transitionTripStatus(..., TripStatus.LOCKED, ...)` to
    `transitionTripStatus(..., TripStatus.COMPLETED, ...)`, carrying the
    same `podApprovalContext`.
  - The `COMPLETED → LOCKED` branch (lines 156-240) is deleted entirely.
  - `BILLABLE_TRIP_STATUSES = [TripStatus.COMPLETED]`.
  - Postgres `trip_status` enum no longer contains `LOCKED`.
  - `governance/locked-entity-manifest.ts` TRIP `terminalStates` =
    `['COMPLETED','CANCELED']`.
  - `trips.carrier_type` has a CHECK constraint `IN ('OWN','EXTERNAL')`.
  - **(Validation + user architectural preference)** `trips.external_carrier_id`
    (locked FK → `customers.id`) is migrated to two **plain columns with no
    DB FK, both nullable**: `external_entity_id integer` (default null) +
    `external_entity_type varchar(20)` (default null). Both null for `OWN`
    trips (the majority); populated only when `carrier_type = EXTERNAL`. The
    pair is a soft pointer resolved by an app-layer helper, not by the DB —
    per the project convention that cross-entity refs are app-layer concerns
    (bank-grade microservices use no FKs at all). Backfill existing EXTERNAL
    rows as `('CUSTOMER', external_carrier_id)`, then drop
    `external_carrier_id` and its FK.
  - Every downstream `=== 'LOCKED'` / `!== 'LOCKED'` site (closure
    predicate, billing eligibility, adjustment governance, transport
    register, P&L) is repointed at `COMPLETED` in this same PR.
- **Non-functional**
  - Migration is forward-only; the enum value is dropped via the 4-step
    safe rewrite (see Implementation Steps).
  - All TypeScript that pattern-matched `LOCKED` is resolved (no `// TODO`
    markers left in the changed surface).

## Architecture

The original draft of this phase assumed `postTripLock` fires at LOCKED-time
and would need to "move". That was **inverted**. Verified against HEAD
(`trip-status-machine.service.ts:377-389`): `LedgerService.postTripLock`
already fires inside the `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` handler, alongside the
financial-posting row creation. So the posting anchor is correct; what is
wrong is the **gate placement**:

- Today, completion (`IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED`, lines 133-151) is
  deliberately permissive — "completion is permissive, photos can be added
  later". The photo gate, zero-rev gate, e-POD binding, and the
  ADMIN/MANAGER/CLERK RBAC check all live in the **separate**
  `COMPLETED → LOCKED` branch (lines 156-240), driven by `POST /trips/:id/lock`
  or by the e-POD ACCEPT path in `shipment.service.ts:1156`.
- Under the PRD's "drop LOCKED" model, those gates must migrate one hop
  earlier: into the `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` handler. The e-POD ACCEPT path
  still exists; it just targets `COMPLETED` instead of `LOCKED`. The
  permissive driver path is removed.

Data flow after migration: driver/Ops submit e-POD → accountant/CUS accepts
→ `transitionTripStatus(tripId, COMPLETED, ..., { podApprovalContext })` →
the migrated gates run (photo/zero-rev/e-POD checks) → on pass, the
financial posting + `postTripCompletion` (renamed from `postTripLock`) fire
inside the same `tx` → the trip is now `COMPLETED` (terminal). There is no
second hop.

**Atomicity — why this phase owns downstream repoints.** Five services
hard-compare `=== 'LOCKED'`:

| File | Line | Today | After Phase 1 |
|---|---|---|---|
| `shipment.service.ts` | 987 | `COMPLETED \|\| LOCKED` | `COMPLETED` |
| `shipment.service.ts` | 1011 | `allLockedAndAccepted` (requires LOCKED) | `allCompletedAndAccepted` |
| `debit-note-lifecycle.service.ts` | 132 | `!== 'LOCKED'` | `!== 'COMPLETED'` |
| `billingDocument.service.ts` | 1605-06 | `!== 'LOCKED'` | `!== 'COMPLETED'` |
| `adjustment-governance.service.ts` | 207, 727 | `!== 'LOCKED'` | `!== 'COMPLETED'` |
| `adjustment-governance.service.ts` | 740 | `eq(status, 'LOCKED')` for TRIP_REOPEN | `eq(status, 'COMPLETED')` |
| `accounting-transport-register.service.ts` | 86 | `eq(status, 'LOCKED')` | `eq(status, 'COMPLETED')` |
| `pnl.service.ts` | 372 | `eq(status, LOCKED)` finalization guard | `eq(status, COMPLETED)` |

Each one breaks the instant the enum value is dropped. They must all be
repointed in the same commit. (Phase 2 then refines the snapshot/dirty-flag
behavior; Phase 3 refines the closure predicate's `pod_recovered_at` clause
— but the raw `LOCKED → COMPLETED` string swap must happen here.)

## Related Code Files

- Modify: `shared/src/constants/index.ts` (lines 1-15: enum + billable set)
- Modify: `backend/src/db/schema.ts` (line 23: `tripStatusEnum`; line 637:
  add CHECK on `carrier_type`; line 639: migrate `external_carrier_id` →
  soft columns `external_entity_id` + `external_entity_type`, no FK)
- Modify: `backend/src/governance/locked-entity-manifest.ts` (lines 486-501:
  TRIP `terminalStates`)
- Create: migration `backend/drizzle/<NEXT_FREE_N>__drop_trip_status_locked.sql`
  (next free number ≥0175 — run `drizzle-kit generate`, **do not hand-number**;
  `0167`–`0174` are taken)
- Modify: `backend/src/services/trip-status-machine.service.ts`
  - Lines 133-151: remove the permissive branch; merge the migrated gates here
  - Lines 156-240: delete the LOCKED branch
  - Line 377-389: keep the `postTripLock` call; rename to `postTripCompletion`
  - Lines 125, 248, 306: drop LOCKED-specific conditionals
- Modify: `backend/src/services/trip-mutations.service.ts:1155` — rename the
  **second** `postTripLock` call site (governed-correction re-posting) to
  `postTripCompletion`. (Validation: two call sites, not one.)
- Modify: `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts`
  - Line 987: `COMPLETED || LOCKED` → `COMPLETED`
  - Line 1011: `allLockedAndAccepted` → `allCompletedAndAccepted` (Phase 3
    adds the `pod_recovered_at` clause)
  - Line 1156: `TripStatus.LOCKED` → `TripStatus.COMPLETED`
  - Line 1172: `TRIP_LOCKED` → `TRIP_COMPLETED`
- Modify: `backend/src/services/ledger.service.ts` — rename `postTripLock` →
  `postTripCompletion`, `postTripUnlock` → `postTripCompletionReverse`;
  rename **both** call sites: `trip-status-machine.service.ts:389`
  (transition handler) + `trip-mutations.service.ts:1155`
  (governed-correction re-posting)
