# Phase 4: Field Ops, Carrier Tag, Push MVP

## Overview

Land the three operational surfaces the PRD adds: (1) the **carrier-tag**
Xe nhà / Xe ngoài P&L split, using `trips.carrier_type` (now CHECK-constrained
by Phase 1); (2) **field-operations cost capture** by Ops (FORWARDER) and
Driver — tạm ứng requests, paid-on-behalf costs, the Ops→Driver order
hand-off with SLA timestamps; (3) the **push-notification MVP** scoped to
Driver and Điều vận only, wired via the existing `PUSH_RULES` +
`sendNotificationPush` (not a parallel `notifyRole` helper — red-team finding).

## Requirements

- **Functional**
  - **Carrier-tag P&L split:** management dashboard surfaces two P&L
    buckets — `Xe nhà` (`carrier_type = 'OWN'`) and `Xe ngoài`
    (`carrier_type = 'EXTERNAL'`). The CHECK constraint from Phase 1
    guarantees no non-canonical value silently drops out of either bucket.
  - **Ops field app (FORWARDER):** cash advance request; paid-on-behalf
    costs with receipt photos; "Đã lấy lệnh giấy" hand-off timestamp.
  - **Driver app (DRIVER):** confirm order receipt; record tolls/lift/fuel;
    submit completion (which feeds the e-POD path).
  - **Push MVP:** notifications fire only for DRIVER and MANAGER/ADMIN
    (Điều vận) via the existing `PUSH_RULES` system. The existing
    `[ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED]: 'all'` rule is narrowed.
- **Non-functional**
  - New FORWARDER-scoped endpoints **field-filter** their responses to
    withhold `revenue`, `grossProfit`, `driverSalary`, `externalFreightCost`
    — the PRD says Ops must not see margin/salary/cost-of-goods (red-team
    finding).
  - Late Ops/Driver cost capture on a completed trip calls
    `ArSnapshotService.markDirty` (Phase 2).
  - Push is best-effort and runs **post-commit** via control-flow (the
    codebase has no after-commit hook — red-team finding), never inside the
    tx body.

## Architecture

**Carrier tag** — `trips.carrier_type` is `varchar(20)` (Phase 1 adds the
CHECK). The PRD's `Xe nhà` / `Xe ngoài` maps 1:1 to `OWN` / `EXTERNAL`. Two
sub-claims verified (red-team):
- The tag is **input-driven** at dispatch (`trip-mutations.service.ts:507`,
  `carrierType: data.carrierType ?? 'OWN'`), NOT inherited from a vehicle
  column. Remove any "inherited from vehicle" language.
- **External-carrier entity resolved via soft columns (validation decision
  + user architectural preference):** Phase 1 replaces the locked
  `external_carrier_id → customers.id` FK with two plain columns
  (`external_entity_id integer` + `external_entity_type varchar(20)`,
  **no DB FK**) — a soft pointer resolved by a thin
  `resolveExternalCarrier(trip)` app-layer helper. An `EXTERNAL` carrier
  (Xe ngoài) can resolve to either a customer (AR-side) or a supplier
  (AP-side) per trip. The P&L split reads only `carrier_type` and is
  unaffected; this resolves the "subcontractor = vendor?" ambiguity without
  FK churn (per the project's "readable/maintainable tables over FK rigor"
  convention). The dispatch UI gains a type selector (Customer/Supplier)
  when `carrier_type = EXTERNAL`.

**Push MVP reuses `PUSH_RULES` + `sendNotificationPush`** (red-team finding,
verified at `shared/src/constants/index.ts:528`,
`notification.service.ts:98`). The existing system already does role-targeted
fan-out. The new trigger types are added to `NotificationType` and
`PUSH_RULES` with explicit audiences. The existing
`[ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED]: 'all'` (line 537) violates the PRD's
"Driver + Điều vận only" scope and is narrowed to `'dispatcher'` (or the
specific driver) here.

| Trigger | NotificationType | Audience |
|---|---|---|
| Trip dispatched to driver | `TRIP_DISPATCHED` (exists) | `'driver'` |
| Driver confirms/completes | `TRIP_DRIVER_COMPLETED` (new) | `'dispatcher'` |
| Ops paper-order collected | `TRIP_PAPER_ORDER_COLLECTED` (new) | `'driver'` |
| Driver advance request | `ADVANCE_REQUEST_SUBMITTED` (new) | `'dispatcher'` |
| Advance settlement approved | `ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED` (exists) | narrow from `'all'` → `'driver'` |

**Field-filtering for FORWARDER endpoints.** The new
`POST /trips/:id/field-costs`, the paper-order endpoint, and the
advance-request endpoint must return only the fields the Ops role needs
(trip id, status, carrier_type, their own cost rows) — never the full
`trips` row, which carries `revenue`, `grossProfit`, `driverSalary`,
`externalFreightCost`. A test asserts FORWARDER responses contain none of
those fields.

## Related Code Files

- Modify: `backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts` + dashboard widget — group
  P&L by `carrier_type`.
- Modify: `frontend` management dashboard — `Xe nhà` / `Xe ngoài` cards.
- Modify: `shared/src/constants/index.ts` — new `NotificationType` members;
  narrow `PUSH_RULES[ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED]`.
- Create: `backend/src/services/field-cost.service.ts` — Ops paid-on-behalf
  cost capture (field-filtered responses).
- Create: `backend/src/services/order-handoff.service.ts` — Ops/Driver
  hand-off timestamps.
- Modify: `backend/src/routes/*` — the new endpoints (FORWARDER/DRIVER
  scoped, field-filtered).
- Modify: cost-edit endpoints — call `ArSnapshotService.markDirty` on
  completed trips (Phase 2 also specifies this; confirm field-cost path).
- Create tests: P&L split by carrier; hand-off timestamps; push audience
  targeting; FORWARDER response field-filtering.

## Implementation Steps

1. **Carrier-tag P&L split.** Add `groupByCarrier` to the P&L query returning
   `{ OWN, EXTERNAL }`. CHECK constraint from Phase 1 guarantees no
   non-canonical silent drop. Frontend renders `Xe nhà` / `Xe ngoài`.
2. **Push MVP via PUSH_RULES.** Add the new `NotificationType` members.
   Narrow `[ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED]: 'all'` to the driver/dispatcher
   audience. Wire the trigger points in the domain services to call the
   existing `sendNotificationPush` (or whichever helper emits the
   notification + push) **post-commit by control-flow** — never inside the
   tx body (no after-commit hook exists).
3. **Ops field cost capture.** `POST /trips/:id/field-costs` (FORWARDER) —
   writes a paid-on-behalf cost row with photo. **Response field-allow-list:**
   return only `{ tripId, status, carrierType, costRowId }`, never the full
   trip. Add a test asserting `revenue`/`grossProfit`/`driverSalary` absent.
4. **Order hand-off timestamps.** `paper_order_collected_at` (Ops) +
   `driver_order_accepted_at` (Driver) on `trips`. Endpoints:
   `POST /trips/:id/paper-order-collected` (FORWARDER);
   `POST /trips/:id/driver-order-accepted` (DRIVER).
5. **Driver advance request.** `POST /advance-requests` (DRIVER) —
   `advanceRequests` already exists for Ops; ensure DRIVER can author.
6. **markDirty on late costs.** Confirm the field-cost endpoint calls
   `ArSnapshotService.markDirty(tripId, tx)` when the trip is `COMPLETED`.
7. **Tests.** P&L split matches manual totals; hand-off timestamps
   recorded; push audience targeting (only DRIVER + MANAGER/ADMIN receive);
   push failure does not fail the originator; FORWARDER response has no
   margin fields; rate-limit on push per `(userId, eventType, targetId)`
   as a requirement with a test.

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Dashboard shows `Xe nhà` / `Xe ngoài` P&L cards summing to existing
  totals (CHECK constraint prevents silent drops).
- [ ] Ops (FORWARDER) records paid-on-behalf costs with photo; responses
  contain no margin/salary fields (test-asserted).
- [ ] Ops/Driver hand-off timestamps persisted and surfaced.
- [ ] Push fires for DRIVER + MANAGER/ADMIN only at the trigger points;
  `ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED` no longer pushes to all roles.
- [ ] Push send failure does not surface as an error to the originator;
  push runs post-commit.
- [ ] Late Ops/Driver cost capture on a completed trip flips
  `ar_snapshot_dirty`.

## Risk Assessment

- **Carrier-tag relabeling (LOW).** Existing UI may show `OWN`/`EXTERNAL`
  in English. **Mitigation:** dashboard is internal; label swap with
  tooltip showing both.
- **Push spam (MEDIUM).** A burst could fan out many pushes.
  **Mitigation:** per-user per-event rate limit is a **requirement**
  (step 7), not a Risk-Assessment suggestion.
- **FORWARDER margin leakage (HIGH).** New endpoints returning the full
  `trips` row leak margin data the PRD forbids Ops from seeing.
  **Mitigation:** field-allow-list + test (step 3).
- **Fuel-AI dependency (LOW).** Photo capture endpoint only stores the
  image; extraction owned by `260801-0942` Phase 4. **Mitigation:**
  document the boundary.
- **EXTERNAL-as-customer semantics mismatch (LOW).** If the customer's
  "subcontractor" mental model is vendor/AP-side, future features built on
  the tag fight the existing `externalCarrierId → customers` FK.
  **Mitigation:** Phase 4 confirms intent or flags a follow-up; the P&L
  split itself is unaffected.
</file>

