# Phase 1: Authority and migration foundation

## Context Links

- [Plan](./plan.md)
- [Master-data source audit](./research/master-data-source-audit.md)
- `backend/src/db/schema.ts`
- `docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md` — Q15, Q17, Q18, Q22, Q23

## Overview

Define one clean authority model before UI work: operational sites, shipment fulfillment units, trip linkage, driver milestones, versioned e-POD, role actions, and aggregate closure. This product has no production compatibility requirement.

## Key Insights

- `trips_shipment_id_live_uniq` currently permits only one non-canceled trip per shipment and must be replaced.
- Dispatch currently snapshots all shipment containers into one trip. FCL requires container-level fulfillment; LCL requires one shipment-level unit.
- `tripStatusEnum` remains execution/financial authority. Fulfillment rows must not duplicate trip lifecycle state.
- Generic `tripPhotos` are not e-POD, and `driverProgressEvents` do not transition trip status.

## Requirements

### Functional

- Create `operational_sites` **(proposed)** for factory/warehouse masters with customer ownership, stable code, type, address, Google Maps URL, billing identity fields, rules, active flag, and version.
- Create `shipment_fulfillments` **(proposed)** as the dispatch unit: `FCL_CONTAINER` references exactly one shipment container; `LCL_SHIPMENT` references no container and is unique per shipment.
- Link one trip to one fulfillment; allow multiple live trips per shipment only through distinct active fulfillments.
- Model fulfillment requiredness separately from trip execution. A canceled fulfillment is unresolved until it has either a valid replacement fulfillment or an approved `NOT_REQUIRED` disposition with actor, reason, and time.
- Create append-only task-aware progress and versioned e-POD authorities without duplicating billing or trip status.
- Create master-import batch and redacted row-result authorities so dry-run/apply state is persistent, reviewable, and idempotent.
- Define idempotency keys and expected-version checks for import, decomposition, assignment, milestone, submit, approve/reject, complete, and close commands.

### Non-functional

- Drizzle only. Add database constraints for cardinality and first-winner behavior.
- Uploaded evidence never stores public URLs; APIs return scoped signed/download routes.
- No Zalo fields, GPS stream, coordinate polling, or live-map contracts.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  S[Shipment] --> F[Shipment fulfillment]
  C[Shipment container] -->|FCL one-to-one| F
  F --> T[Trip]
  T --> P[Progress events]
  T --> E[e-POD submission versions]
  T --> B[Existing billing and ledger authority]
  F --> A[Shipment aggregate projection]
```

`shipments` owns booking/cargo. `shipment_fulfillments` owns decomposition and assignment identity. `trips` owns execution and financial lifecycle. e-POD owns delivery evidence/review. `billingDocuments` owns Debit Note/AR.

## File Inventory

| Action | File | Purpose | Test impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| Modify | `backend/src/db/schema.ts` | Add sites, import batches/results, fulfillments, POD tables/enums; replace shipment live-trip uniqueness | Full schema/backend/E2E |
| Create | `backend/drizzle/<generated>_dispatch_workflow.sql` | Forward migration generated from Drizzle schema | Migration apply/reset |
| Modify | `shared/src/schemas/index.ts` | Shared inputs/results/status contracts | Shared/backend/frontend typecheck |
| Modify | `shared/src/constants/index.ts` | Milestone/evidence labels and notification types | Contract tests |
| Modify | `backend/src/casbin/policy.csv` | Narrow resource/action matrix | Full RBAC/E2E |
| Create | `backend/src/services/shipment-fulfillment.service.ts` | Canonical decomposition/link/assertions | New service tests |
| Create | `backend/src/tests/shipment-fulfillment-schema.test.ts` | Cardinality/constraint/migration coverage | Backend |

## Exact Interface Checklist

- [x] Replace `trips_shipment_id_live_uniq` with unique active `trip.fulfillmentId` and fulfillment cardinality constraints.
- [x] Add unique active `drivers.userId` binding to one authenticated `DRIVER` principal; nullable means not dispatchable, never an implicit account.
- [x] Fulfillment cancellation fields enforce `REPLACED` with `replacementFulfillmentId` or `NOT_REQUIRED` with approval attribution; an unresolved cancellation remains required by aggregate checks.
- [x] `createShipmentFulfillments(tx, shipmentId, expectedVersion, idempotencyKey)` **(proposed)**.
- [x] Import batches uniquely identify file hash + parser version; applied row results store classification and redacted reasons, not raw personal data.
- [x] `assertFulfillmentBelongsToShipment(...)` and `assertFulfillmentReadyForDispatch(...)` **(proposed)**.
- [x] Site snapshot DTO contains only operationally necessary fields; sensitive contacts remain role-scoped.
- [x] Existing `transitionTripStatus()` remains the only trip lifecycle transition authority.

## Implementation Steps

1. Write characterization tests for existing shipment/container/trip constraints and financial posting at `COMPLETED`.
2. Define schema/enums/checks and exact delete/cancel/replacement behavior.
3. Generate and inspect the Drizzle migration; update dev reset/seed order for the new clean model.
4. Define the role/action matrix: ADMIN/MANAGER dispatch; scoped CLERK intake and e-POD approval; DRIVER own-trip actions; ACCOUNTANT read/export only; CUSTOMER scoped portal read.
5. Implement core fulfillment service and transaction boundaries.
6. Prove concurrent retries cannot create duplicate fulfillment/trip rows.

## Test Scenario Matrix

| Priority | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| P0 | Two processes decompose one FCL shipment | One fulfillment per container |
| P0 | LCL decomposition retried | Exactly one fulfillment |
| P0 | Same container attached twice | DB rejection, no partial rows |
| P0 | Trip linked to second fulfillment | DB rejection |
| P0 | Two active drivers bind the same user | DB rejection |
| P1 | Cancel then replace task | Old row auditable; one active replacement |
| P0 | Canceled task lacks replacement/waiver | Still required; shipment cannot close |
| P1 | CLERK outside unit/customer scope | 404 and no mutation |
| P1 | ACCOUNTANT calls operational approval | 403 |

## QA and Regression Gate

- Focused schema/service/contract/RBAC tests first.
- Then root lint, both typechecks/tests, build, and full E2E because schema/RBAC/public contracts change.
- Save every run under `qa/2026-08-01_dispatch-workflow_*`.

## Success Criteria

- [x] Authority boundaries are encoded in schema and services, not comments.
- [x] FCL/LCL cardinality and trip linkage are database-enforced.
- [x] No compatibility or duplicate finance layer exists.
- [x] Concurrency, scope, and migration tests are green.

## Risks, Security, and Rollback

Main risks: duplicate execution units, cross-customer evidence, and driver-triggered financial transitions. Mitigate with row locks, unique constraints, live scope checks, idempotency, and narrow commands. Before release, a corrective migration or dev/staging reset is acceptable; no production rollback machinery is required.

## Next Steps

Phase 2 uses these contracts for import and intake. Phase 3 consumes fulfillments for dispatch.
</file>

