# Phase 2: Master data and shipment intake

## Context Links

- [Plan](./plan.md)
- [Master-data source audit](./research/master-data-source-audit.md)
- `docs/quytrinh/BIẾU MẪU BÁO CÁO/29.7 - DATA PM.xlsx`
- `frontend/src/pages/clerk/ClerkShipmentCreatePage.tsx`
- `frontend/src/pages/clerk/ClerkShipmentDocsPage.tsx`
- `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts`
- `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts`

## Overview

Build an Admin-controlled, repeatable Master Data import and update flow, then make shipment intake reference canonical customer, route, operational-site, port/yard, shipping-line, vehicle, and driver records. Keep the FCL/LCL form dynamic, allow incomplete work to remain `DRAFT`, and make the explicit submit action enter the dispatch queue as `Chờ điều phối`.

## Source Findings

- `DATA PM.xlsx` contains eight populated factories, nineteen port/yard rows, thirty-seven plates, thirty-six trailers, and a personnel sheet containing thirty-two driver rows.
- Customer and route sheets contain headers but no usable populated rows. The `THÔNG TIN NCC` row is ambiguously labeled. These are validation findings, not seedable defaults.
- Site invoice identity and strict rules are long free text. Import must parse safe structured fields while retaining source text for Admin review.

## Requirements

### Functional

- Admin uploads `.xlsx`, receives a dry-run summary by sheet/entity, corrects or rejects invalid rows, then explicitly applies the accepted batch.
- Import is idempotent by source hash + entity natural key; every applied batch records actor, file hash, counts, warnings, and row-level outcome without storing private row content in logs.
- Preserve leading-zero identifiers and normalize dates, phones, plates, tax codes, weights, and capacity units before validation.
- Empty/template/example rows never create records. Ambiguous supplier/customer or missing route rows remain `BLOCKED`, never guessed.
- Selecting a factory opens a detail dialog with address, maps link, lift-fee billing identity, contacts, and strict rules.
- FCL intake supports repeated container rows with container number/type/weight, shipping line, pickup port, and drop port.
- LCL intake supports one pickup warehouse, package type/count, KG, CBM, and planned delivery date; no fake container.
- Submitting a valid intake atomically moves the shipment to `IN_PROGRESS` and creates one active `UNSEEN` dispatch handoff; the UI label is `Chờ điều phối`. Saving an incomplete form only updates `DRAFT` and creates no handoff.

### Non-functional

- Import supports realistic file sizes without holding uploaded bytes or all database rows indefinitely.
- Admin-only import/apply; CLERK/MANAGER read active masters. Sensitive personnel fields are not returned to operational dropdowns.
- Admin may bind an imported driver master to one existing active user whose role is exactly `DRIVER`; import never creates a login. Unbound, duplicate-bound, inactive, deleted, or role-mismatched drivers are not dispatchable.
- Master DTO allowlists are role-specific: scoped CLERK and MANAGER/ADMIN may read operational-site contacts, strict rules, and billing identity required by intake; DRIVER receives only issued-trip contact/instructions; ACCOUNTANT receives billing identity without private operational contacts; cross-customer direct reads return 404.
- Desktop/mobile parity: searchable selects, readable rule dialog, 44px actions, and no horizontal overflow.

## Architecture and Data Flow

`Workbook upload -> parse/normalize -> row classification -> dry-run report -> Admin apply -> canonical masters -> shipment create/update -> site snapshot/decomposition readiness`.

The workbook is an onboarding source, not a runtime authority. After apply, database master records are authoritative and subsequent Admin changes use normal CRUD/versioning.

## File Inventory

| Action | File | Purpose | Test impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| Modify | `backend/src/routes/config.ts` | Register master import endpoints | Config/RBAC |
| Create | `backend/src/routes/config/master-data-import.routes.ts` | Upload, dry-run, apply, batch status | Route/idempotency |
| Create | `backend/src/services/master-data-import.service.ts` | Parse, classify, validate, apply | Parser/service |
| Modify | `backend/src/services/config.service.ts` | Return active sites/ports/vehicle metadata safely | Bootstrap tests |
| Modify | `backend/src/db/schema.ts` | Enforce unique active driver-user binding from Phase 1 authority | Schema/RBAC |
| Modify | `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts` | Reference-aware create/update/detail | Shipment routes |
| Modify | `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts` | Validate master refs and snapshots | Shipment service |
| Modify | `shared/src/schemas/index.ts` | Site/import/FCL/LCL contracts | Shared tests |
| Modify | `frontend/src/pages/clerk/ClerkShipmentCreatePage.tsx` | Dynamic reference-based intake | Frontend |
| Modify | `frontend/src/pages/clerk/ClerkShipmentDocsPage.tsx` | Edit/detail parity | Frontend |
| Create | `frontend/src/components/shipment/OperationalSiteDetailsDialog.tsx` | Factory rule/billing detail | A11y/responsive |
| Create | `frontend/src/pages/config/MasterDataImportPage.tsx` | Admin dry-run/apply workflow | Frontend/RBAC |
| Create | `backend/src/tests/master-data-import.test.ts` | Classification/idempotency/privacy | Backend |

## Exact Interface Checklist

- [x] `analyzeMasterWorkbook(file, actor)` **(proposed)** returns typed counts/warnings without raw PII logs.
- [x] `applyMasterImport(batchId, expectedVersion, idempotencyKey)` **(proposed)** rejects unresolved/changed batches.
- [x] Natural keys: customer/partner tax code or approved internal code; site customer+code; port stable code/name; vehicle plate; trailer plate; driver approved internal identity.
- [x] `quickCreateShipmentSchema` and `updateShipmentSchema` accept canonical IDs; display snapshots preserve issued-task meaning.
- [x] The submit-for-dispatch command uses shipment expected version + idempotency key and atomically creates/reuses the single active handoff.
- [x] Existing CLERK scope checks run for every customer/site/shipment read and write.
- [x] `bindDriverUser(driverId, userId, expectedVersion)` **(proposed)** validates active records, exact `DRIVER` role, and one-to-one binding without creating credentials.
- [x] Site/master response schemas are separate allowlisted DTOs for intake, driver order, and accounting contexts.

## Implementation Steps

1. Add failing parser tests from sanitized fixtures representing populated, blank, ambiguous, duplicate, and malformed workbook rows.
2. Implement normalized row classification and a persistent import-batch/result model from Phase 1 schema.
3. Implement Admin dry-run/apply UI with explicit counts and downloadable redacted error report.
4. Seed/configure the populated site, port, fleet, and driver rows only after dry-run passes; leave blank customer/routes unseeded.
5. Replace free-text factory/port choices in create/edit with canonical searchable selects and a detail dialog.
6. Preserve partial draft behavior while validating mode-specific FCL/LCL fields before handoff.

## Test Scenario Matrix

| Priority | Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| P0 | Blank customer/route template row | Classified template; zero writes |
| P0 | Same file/apply retried | Same result; no duplicates |
| P0 | Plate assigned to unknown driver | Blocked row with actionable error |
| P0 | Driver has no valid authenticated binding | Import may retain master row; dispatch eligibility is false with an actionable Admin reason |
| P0 | Bind non-DRIVER, duplicate, inactive, or deleted user | Rejected; no partial binding |
| P0 | Tax/phone identifiers parsed as numbers | Leading zero preserved as text |
| P1 | Factory rules updated after shipment handoff | Existing task snapshot unchanged |
| P1 | LCL switches to FCL | Explicit confirmation clears LCL-only fields |
| P0 | Valid submit double-tapped | One `IN_PROGRESS` shipment state and one active `UNSEEN` handoff |
| P0 | Incomplete draft saved | Remains `DRAFT`; no dispatch queue item |
| P1 | CLERK selects out-of-scope customer | No options/leak; server rejects direct ID |
| P0 | Cross-customer site/contact direct read | 404; response contains no billing/contact fields |

## QA and Regression Gate

- Focused parser/import/shipment and create-form tests.
- Full schema/RBAC/typecheck/test/build/E2E gates.
- Manual 1440/1024/768/390/320 checks for import report, dynamic form, and site dialog.

## Success Criteria

- [x] Every source row is `ACCEPTED`, `BLOCKED`, `TEMPLATE`, or `EXAMPLE`; only accepted rows write.
- [x] Eight site and nineteen port/yard source rows can pass validated dry-run without exposing private data.
- [x] Blank customer/route sheets produce zero business rows.
- [x] FCL and LCL fields persist through create, detail, edit, and handoff readiness.
- [x] Site rules are visible before dispatch and available for immutable task snapshots.

## Risks, Security, and Rollback

Treat workbook files as sensitive. Enforce size/type limits, formula-safe parsing, no macro execution, redacted errors, and Admin authorization. Before release, bad imports can be corrected by deleting the import batch and resetting/reseeding dev/staging; do not introduce production compatibility machinery.

## Next Steps

Phase 3 decomposes validated shipments into dispatchable units.
</file>

