## What Is Already Authoritative

- Debit Note issuance is not a fake stub. It uses saved billing documents, governance actions, PDF/HTML export, and explicit role gating in [billing-documents.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts#L36).
- Payment receipts are real ledger-affecting records. The allocation service persists receipts, unapplied balances, ledger entries, and receipt-level governance actions in [payment-allocation.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts#L807).
- Debt offsets are explicit, server-computed, and approval-gated. The amount is clamped to `min(AR, AP)` and approval/cancel both post mirrored ledger entries in [debtOffset.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/debtOffset.service.ts#L176).
- Executive finance reporting is already source-linked. [dashboard-stats.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts#L20) composes P&L, receivables, treasury, and reminders into one executive payload; access is capability-gated through role/Casbin.
- Reminder delivery is operational. [receivable-reminder.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/receivable-reminder.service.ts#L114), [email.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/email.service.ts#L78), and [notification.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/notification.service.ts#L69) already handle durable in-app rows, retry logic, and role-scoped push.

## Current Gaps And Risks

1. No workbook-specific projection across the existing accountant destinations.
- The finance routes already provide the role-first workflow; a new shell would duplicate them.
- Missing workbook columns, filters, and summaries should be added to the authoritative destinations or linked drill-downs.

2. In-place edit vs lock semantics are still mixed.
- [billing-documents.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts#L78) still exposes `PUT /finance/billing-documents/:id` as always-editable.
- The same file also has governance/issue/send-for-confirmation endpoints, so the authority exists, but the workbook will need a clear rule for when the user is editing a draft versus viewing a locked document.

3. Finance math is duplicated across services.
- Debit-note AR impact is computed in [billingDocument.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts#L169).
- Receipt allocation, unapplied balance, and refund deltas are recomputed in [payment-allocation.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts#L729).
- P&L and dashboard widgets each recompute period totals in [pnl.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts#L29), [dashboard-stats.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts#L20), and [dashboard-widgets.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/dashboard-widgets.service.ts#L45).
- This is acceptable for a service layer, but risky if the workbook tries to present one combined number set without a shared projection contract.

4. Export and delivery are fragmented.
- Debit Note export is xlsx or printable HTML in [billing-documents.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts#L190).
- Ledger statement export is separate in [ledger.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/ledger.routes.ts#L43).
- There is no single workbook export path that bundles the accountant-relevant sections together.

5. Reminder/email is scheduler-first.
- The reminder service and email pipeline are strong, but they are not surfaced as a workbook module.
- Scheduled history may be projected read-only. Manual preview/send requires a separate side-effecting contract and is not part of this MVP.

## Decision Gates

- Finance write endpoints are already role-gated with `ADMIN`, `MANAGER`, and `ACCOUNTANT` in [billing-documents.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/billing-documents.routes.ts#L31) and [payments.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/payments.routes.ts#L176).
- Debt offset approval/cancel is restricted to `ADMIN` and `MANAGER` in [debt-offsets.routes.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/routes/financial/debt-offsets.routes.ts#L58).
- Executive dashboard access is capability-gated through role/Casbin; [dashboard-stats.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts#L138) always computes the canonical payload for authorized callers.
- Notification routing is role-aware and deep-link aware in [notification.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/notification.service.ts#L190).
- Shared input contracts for money/reporting live in [shared/src/schemas/customer-service-finance.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/shared/src/schemas/customer-service-finance.ts#L31), so the workbook should bind to those schemas rather than inventing a parallel shape.

## Exact Likely Touchpoints For A Workbook

- Existing navigation files are verification-only for this plan; no new page key is required for MVP.
- Frontend dashboard composition around [frontend/src/components/dashboard/ExecutiveFinancialStrip.tsx](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/frontend/src/components/dashboard/ExecutiveFinancialStrip.tsx#L20), [frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentsPanel.tsx](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/frontend/src/components/billing/BillingDocumentsPanel.tsx#L33), and [frontend/src/pages/debt-detail-ledger.tsx](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/frontend/src/pages/debt-detail-ledger.tsx#L1).
- Backend finance aggregation around [backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts#L20), [backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts#L29), and [backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts).
- Route mounting and guards in [backend/src/middleware/casbin.ts](/Users/dev/Documents/projects/silversea/backend/src/middleware/casbin.ts#L19) and the finance route modules.

## Tests That Already Anchor The Scope

- Billing documents / Debit Note: `backend/src/tests/billingDocument.service.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/q15-debit-note-governance.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/m36-debit-note-lifecycle.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/debit-note-pdf.test.ts`.
- Receipts / refunds / allocations: `backend/src/tests/q03-payment-receipts-route.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/q03-payment-refund-route.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/m56-payment-allocation.test.ts`.
- Debt offsets: `backend/src/tests/m64-debt-offsets.test.ts`.
- P&L / dashboard: `backend/src/tests/pnl-invariant.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/m115-dashboard-widgets.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/executive-dashboard-rbac.test.ts`.
- Reminder/email: `backend/src/tests/m57-receivable-reminder.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/email-service.test.ts`, `backend/src/tests/email-settings.test.ts`.

## Ranked Recommendation

1. Build the accountant workbook as a composition layer over existing authorities, not as a new finance engine.
- Best fit for current code.
- Lowest risk.
- Preserves the current approval and ledger contracts.

2. Before composing the workbook, define one explicit lock/edit rule for billing documents and exports.
- This is the main ambiguity in the current code.
- Without it, the workbook will surface mixed semantics: editable draft, approved issue flow, and export-only locked states.

3. Add one shared workbook projection contract for totals and period logic.
- Reuse the current service authorities, but do not let the UI recompute its own financial truth.
- This is the main guard against drift between AR/AP, P&L, and dashboard numbers.

## Limitations

- I did not inspect every route mount or every frontend page file in this pass, so the exact browser route that should host the workbook is an inference from `pageCatalog`, dashboard surfaces, and finance components.
- I did not browse the web.

## Resolved Scope Decisions

- Use `/accounting` as Accountant home and keep existing finance routes as drill-downs; no compatibility redirect is required.
- Preserve upstream draft/lock/governance semantics; this plan does not invent a second edit lifecycle.
- Keep exports section-specific; a bundled package remains deferred pending measured need and retention/content approval.
</file>

