# Phase 1: Authority and requirement contract

## Context Links

- [Workbook requirements](./research/workbook-accountant-requirements.md)
- [Current finance gap map](./research/accounting-codebase-gap-map.md)
- [Upstream finance plan](../260730-2232-customer-service-finance-workflow/plan.md)
- [Upstream dispatch plan](../260801-0942-end-to-end-dispatch-workflow/plan.md)
- `docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md`

## Overview

Freeze the accountant vocabulary, dates, roles, posting boundaries, report
definitions, and source ownership before adding schema or money writes.

## Accepted Pre-release Contract (2026-08-01)

- Product lifecycle: pre-release. Replace conflicting development contracts
  directly; no dual paths, compatibility shims, or legacy data backfill.
- Accountant home: `/accounting`, label `Kế toán`; existing finance routes are
  drill-downs, not alternate authorities.
- Periods in `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh`: `T1` = service days 1–25; `T2` = service days
  26–month end; `T3` = a governed late adjustment posted in the current open
  cycle and linked to its original locked period. Direct date range remains
  visible in every API/export so a T label never hides its boundary.
- Profit visibility: `ACCOUNTANT`, `MANAGER`, and `ADMIN` may read management
  profitability. Execution/approval capabilities remain separately governed.
- VAT: document/line net amounts are VAT-exclusive; allowed configured rates are
  0%, 5%, 8%, and 10%; VND tax rounds half-up per line and the document stores
  net, tax, and gross snapshots. Zero-rate and exempt are distinct treatments.
  Corporate-income tax and VAT payable remain unavailable without booked tax postings.
- Dates: completion/service date owns transport and management-profit periods;
  document issue owns billing issuance; contractual due date owns aging;
  receipt/allocation value date owns payment; official reporting period remains
  the period-lock authority.
- Reporting consistency: combined Accountant overview responses use one
  repeatable-read database transaction and return `asOf` plus a deterministic
  source checksum; exports repeat the same query contract.
- Row scope: in the pre-release single-company product, `ADMIN`, `MANAGER`, and
  `ACCOUNTANT` have company-wide finance scope; `CUSTOMER` is self-scoped;
  operational roles receive no finance rows unless a named capability says otherwise.
- Manual reminder send and refunds of applied allocations remain deferred.

## Requirements

- Functional:
  - Publish a requirement-disposition matrix for every populated workbook
    range: reuse, extend, defer, reject, or decision-blocked.
  - Define immutable date semantics for service, e-POD/lock, transport
    confirmation, document issue/export, original/processing due date,
    payment value date, and reporting period.
  - Define `T1/T2/T3`; only `T1 = day 1–25` is evidenced, so T2/T3 remain blocked.
  - Approve a role/action/field/row-scope matrix for `ADMIN`, `MANAGER`,
    `ACCOUNTANT`, and read-only operational access; include direct IDs, API,
    export, search, queue counts, cache, and UI, backed by an authoritative
    user-to-unit/customer assignment.
  - Inherit approved reminder cadence, maker/checker separation, completion-date
    attribution, period locks, and late-adjustment rules without reopening them.
  - Close only the true delta decisions in `plan.md`: T2/T3 mapping,
    profitability visibility, VAT/tax authority, cost taxonomy, report date
    mapping, row scope, reminder attempt identity, and report consistency.
  - Choose either one repeatable-read transaction or a persisted immutable
    report run/snapshot as the combined-report consistency contract.
  - Confirm `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST` as sole carrier AP obligation and
    `PAYMENT_STATEMENT` as presentation-only.
- Non-functional:
  - One versioned metric glossary and one authority per financial fact.
  - VND integer storage/display unless an accepted contract requires otherwise;
    use `round2dp()`/shared calculations where decimal rates apply.
  - Audit every approved decision with owner, effective date, and version.

## Architecture

`accepted shipment/fulfillment -> locked trip -> trip financial posting ->
billing document/AP source -> ledger -> receipt/allocation -> read models`.

The workbook projection is read-only composition. It never owns balances.
Debit Note is the AR instrument; current carrier/vendor payables remain AP;
receipts/allocations own settlement; profitability snapshots/P&L own reports.

## Related Code Files

- Modify: `docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md` only after decisions are approved.
- Modify: `shared/src/schemas/customer-service-finance.ts` for the accepted
  period/filter/visibility contracts.
- Modify: `shared/src/types/index.ts`, `shared/src/schemas/index.ts`, and barrel
  exports only for accepted shared contracts.
- Verify: `backend/src/db/schema.ts`, `backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts`,
  `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts`,
  `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts`, `backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts`,
  `backend/src/services/profitability.service.ts`, and `backend/src/services/receivable-reminder.service.ts`.
- Tests: add a focused contract test file only after the shared contract is accepted.

## Implementation Steps

1. Re-scout all named files because the worktree contains concurrent dispatch
   and billing changes; record current symbols and test baselines.
2. Create the workbook range-to-authority/disposition matrix and explicitly
   exclude sample rows, example formulas, and `PHƠI PHIẾU`.
3. Record inherited approved rules, then run a focused decision workshop only
   for the true deltas in `plan.md`; record owner, safe default, and blocked slices.
4. Write the period/metric/status glossary with formula examples and edge cases,
   but reference canonical services rather than embedding new calculations.
5. Write the exact role/action/field/row-scope matrix and map it to service
   query predicates, Casbin resources, export/search/cache enforcement, and
   frontend capabilities.
6. Add contract-level tests for approved enums/date fields and rejection of
   unknown period codes or VAT treatment.

## Success Criteria

- [ ] T1/T2/T3 and all seven date meanings are unambiguous and testable.
- [ ] Approved reminder, governance, attribution, and period-lock rules are
  inherited without a conflicting workshop decision.
- [ ] VAT, manual-reminder collision, profit visibility, cost/tax sources,
  report-date mapping, row scope, and report consistency have named owners,
  safe defaults, and accepted decisions for any enabled slice.
- [ ] Every workbook range has a disposition and authoritative data source.
- [ ] No new ledger, receivable, payable, tax, or profitability authority is proposed.
- [ ] Shared contracts compile and their focused tests pass with artifacts under `qa/`.

## Risk Assessment

Highest risk is mistaking workbook layout for accounting policy. Stop the
phase if any amount can be produced from two authorities. Rollback is removal
of additive contract code/docs only; do not migrate data in this phase.

## Security And RBAC

Server field projection—not CSS hiding—must enforce restricted facts. Row-scope
predicates must constrain lists, direct IDs, exports, search, queue counts, and
caches. Accountant may read authorized shipment evidence but cannot dispatch,
approve e-POD, or lock trips.
</file>

