# Phase 5: Dedicated accountant home and exports

## Context Links

- [UI codebase map](./research/accounting-codebase-gap-map.md)
- `frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx`
- `shared/src/navigation/pageCatalog.ts`

## Overview

Create a thin, flat `/accounting` home labeled `Kế toán` that composes finance
work queues and links to existing bounded destinations without duplicating their
financial calculations or detailed workflows.

## Requirements

- Functional:
  - Make `/accounting` the Accountant home and first finance navigation item.
    Preserve `/debt`, `/payables`, `/finance`, `/profit`, billing detail, and
    governance as authoritative drill-downs.
  - Transport register supports server filters, saved/copyable URL state,
    selection summary, preview, bulk confirmation, export, and visible failures.
  - Debt/report surfaces preserve `asOf`, period, entity, status, search, sort,
    page, and expanded detail when navigating back.
  - Exports are section-specific and authority-versioned; a bundled package is
    deferred unless finance approves retention/content and performance needs.
  - Every list, direct detail URL, search, queue count, preview, and export uses
    the same server-enforced unit/customer row scope; the client cannot broaden it.
- Non-functional:
  - Desktop/tablet use a bounded table plus detail/drawer where useful.
  - Mobile converts wide rows to labeled cards or focused detail; no page-level
    horizontal overflow, hidden actions, or tiny touch targets.
  - Accessible selection announcements, keyboard operation, focus restoration,
    44px touch targets, and reduced-motion support.
  - Flat design with compact density; no nested decorative cards or shadows.

## Architecture

The new route is a composition shell only. Money stays server-derived and each
queue uses the same versioned query contract as its drill-down. The shell owns
layout, shared filter context, counts, and links—not balances or posting logic.

UI references consulted: Untitled UI's public application table/filter patterns
and Tailkit `a-c-tables-04` responsive rows, `a-c-tables-05` selection, and
`a-c-tables-15` search/actions. Adapt patterns to the existing design system;
do not install or copy them verbatim. Shadcn MCP was unavailable in this session,
