# Kế toán Workflow and Reporting Requirements

## Outcome

Turn the revised `29.7 - DEMO KẾ TOÁN.xlsx` into a finance-safe accountant
workflow without copying spreadsheet formulas into a second accounting engine.
The app keeps its existing `billingDocuments`, governed Debit Note lifecycle,
ledger, receivable authority, carrier/vendor payable projections, payment
receipts/allocations/refunds, reminders, trip financial postings, and P&L as
the only sources of truth.

The attachment is a requirements source. Its sample companies, trips, amounts,
VAT example, 50% margin threshold, and unfinished `PHƠI PHIẾU` sheet are not
approved production data or policy.

This is a new product with no running production deployment. Implementation may
replace pre-release contracts directly: no compatibility shims, dual reads or
writes, legacy route redirects, or historical-data migration layer. Favor one
maintainable modular authority and reset/reseed development data when required.

## Current Delivery Slice

The worktree already delivers a bounded accountant slice, but the six-phase
plan remains `in-progress`.

- `/accounting` is the dedicated `Kế toán` home and thin composition shell over
  the existing finance drill-downs.
- Transport register read surfaces support customer and carrier filters,
  current-page selection, bounded pagination, and source/version provenance.
- Debit Note handling is authoritative on source references, VAT treatment, and
  immutable financial-posting provenance instead of caller-authored money.
- Historical `asOf` reporting uses explicit Vietnam business-date cutoffs and
  preserves the same report identity on re-export.

Deferred from this slice:

- filter-wide select-all across the full filtered dataset
- carrier confirmation and payment-statement save flow
- repeatable-read combined Accountant overview with deterministic checksum
- the remaining monthly, aging, reminder, and bundled export surface

See [implementation status](./reports/implementation-status.md) for the
bounded-slice checkpoint that mirrors the current worktree.

## Accountant Requirements

| Area | Required behavior | Workbook evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Transport reconciliation | Filter by date, customer, carrier/owner and period; select rows; record invoice-readiness confirmation; keep transport details collapsible | `TH VẬN TẢI!A1:AG18` |
| Customer billing | Preview selected rows, choose approved VAT treatment, generate the configured Debit Note, export PDF/XLSX, then govern the single AR posting | `TH VẬN TẢI!A21:U66` |
| Carrier/vendor payable | Confirm selected rows and issue a source-linked statement over the AP already posted by `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST`; confirmation must never create a second payable | `TH VẬN TẢI!B20:S29` |
| Collections | Show invoice/document reference, due date, paid amount, balance, actual payment date, warning state, and scheduled-reminder history; manual reminder send is a separately governed deferred action | `BÁO CÁO CÔNG NỢ THEO THÁNG!A1:Q25` |
| Aging and customer quality | Show count, amount, and ratio by aging bucket; top on-time and overdue customers; preserve a selected `asOf` date | `BÁO CÁO TÌNH TRẠNG KH!A2:I21` |
| Daily margin | Separate external and own-fleet trips; show revenue, direct-cost breakdown, profit and margin with expandable detail | `BC HÀNG NGÀY!A1:AC25` |
| Monthly reporting | Revenue/cost/profit KPIs, prior-period margin change, trends, cost mix, due/overdue summaries, and a source-linked monthly P&L taxonomy | `BC LÃI LỖ!A1:N28`, `LN THÁNG!A1:D45` |
| Roles and delivery | Finance-first desktop/mobile workspace, field-level visibility, full `vi-VN` digits, accessible bulk actions, and auditable exports | Workbook visibility/interaction notes across the sheets above |

## Authority And Scope Boundaries

- Reuse current finance services; do not add a spreadsheet-shaped ledger or a
  second receivable/payable calculator.
- A transport row becomes financially reportable only from the accepted,
  ACTIVE, versioned dispatch/trip financial posting. Persist that
  `financialPostingId` and its immutable version/checksum on every financially
  sourced snapshot; operational `trip.version` is not financial provenance.
- UI and API callers submit source identities, not authoritative amounts.
  Arbitrary ad-hoc lines, exclusions, base amounts, and overrides require a
  separately governed adjustment contract and may not flow through normal save.
- Debit Note remains the sole AR debt instrument unless finance/legal approves
  the one-posting legal-invoice replacement/alias contract in the upstream plan.
- Payment and actual-payment-date fields come from persisted receipts and
  allocations, never manual report overrides.
- Taxes are displayed only from an approved tax/accounting authority. VAT
  selection is not sufficient to derive tax payable or corporate income tax.
- The existing `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST` ledger post is the sole carrier AP
  obligation. `PAYMENT_STATEMENT` remains presentation-only; a future change of
  posting pivot requires a separately approved migration and reversal design.
- Historical views use one explicit `asOf` cutoff and one report snapshot/run
  identity through API, cache, UI, and export. Current-time recomputation may
  not be labeled as a historical report.
- Access control covers role, action, field, and row scope. Direct IDs, search,
  exports, queue counts, and caches must enforce the same unit/customer scope.
- This plan supports the existing unapplied-cash refund contract. Refunds of
  already-applied allocations are explicitly deferred to a governed
  deallocation/chargeback plan and may not be represented as completed here.
- `ACCOUNTANT` remains read-only for dispatch and e-POD approval.
- No workbook import, demo-row seed, local/staging mutation, deployment, or
  production cutover is authorized by this plan.

## Inherited Approved Rules

These are not reopened by the workbook: T−3/due/T+3/weekly reminder cadence and
business-hour handling; maker/checker/approver separation; completion-date
attribution; customer-cycle period locks; and post-lock late adjustments linked
to the original period. They remain authoritative until the user explicitly
changes the approved PRD.

## True Delta Decisions

| Delta | Owner | Safe default while unresolved | Blocks |
|---|---|---|---|
| Define `T2/T3` and map workbook confirmation labels to the approved billing cycle (`T1 = day 1–25` is the only evidenced rule) | Product + Finance | Show canonical dates; omit unresolved period labels | Period filters only |
| Reconcile workbook Admin-only profit/commission/margin notes with current Accountant access | Product + Finance + Security | Preserve current server policy; do not broaden access | Restricted fields in Phases 4–5 |
| Approve VAT authority, allowed rates/effective dates, line/document basis, rounding residuals, zero/exempt/unknown treatment, corrections, and template/legal-invoice boundary | Finance + Legal | Preserve inclusive legacy totals as `UNKNOWN`; do not decompose or infer VAT | VAT authoring and tax fields |
| Approve sources for revised own-fleet costs, fixed/finance costs, tax, and before/after-tax taxonomy | Finance | Return unavailable/source-missing state | Affected Phase 4 categories only |
| Map each workbook output to existing service, issue, due, payment, and official reporting dates | Finance + Product | Use the existing authority per fact; never collapse dates into one “month” | Conflicting workbook projections |
| Choose the cross-service consistency mechanism: one repeatable-read transaction or a persisted immutable report run/snapshot with source watermark and checksum | Architecture + Finance | Do not issue/re-export a combined report as reconciled | Phase 4 combined reports/exports |
| Define authoritative user-to-unit/customer row scope for finance data | Product + Security | Deny cross-scope detail/export/search; do not infer assignment | Phases 2–5 scoped access |
| Define manual-versus-scheduled reminder suppression and canonical attempt identity | Finance + Operations | Manual preview only; scheduled approved cadence remains unchanged | Manual send in Phase 3 |

## Phases

| Phase | Name | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Authority and requirement contract](./phase-01-authority-and-requirement-contract.md) | In Progress |
| 2 | [Transport register adapter delta](./phase-02-transport-reconciliation-and-posting-readiness.md) | Pending |
| 3 | [Debt and collections presentation delta](./phase-03-receivables-payables-and-collections.md) | Pending |
| 4 | [Profitability workbook mapping delta](./phase-04-profitability-and-monthly-financial-reporting.md) | Pending |
| 5 | [Dedicated accountant home and exports](./phase-05-accountant-workspace-and-exports.md) | Pending |
| 6 | [Accountant-delta closed-loop QA](./phase-06-closed-loop-qa-and-rollout.md) | Pending |

## Dependencies

- The customer-service finance plan supplies legal-invoice, treasury,
  attribution, and finance-role decisions.
- The dispatch plan supplies accepted fulfillment/trip closure, e-POD, Debit
  Note source rows, and their canonical financial posting/version.
- This plan blocks customer-data cutover because example/template rows must not
  be loaded before accountant sources and reconciliation rules are accepted.
- Phase 1 blocks Phases 2–5. Phases 2–4 consume versioned upstream contracts and
  can proceed independently only for closed delta slices. Phase 5 follows those
  contracts; Phase 6 closes accountant-specific QA without taking upstream rollout ownership.

## Single-Owner Contract Matrix

| Public contract | Single owner | This plan's responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Locked trip/e-POD billing eligibility, source selection, Debit Note generation/export | Dispatch plan Phase 6 | Consume the versioned contract; add only workbook transport columns/filters not already supplied |
| Debit Note/AR, AP projections, receipts, allocations, reminder scheduler, profitability authority, role workspace | Customer-service finance plan | Consume and verify; file any missing authority fix in that plan before accountant UI depends on it |
| `financialPostingId` provenance and reporting authority | Customer-service finance plan schema/reporting phases | Require the completed versioned output; do not independently change its public contract here |
| Workbook VAT snapshot semantics | Customer-service finance plan after Finance/Legal decision | Map workbook presentation only after the upstream additive contract exists |
| Accountant workbook projection and presentation | This plan | Requirement disposition, exact adapter DTOs, existing-route UI deltas, and delta-specific QA |

Shared billing, finance, navigation, E2E, and rollout files may have only one
active owning plan. This plan records upstream gaps as dependency findings; it
does not implement the same contract in parallel.

## User-Approved Route Decision

`/accounting` is the dedicated Accountant home with Vietnamese label `Kế toán`.
`/debt`, `/payables`, `/finance`, and `/profit` remain focused drill-downs. Since
the product is pre-release, update `homeForRole(ACCOUNTANT)` directly and do not
preserve `/debt` as a compatibility redirect.

## Definition Of Done

- Every workbook requirement is implemented, explicitly deferred, or rejected
  with an owner and reason; no placeholder remains.
- Selected transport sources post at most one governed AR/AP obligation and
  retry/reversal tests reconcile source, document, ledger, and payment totals;
  carrier statement confirmation creates no second AP credit.
- Financially sourced billing lines persist `financialPostingId` plus immutable
  posting version/checksum, and hostile callers cannot author debt amounts.
- AR/AP status, reminders, aging, daily margin, and monthly P&L reconcile to
  their canonical authorities for one shared `asOf`/period definition.
- Historical `asOf` excludes later documents, adjustments, allocations,
  refunds, and ledger events and is identical on re-export.
- Role/page/action/field/row-scope visibility is proven server-side and in UI
  for all roles; hidden or out-of-scope fields never leak through API, export,
  direct ID, search, queue count, or warm cache.
- Desktop, tablet, 390px, and 320px workflows preserve filters, bulk actions,
  readable detail, focus, and zero page-level horizontal overflow.
- All affected QA gates are green and every pass/fail/re-run artifact is saved
  under `qa/` per `AGENTS.md`.

## Research

- [Workbook accountant requirements](./research/workbook-accountant-requirements.md)
- [Accounting codebase gap map](./research/accounting-codebase-gap-map.md)

## Red Team Review

Four adversarial lenses reviewed the complete plan. The controller accepted the
evidence-backed integrity and scope corrections and consolidated duplicates;
the authoritative dispositions are in
[`reports/from-controller-to-planner-red-team-consolidated-accountant-workflow-plan-review-report.md`](./reports/from-controller-to-planner-red-team-consolidated-accountant-workflow-plan-review-report.md).

| Disposition | Count |
|---|---:|
| Accepted and incorporated | 13 |
| Explicitly deferred with product boundary | 2 |
| Rejected | 0 |

Whole-plan consistency sweep: carrier AP has one posting authority; payment
statements are presentation-only; financial posting identity replaces
operational version as provenance; VAT legacy state is never guessed; historical
`asOf`, row scope, cache redaction, reminders, and report consistency now have
explicit contracts and tests. No accepted finding remains contradictory.

The earlier red-team recommendation to retain `/debt` as home was a scope default
made before a product decision existed. The user subsequently approved a
dedicated `/accounting` home, so that finding is superseded by explicit evidence;
the route must remain a thin composition over the same finance authorities.

## Open Questions

Only the true delta decisions above remain open. Phase 1 may reconcile and test
contracts; later work may proceed only for slices whose named delta is closed.
No unresolved decision authorizes inferred VAT, tax, cost, access, or period data.
