# O2C Reconciliation: Drop LOCKED, Single Terminal State

## Outcome

Bring the shipped dispatch workflow (`plans/260801-0942-...`, Phases 1–5 done,
Phase 6 shipped per its reports) into line with the customer-approved PRD
`docs/prd/O2C dev.md`. The 01/08/2026 decisions in that PRD are **source of
truth** and supersede the conflicting locked decisions of `260801-0942`.

Concretely, this plan delivers three things:

1. **Drop `TripStatus.LOCKED` entirely.** `COMPLETED` becomes the single
   terminal / posting state. Costs remain editable after completion (no
   hard-freeze); the freeze feature is explicitly deferred until the customer
   asks for it.
2. **Migrate the photo / zero-revenue / e-POD gates and the P&L finalization
   anchor onto the `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` transition.** Today those gates
   live in the separate `COMPLETED → LOCKED` branch
   (`trip-status-machine.service.ts:156-240`); the LOCKED branch is deleted
   and its gates move "one hop earlier" into the completion handler. The
   accountant/CUS e-POD acceptance that used to drive `→ LOCKED` now drives
   `→ COMPLETED` directly (and carries the same gates).
3. **Land the remaining O2C dev-note requirements:** session-scoped delete
   rules with the accountant-approved undeletable exception; the boolean
   POD-recovery gate before `Completed`; the tạm ứng settlement→advance
   offset; the Xe nhà / Xe ngoài P&L split; and a push-notification MVP
   scoped to Driver + Điều vận only.

## Source of truth and superseded decisions

- **Source of truth:** `docs/prd/O2C dev.md` (corroborated by
  `docs/prd/O2C Flow.md`). Both carry the same 01/08/2026 decision block.
- **Superseded:** the "Locked Decisions" in
  `plans/260801-0942-end-to-end-dispatch-workflow/plan.md` that reference
  `LOCKED` are **void** for all new work:
  - *"scoped CUS or Điều vận first-winner approval sets it to `LOCKED`"*
    → the e-POD acceptance now sets `COMPLETED` directly.
  - *"All active tasks must have accepted e-POD and `LOCKED` trips before the
    shipment becomes `CLOSED`."* → the gate becomes accepted e-POD **and
    `COMPLETED`** trips.
- **Phase 6 of `260801-0942`** (Debit Note export, shipped) reads trip status
  to determine billing eligibility (`debit-note-lifecycle.service.ts:132`,
  `billingDocument.service.ts:1605`). It is repointed at `COMPLETED` + the
  snapshot dirty-flag in Phase 2 of this plan.

## Locked Decisions

- **O2C dev.md is authoritative.** Any conflict between the PRD and existing
  plans, code, schemas, or tests is resolved in favour of the PRD.
- **Remove `TripStatus.LOCKED` entirely.** Collapse to `COMPLETED` as the
  single terminal/posting state. No "LOCKED-as-milestone" intermediate.
- **The gates move with the anchor, they are not deleted.** Today's
  `COMPLETED → LOCKED` branch carries: the e-POD-acceptance binding
  (`podApprovalContext`), the photo-evidence gate (≥1 photo baseline;
  CONTAINER + SEAL when `cargoTypes.requiresPhotos`), the zero-revenue soft
  guard, and the "ADMIN/MANAGER/CLERK-with-podApprovalContext only" RBAC
  check. Under the new model these gates migrate into the
  `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` handler — the e-POD acceptance path
  (`shipment.service.ts:1156`) is repointed from `transitionTripStatus(...,
  LOCKED, ...)` to `transitionTripStatus(..., COMPLETED, ...)`, carrying the
  same `podApprovalContext`. **Validation decision:** the permissive
  driver-Hoàn thành path (`POST /trips/:id/complete`, `routes/trips.ts:451`)
  is **deleted** — the sole path to `COMPLETED` is the migrated e-POD
  acceptance path. Drivers submit evidence; accountant/CUS acceptance runs
  the gates and completes.
- **`postTripLock` already fires at `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED`**
  (`trip-status-machine.service.ts:377-389`) — it does *not* need to move.
  It needs to be **renamed** to `postTripCompletion`. **Validation
  correction:** it has **two** call sites (verified), not the one the
  original draft claimed — `trip-status-machine.service.ts:389` (the
  transition handler) and `trip-mutations.service.ts:1155` (the
  governed-correction re-posting path for edits to completed trips). Both
  are legitimate and both are renamed. (The original draft of this plan
  inverted this; verified against HEAD — see Red Team Review.)
- **Costs stay editable after `COMPLETED`.** No read-only freeze. AR hand-off
  is therefore a **snapshot + dirty-flag** model on `billing_documents`
  (which already exists with `totalInclVat`, template snapshots, lifecycle),
  not a new table.
- **Roles: reuse the existing 7-value `roleEnum`, do not add `OPS`.**
  - Admin → `ADMIN`, Giám đốc → `MANAGER`, Kế toán → `ACCOUNTANT`,
    Điều vận → `MANAGER`/`ADMIN` (dispatcher authority), CUS → `CLERK`,
    Lái xe → `DRIVER`.
  - **Hiện trường (Ops) → `FORWARDER`** (reuse). **Caveat (red-team
    finding):** the prior plan text claimed this "matches the shipped
    dispatch plan's mapping" — that citation is fabricated
    (`260801-0942/plan.md` contains no such mapping). The real justification
    is YAGNI: reusing FORWARDER avoids a second enum migration. Ops users
    will inherit FORWARDER's existing surface (`forwarder_portal` capability,
    `my-forwarder-trips`, the advance/settlement flow) — this is an
    **intentional trust consolidation**, documented here, not an oversight.
    If real operations later need Ops-vs-Forwarder separation, a follow-up
    plan adds `OPS`. New Ops endpoints added by Phase 4 must field-filter
    responses to withhold margin/salary/cost-of-goods (per PRD §B0).
- **Carrier tag = existing `trips.carrier_type` (`OWN` / `EXTERNAL`).**
  - **Caveat (red-team finding):** the column is `varchar(20)` with
    `default 'OWN'` and **no CHECK constraint** — not an enum. P&L split is
    therefore best-effort unless we add the constraint. Phase 1 adds
    `CHECK (carrier_type IN ('OWN','EXTERNAL'))` and a data cleanup of any
    non-canonical rows.
  - **Polymorphic external-carrier reference, modeled as soft columns
    (validation decision + user architectural preference):** the PRD's
    `Xe ngoài (Subcontractor)` may be a customer (AR-side) or a supplier
    (AP-side). Phase 1 migrates the locked `external_carrier_id → customers.id`
    FK to two **plain columns** with **no DB FK constraint**:
    `external_entity_id integer` (nullable, default null) +
    `external_entity_type varchar(20)` (nullable, default null). Both null
    for `OWN` trips (the majority); only `EXTERNAL` trips populate them. The
    pair is a soft pointer resolved by a thin app-layer
    helper (`resolveExternalCarrier(trip)`), not by the DB. This follows the
    project's "readable/maintainable tables over FK rigor" convention (user
    preference: cross-entity references are app-layer concerns; bank-grade
    microservices use no FKs at all). Migration backfills
    `external_entity_type = 'CUSTOMER'`, `external_entity_id =
    external_carrier_id` for existing rows, then drops `external_carrier_id`
    (and its FK). The P&L split reads only `carrier_type` and is unaffected.
- **Push MVP reuses the existing `PUSH_RULES` + `sendNotificationPush`**
  (`shared/src/constants/index.ts:528`, `notification.service.ts:98`). New
  trigger types are added to `NotificationType` + `PUSH_RULES` with explicit
  audiences (`'driver'` / `'dispatcher'`), not a parallel `notifyRole`
  helper. The existing `[ADVANCE_SETTLEMENT_APPROVED]: 'all'` rule is
  **audited and narrowed** — it currently pushes to all roles, violating the
  PRD's "Driver + Điều vận only" MVP scope.
- **Tạm ứng offset, not a new contra primitive.** The settlement flow already
  posts `FORWARDER_ADVANCE` / `SERVICE_FEE` / `ADJUSTMENT` ledger entries
  (`advance.service.ts:397, 1150, 1693`). The outstanding-balance reader
  intentionally bypasses `LedgerService`
  (`advance.service.ts:1797` "forwarder ancillary-fee debits pollute it").
  Phase 3 adds only the **settlement→advance-request offset linkage** (the
  `advance_settlement_requests` join that marks requests as settled), not a
  new ledger method that would re-pollute the balance reader.
- **POD-recovery is a separate flag from e-POD acceptance, with PRD backing.**
  The PRD distinguishes "Đã thu hồi chứng từ gốc (POD mộc đỏ)" — physical
  paper return — from digital e-POD acceptance. It is modeled as
  `trips.pod_recovered_at` + `trips.pod_recovered_by`. (Original draft
  conflated this with the `Pending` TripStatus value, which does not exist.)
- **Session-scoped delete = `user + server-side idle window`** from
  `row.created_at` (default 4h, in `app_settings`). Not a literal browser
  session (no `sessions` table exists). The PRD's "phiên làm việc hiện tại"
  is satisfied by the idle window — this is a **new concept**, documented
  here, not a reuse.
- **`accountant-approved` = `approvedAt IS NOT NULL`** (a real approval
  action), **not** `approvalStatus = 'APPROVED'` (which defaults to APPROVED
  on `tripExpenses` for legacy rows, `schema.ts:1672`). The delete block
  keys off the timestamp column, not the status string — otherwise the
  blanket backfill would make every historical expense undeletable.
- **No backward-compatibility layer.** The dev/staging DB is resettable
  (matches `260801-0942` delivery strategy). No dual-read, no shadow mode.
- **Drizzle ORM only — no raw SQL** except the forward migration that drops
  the enum value.

## Scope Boundary

**In scope:**

- `shared/src/constants/index.ts` — drop `TripStatus.LOCKED`, fix
