# Phase 3: Fuel Surcharge Auto-Trigger

## Overview

Rev1 §B1 requires an automatic fuel surcharge (Phụ phí xăng dầu) computed
when a lô hàng/trip is created:
`Phụ phí = (Giá dầu hiện tại − Giá dầu gốc cấu hình) × Số Lít định mức × Tỷ lệ % chia sẻ của Khách hàng`.

Today there is **no** fuel-surcharge field, no `baseFuelPrice` config, and no
customer share-% anywhere in the schema. The debit-note template already
defines a `fuelSurchargeAmount` render variable (`seed-customers.ts:35`,
read at `billingDocument.service.ts:3084`) but **no code ever writes it** —
it is always null.

> **Red-team correction (D4, D22):** the original draft assumed
> `resolveFuelNorm` produces a trip-total `fuelLiters` available at
> `createTrip` time. It does not. `resolveFuelNorm`
> (`backend/src/services/fuel.service.ts:54`) returns per-100km norm rates,
> and the trip-total `totalFuelLiters` is produced only by
> `computeTripTotals` over `legs[]` (`shared/src/calculations/tripTotals.ts:114`),
> which `createTrip` does **not** call; the trip insert payload
> (`trip-mutations.service.ts:453-513`) has no `fuelLiters` key. The
> surcharge must therefore be captured on the path that already computes
> `totals.totalFuelLiters` — the `updateTripFigures` flow
> (`trip-mutations.service.ts:~1028-1080`) — NOT at `createTrip`. This
> phase is rewritten accordingly below.

## Requirements

- **Functional:**
  - `fuelConfig` gains a `baseUnitPrice` (the "giá dầu gốc cấu hình"),
    distinct from the existing live `unitPrice`.
  - `customers` gains `fuelSurchargeSharePct` (`numeric(5,2)`, 0–100). When
    NULL, the feature is off for that customer (surcharge = 0).
  - `trips` gains `fuelSurchargeAmount` (stored, incl-VAT-neutral),
    `fuelSurchargeSnapshot` (jsonb of the inputs at compute time), and a
    `fuelSurchargeSnapshotDirty` boolean (D23) so post-completion drift is
    surfaced to kế toán via the same dirty-queue mechanism as AR/AP.
  - The surcharge is computed on the path that already produces
    `totals.totalFuelLiters` (the `updateTripFigures` flow), NOT at
    `createTrip` (which has no liters in scope — D4).
  - The computed `fuelSurchargeAmount` flows into the debit-note render
    data via `buildTripRenderData` (which today neither accepts nor returns
    it — D5). The wiring is: extend `buildTripRenderData`'s `trip` param
    type + return shape, and populate it at the per-trip render loop site.
  - When the customer has no share-%, or `baseUnitPrice` is unset, or
    `currentFuelPrice ≤ baseFuelPrice`, the surcharge is `0`.
  - Shipment-sync (`syncShipmentAuthorityToTrips`) does **not** re-resolve
    the surcharge (it has no `fuelLiters`/`resolveFuelNorm` in scope — D22);
    re-resolution is deferred to a follow-up. Any later change to
    share-%/base price on a COMPLETED trip must flip
    `fuelSurchargeSnapshotDirty` (D10/D23).
- **Non-functional:**
  - Computation uses the shared `round2dp` then `roundInt` helpers
    (`shared/src/calculations/round.ts`) — financial precision is
    non-negotiable per `AGENTS.md`.
  - Snapshot is auditable: the jsonb stores `currentFuelPrice`,
    `baseFuelPrice`, `quotaLiters`, `customerSharePct`, `customerId`,
    `computedAt`.
  - No new dependency.

## Architecture

```
TRIP FIGURES UPDATE (trip-mutations.service.ts updateTripFigures, ~lines 1028-1080)
  ── this is where totals.totalFuelLiters is already in scope (line 1028, 1080) ──
  existing line 1028: const totals = computeTripTotals(totalsInput);
  existing line 1080: fuelLiters: String(totals.totalFuelLiters),
  ── NEW (after totals computed) ──
  const surcharge = await resolveFuelSurcharge({
    customerId: trip.customerId,
    fuelLiters: totals.totalFuelLiters,   // ← the real integer liter total
    date: trip.departureDate,
  });
  ...persist trips.fuelSurchargeAmount = surcharge.amount,
       trips.fuelSurchargeSnapshot = surcharge.snapshot...

NOTE: createTrip (lines 271-579) does NOT call computeTripTotals and has no
fuelLiters in scope — do NOT wire the surcharge there (D4).

DEBIT NOTE RENDER (corrected per D5 — buildTripRenderData is the gatekeeper)
  today: billingDocument.service.ts:1646-1682 buildTripRenderData()
           - input trip param shape has NO fuelSurchargeAmount field
           - return object has NO fuelSurchargeAmount key
         line 3084: case 'fuelSurchargeAmount': return data.fuelSurchargeAmount ?? null
           (READS from line renderData jsonb; always null because nothing WRITES it)
  ── CHANGE (multi-step, not one bullet) ──
  1. Extend BillingLineRenderData type + buildTripRenderData input `trip` param
     to include fuelSurchargeAmount.
  2. In buildTripRenderData return, set fuelSurchargeAmount: Number(trip.fuelSurchargeAmount ?? 0).
  3. Update both call sites (billingDocument.service.ts:1255, 1416) to pass
     trip.fuelSurchargeAmount through.
  4. Verify Long Minh aggregation (lines 3391-3406) classifies it as a
     service-line amount (it already sums data.fuelSurchargeAmount).
```

### Formula (canonical — also in plan.md)

```
delta        = max(0, currentFuelPrice − baseFuelPrice)
shareFraction= (customerSharePct ?? 0) / 100
surcharge    = roundInt(round2dp(delta × quotaLiters × shareFraction))
```

- If `customerSharePct` is NULL → `shareFraction = 0` → surcharge `0`.
- If `baseFuelPrice` is NULL → treat as feature-off → surcharge `0`
  (and the snapshot records `baseFuelPrice: null`).
- `quotaLiters` is the trip's resolved `fuelLiters` (already an integer from
  `computeTripTotals`).

## Related Code Files

- **Modify:** `backend/src/db/schema.ts:420-431` — add
  `baseUnitPrice: numeric('base_unit_price', { precision: 10, scale: 0 })`
  to `fuelConfig`.
- **Modify:** `backend/src/db/schema.ts` (`customers` table, around line
  282) — add
  `fuelSurchargeSharePct: numeric('fuel_surcharge_share_pct', { precision: 5, scale: 2 })`.
- **Modify:** `backend/src/db/schema.ts` (`trips` table, near the existing
  fuel columns at lines 583-601) — add
  `fuelSurchargeAmount: numeric('fuel_surcharge_amount', { precision: 15, scale: 0 }).notNull().default('0')`,
  `fuelSurchargeSnapshot: jsonb('fuel_surcharge_snapshot')`, and
  `fuelSurchargeSnapshotDirty: boolean('fuel_surcharge_snapshot_dirty').notNull().default(false)` (D23).
- **Modify:** `backend/src/services/pricing.service.ts` — add
  `resolveFuelSurcharge(input)`:
  ```ts
  export async function resolveFuelSurcharge(input: {
    customerId: number;
    fuelLiters: number;
    date?: Date;
  }): Promise<{ amount: number; snapshot: FuelSurchargeSnapshot }> {
    const [customer, config] = await Promise.all([
      db.query.customers.findFirst({ where: eq(customers.id, input.customerId) }),
      db.query.fuelConfig.findFirst(),
    ]);
    const currentPrice = config?.unitPrice ?? null;
    const basePrice    = config?.baseUnitPrice ?? null;
    const sharePct     = customer?.fuelSurchargeSharePct ?? null;
    const amount = computeFuelSurcharge({ currentPrice, basePrice, sharePct, quotaLiters: input.fuelLiters });
    return { amount, snapshot: { currentPrice, basePrice, sharePct, quotaLiters: input.fuelLiters, customerId: input.customerId, computedAt: new Date().toISOString() } };
  }
  ```
- **Create:** `shared/src/calculations/fuelSurcharge.ts` — pure function
  `computeFuelSurcharge({ currentPrice, basePrice, sharePct, quotaLiters })`
  implementing the formula with `round2dp` + `roundInt`. Pure so it is
  unit-testable in `shared` without a DB. Export the snapshot type too.
- **Create:** `shared/src/calculations/fuelSurcharge.test.ts` — table-driven
  unit tests (see Success Criteria).
- **Modify:** `backend/src/services/trip-mutations.service.ts` — wire
  `resolveFuelSurcharge` into `updateTripFigures` (the function that already
  computes `totals.totalFuelLiters` at line 1028 and persists `fuelLiters`
  at line 1080), NOT into `createTrip`. Add `fuelSurchargeAmount` +
  `fuelSurchargeSnapshot` to the UPDATE payload there. (D4/D22)
- **Modify:** `backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts` — the
  render-data chain (D5): (a) extend `buildTripRenderData` input `trip`
  param type (`:1646-1655`) and return shape (`:1661-1676`) to include
  `fuelSurchargeAmount`; (b) update both call sites (`:1255`, `:1416`) to
  pass `trip.fuelSurchargeAmount`; (c) verify the Long Minh aggregator
  (`:3391-3406`) still classifies it correctly. The cited `:3084` is a READ
  site, not a WRITE site — do not edit it expecting the value to appear.
- **Modify:** `shared/src/schemas/index.ts:821-828` (`fuelConfigSchema`) —
  add `baseUnitPrice` (D15). This zod schema is parsed TWICE in the
  governed fuel-config flow (`config.ts:1368` on write, `config.ts:409` on
  apply); zod `.object()` strips unknown keys by default, so without this
