# Phase 4: AP Snapshot & Supplier-Carrier Resolution

## Overview

Rev1 §B4 requires that on completion the system pushes **both** an AR record
(Công nợ Phải thu Khách hàng) **and** an AP record (Công nợ Phải trả
NCC/Chủ xe ngoài) to the công nợ module, as snapshots with a dirty-flag for
post-completion cost edits.

The prior plan `260801-2200` shipped the AR side: `trips.arCostHash` /
`arSnapshotDirty` / `arSnapshotChangedAt` columns
(`schema.ts:675-677`) + `ArSnapshotService` (`ar-snapshot.service.ts`) +
capture-on-completion at `trip-status-machine.service.ts:392` +
markDirty-on-edit at `forwarder.service.ts:328/481/625` &
`field-cost.service.ts:62`. **There is no AP counterpart.**

> **Red-team corrections (D1, D2, D3):** the original draft claimed a
> "money leak" where `externalEntityType === 'SUPPLIER'` external carriers
> post no payable, and proposed fixing `resolveExternalCarrierId`
> (`ledger.service.ts:47-52`). **That premise was wrong.** Every write site
> for `externalEntityType` hardcodes `'CUSTOMER'` (`trip-mutations.service.ts:508/1101/1287`,
> `dispatch-planning.service.ts:1203/1250`) — the `'SUPPLIER'` branch is
> dead code the system can never reach (D1). Even if it were reachable,
> the callers hardcode `entityType:'CARRIER'` + `txnType:EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST`
> (`ledger.service.ts:309-321`), so the fix would misroute supplier payables
> into the CARRIER subledger and collide with customer IDs (separate
> `serial` tables) (D3).
>
> **The REAL AP gap (D2):** the PRD requires AP for "NCC" (suppliers). The
> true supplier payable is the chi-hộ `trip_expenses` row with non-null
> `supplierId` + `buyAmount` (the `COMPANY_DIRECT` settlement path). But
> `LedgerService.postTripCompletion` (`ledger.service.ts:215-345`) posts
> only 5 blocks (customer revenue, driver salary, fuel supplier, external
> CARRIER cost, ancillary fee sell-side) — **it never posts the chi-hộ
> expense buy-side as a `VENDOR_EXPENSE` ledger row.** `VENDOR_EXPENSE` has
> zero write sites in the function. This phase fixes THAT gap, plus adds
> the AP snapshot mirror, plus the net-new accountant queue endpoints.

This phase therefore: (a) adds the AP snapshot mirror columns + service;
(b) fixes the REAL AP gap (chi-hộ `trip_expenses.supplierId` posted as
`VENDOR_EXPENSE` at completion); (c) creates the net-new AR + AP
dirty-queue/recapture endpoints (the AR one was never exposed either — D8);
(d) wires AP capture + markDirty with tx safety.

## Requirements

- **Functional:**
  - `trips` gains `apCostHash`, `apSnapshotDirty`, `apSnapshotChangedAt`,
    mirroring the AR columns.
  - An `ApSnapshotService` mirrors `ArSnapshotService`
    (`captureSnapshot`, `markDirty`, `listDirty`, `recapture`).
  - The AP snapshot payload covers ONLY vendor-payable costs (D14):
    - For `OWN` trips: `totalFuelCost` (when `fuelSupplierId` set) +
      `trip_expenses[]` filtered to `supplierId IS NOT NULL`. NOT
      `driverSalary` (DRIVER entity), `tollCost`, or `totalRoadAllowance`
      (those are internal P&L, not vendor payables — including them would
      spuriously flip `apSnapshotDirty`).
    - For `EXTERNAL` trips: `externalFreightCost` (the CARRIER-entity
      payable, already posted by the existing `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST` block
      at `ledger.service.ts:311-320` for `CUSTOMER`-typed carriers).
  - **The real AP fix (D2):** `postTripCompletion` adds a new posting block
    that emits a `VENDOR_EXPENSE` ledger row for each chi-hộ
    `trip_expenses` row with non-null `supplierId` and
    `settlementMethod === 'COMPANY_DIRECT'`, posting to
    `entityType:'VENDOR', entityId: expense.supplierId`, with
    `paymentTermDaysApplied` from Phase 1's `resolveSupplierPaymentDueDate(…,
    'CHI_HO', …)`. The matching reversal is added to
    `postTripCompletionReverse`. The `validateAncillaryFees` no-op
    (`ledger.service.ts:194-199`) is replaced with real per-supplier
    payload assembly.
  - **`resolveExternalCarrierId` is NOT changed (D1/D3).** The dead
    `'SUPPLIER'` branch is left as-is (or optionally deleted as dead code
    in a follow-up). External carriers are `CUSTOMER`-typed by design
    (schema.ts:858-859, decision D-E/F); their payable already posts via
    the `EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST` block.
  - On `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED`, `ApSnapshotService.captureSnapshot` runs
    after the existing `ArSnapshotService.captureSnapshot`. **AP capture is
    wrapped in try/catch (D11):** on failure it logs, leaves
    `apCostHash = null` with `apSnapshotDirty = true`, and lets the
    completion succeed — degrading to "AP snapshot unavailable, surfaced in
    the dirty queue" rather than rolling back the entire financial close.
  - On post-completion cost edits, a single
    `SnapshotServices.markBothDirty(tripId, txOrDb)` helper (D12) updates
    BOTH `arSnapshotDirty` and `apSnapshotDirty` inside one explicit
    transaction, replacing the pattern of calling AR and AP markDirty
    separately at sites where `txOrDb` may be bare `db`.
  - **Net-new accountant endpoints (D8/D21):** both AR and AP
    dirty-queue/recapture endpoints are created (the AR one was never
    exposed — only the service method exists). Mounted under the financial
    router so they inherit `casbinAuthz('financial')`; CLERK is excluded;
    `recapture` is a mutating action with `registerAuditEvent`.
- **Non-functional:**
  - AP capture failure does NOT abort completion (D11) — degradation path
    via the dirty flag.
  - AR + AP markDirty are atomic (D12).
  - Hash reuses the canonical SHA-256-over-`round2dp` pattern from
    `ar-snapshot.service.ts:28-73`.

## Architecture

```
