# Phase 5: Test Rewrite & QA Closure

## Overview

Own the cross-cutting test surface and the QA-gate closure for all four
feature phases. Each phase ships its own unit tests; this phase owns the
**integration** tests that cross phase boundaries, the **E2E** gate (which
`AGENTS.md` mandates whenever schema / flow / RBAC change — and this plan
changes all three), and the **QA artifact** save-under-`qa/` discipline.

## Requirements

- **Functional:**
  - Integration tests covering the end-to-end O2C paths that the four
    features touch, above and beyond the per-phase unit tests.
  - An E2E suite (or extended existing E2E) exercising:
    - Ops expense auto-fill from the lift matrix (Phase 2).
    - Trip creation producing a non-zero fuel surcharge (Phase 3).
    - Completion posting both AR and AP snapshots; cost edit flipping both
      dirty flags; accountant recapture (Phase 4).
  - Every QA gate in `AGENTS.md` is green, with artifacts saved under
    `qa/` per the naming convention.
- **Non-functional:**
  - No `test.skip`, no `TODO`, no stub assertions (per `AGENTS.md` fix-loop
    rules).
  - Existing tests that break due to the schema additions (e.g. snapshot
    fixtures, ledger row-count assertions) are **updated**, not weakened.

## Architecture

```
INTEGRATION TESTS (backend, vitest/jest — match existing backend test runner)
  backend/src/tests/o2c-rev1.ncc-dual-terms.integration.test.ts   (Phase 1)
  backend/src/tests/o2c-rev1.lift-matrix.integration.test.ts       (Phase 2)
  backend/src/tests/o2c-rev1.fuel-surcharge.integration.test.ts    (Phase 3)
  backend/src/tests/o2c-rev1.ap-snapshot.integration.test.ts       (Phase 4)
  backend/src/tests/o2c-rev1.completion-ar-ap.integration.test.ts  (cross-phase)

NOTE (D18): backend tests live in `backend/src/tests/`, NOT `backend/test/`
(`backend/test/` does not exist; verified: `ls backend/src/tests/*.test.ts`
returns the existing suite). Creating files under `backend/test/` would
silently produce phantom tests that the runner never picks up.

E2E (e2e/ — uses ./run_all.sh per AGENTS.md)
  extend the dispatch / accountant flow specs to assert:
    - Ops lift/lower auto-fill
    - Fuel surcharge on created trip
    - AP dirty queue after post-completion edit
    - Recapture clears the queue

QA ARTIFACTS (qa/)
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_lint.txt
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_backend-typecheck.log
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_backend-test.log
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_frontend-typecheck.log
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_frontend-test.log
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_build.log
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_e2e.log
  qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_review.md   (code-reviewer / self-review report)
```

## Related Code Files

- **Create:** `backend/src/tests/o2c-rev1.*.integration.test.ts` (5 files above).
- **Modify:** existing backend tests that assert on `trips` column sets,
  ledger row counts, or snapshot fixtures — these will need the new columns
  / new ledger row accounted for. Find them via the existing test files in
  `backend/src/tests/` (the actual layout — `backend/test/` does not exist,
  D18).
- **Modify:** `e2e/` specs for the dispatch and accountant flows (locate
  via the existing `e2e/run_all.sh` and the specs it runs).
- **Create:** QA artifacts under `qa/` (one per gate, exact command output).
- **Create:** `qa/2026-08-02_o2c-rev1_review.md` — self-review (or
  `code-reviewer`-agent) report of the full diff.

## Implementation Steps

1. **Inventory existing test breakage.** Before writing new tests, run the
   existing backend + frontend test suites against the migrated schema and
   list every failure caused by the four phases (new columns on `trips`/
   `suppliers`/`customers`/`fuelConfig`/`liftPricing`, the new ledger row
   for SUPPLIER external trips, etc.). Triage each: update the expectation
   to match the new correct behavior. Never `skip`.
2. **Phase-1 integration test.** Create a supplier with both terms; post a
   chi-hộ expense and a freight cost; assert each ledger row carries the
   matching `paymentTermDaysApplied`.
3. **Phase-2 integration test.** Seed the lift matrix subset; call
   `resolveLiftPrice` for LOADED vs EMPTY; assert the Ops resolve endpoint
   returns the right price; assert the unknown-combo fallback is MANUAL.
4. **Phase-3 integration test.** Set `fuelConfig.{unitPrice=25000,
   baseUnitPrice=20000}`, customer `sharePct=50`; create a trip with
   resolved `fuelLiters=100`; assert `trip.fuelSurchargeAmount === 2500`
   and the snapshot jsonb matches; assert the debit-note renderData for
   that trip has a non-null `fuelSurchargeAmount`.
5. **Phase-4 integration test (corrected for D1/D2/D11/D12/D14).**
   - Complete a trip with a chi-hộ `trip_expense` (`supplierId=3`,
     `COMPANY_DIRECT`, `buyAmount=5M`) → assert exactly one new
     `VENDOR_EXPENSE` ledger row to `entityType='VENDOR', entityId=3`
