# O2C Rev1 Extensions: NCC Dual Terms, Lift Matrix, Fuel Surcharge, AP Snapshot

## Outcome

`docs/prd/O2C dev-rev1.md` is the source of truth for the Order-to-Cash
workflow. A precise diff against the shipped rev0 (`docs/prd/O2C dev.md` at
HEAD) shows rev1 keeps every prior decision intact and **adds five new
dev-notes**. The prior plan `260801-2200-o2c-drop-locked-reconciliation`
(status: `done`, shipped in `099abde`) already delivered the LOCKED-drop,
session-scoped delete, POD gate, tạm ứng offset, P&L split, and push MVP.

**This plan delivers ONLY the five NEW rev1 items.** It does not re-implement
anything 260801-2200 shipped.

Concretely:

1. **NCC dual payment terms.** Suppliers (`Nhà cung cấp`) get two separate
   payment-term fields — `chiHoDueDays` (Hạn thanh toán Chi hộ) and
   `cuocDueDays` (Hạn thanh toán Cước) — because a real NCC has two distinct
   debt milestones. Today suppliers have NO payment-term field at all; only
   `customers.paymentTermDays` exists (`schema.ts:282`).
2. **Lift/lower fee matrix + Ops auto-fill.** The `liftPricing` table
   (`schema.ts:479-493`) already exists keyed by `port × containerType ×
   direction`, but it is **missing the `Hàng/Rỗng` (loaded/empty) dimension**
   rev1 requires, it has **no seed data**, and the existing
   `resolveLiftPrice` service (`pricing.service.ts:348-368`) is **not wired**
   into the Ops expense form — staff type the amount manually at
   `ForwarderTripDetailPage.tsx:486-496`. This phase adds the dimension,
   seeds the matrix, and wires auto-fill so Ops staff only pick
   `Cảng + Loại Cont + Hàng/Rỗng` and the system fills the price.
3. **Fuel surcharge auto-trigger.** No fuel-surcharge field, base-price
   config, or customer share-% exists anywhere today. This phase adds the
   config (`baseFuelPrice`, `customerSharePct`), computes
   `(current − base) × quotaLiters × sharePct` at trip creation alongside
   the existing `resolveFreightPrice` + `resolveFuelNorm` calls
   (`trip-mutations.service.ts:365-396`), stores the snapshot on the trip,
   and populates the already-defined-but-always-null
   `fuelSurchargeAmount` debit-note render variable.
4. **Parallel AP snapshot + the REAL supplier-payable fix.** The
   `IN_TRANSIT → COMPLETED` handler (`trip-status-machine.service.ts:354-406`)
   captures an AR snapshot but has **no AP counterpart**. Separately,
   `LedgerService.postTripCompletion` (`ledger.service.ts:215-345`) posts
   only 5 blocks and **never posts chi-hộ `trip_expenses.supplierId` as a
   `VENDOR_EXPENSE`** — the real supplier-payable gap the PRD cares about
   (D2). This phase adds the AP snapshot columns + `ApSnapshotService`,
   fixes the real `VENDOR_EXPENSE` posting gap, wires AP capture with a
   degradation path (capture failure does not abort completion), makes
   AR+AP markDirty atomic, and creates the net-new AR+AP dirty-queue
   endpoints (the AR one was never exposed either). **Note (D1/D3):** the
   earlier "fix `resolveExternalCarrierId` for SUPPLIER carriers" premise
   was wrong — that state is unreachable dead code; it is dropped.
5. **Test rewrite + QA closure.** Each phase above ships its own unit tests;
   this phase owns the cross-cutting integration tests, the E2E gate run, and
   the QA artifact closure under `qa/`.

