## Risk assessment

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|------|----------|------------|
| The real `VENDOR_EXPENSE` post (D2) changes the books — supplier payables now appear in AP aging | **High** | Phase 4 scopes the new post narrowly (only chi-hộ `trip_expenses` with `supplierId` + `COMPANY_DIRECT`); integration test asserts the row-count gain equals the qualifying-expense count; reversal symmetry tested; full E2E + aging reconciliation in Phase 5. |
| Governance bypass on new money fields (D7) | **High** | Add `fuelSurchargeSharePct` to `MATERIAL_CUSTOMER_CONFIG_FIELDS`; add supplier terms to the supplier allowlist; extend `fuelConfigSchema` (D15). Without these, ACCOUNTANT/MANAGER can silently waive surcharges or extend terms. |
| Fuel-surcharge snapshot drifts post-completion without signal (D23) | Medium | Add `fuelSurchargeSnapshotDirty`; flip it when `fuelConfig` or share-% changes on COMPLETED trips; expose recapture alongside AR/AP. |
| `fuelConfigSchema` strips `baseUnitPrice` → feature silently off (D15) | Medium | Make the schema extension a Success Criterion; the governed apply path parses twice. |
| AR + AP `markDirty` diverge when `txOrDb` is bare `db` (D12) | Medium | `SnapshotServices.markBothDirty` forces one explicit tx. |
| AP capture failure aborts completion (D11) | Medium | try/catch degrades to `apSnapshotDirty=true`; completion succeeds. |
| `liftPricing` seed double-inserts without wipe (D17) | Low | UNIQUE index on the full key + `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` seed. |
| Lift-resolve selector race overwrites price (D13) | Medium | `useQuery` keyed on selectors or `AbortController`. |
| Forwarder can't reach lift-resolve endpoint under `config` RBAC (D9) | Medium | Mount under forwarder portal router; scope response to single resolved price. |
| Migration has no rollback tooling (D16) | Low | `drizzle-kit` is forward-only; each phase documents the manual rollback SQL. |
| Real supplier tax codes in existing seed impersonate real entities in non-dev envs (D20) | Low (pre-existing) | Out of scope for this plan; flag as a separate concern. Each phase's new seed additions use the existing pattern and must not worsen it. |

## Acceptance criteria (whole plan)

1. A supplier with `chiHoDueDays=15, cuocDueDays=30` returns the correct
   due date when the ledger posts a chi-hộ expense (`VENDOR_EXPENSE`,
   `FUEL_EXPENSE`) vs a freight cost (`EXTERNAL_CARRIER_COST`) — verified
   by integration test against `resolveSupplierPaymentDueDate` + the
   `paymentTermDaysApplied` actually written on the ledger row.
2. On the Ops expense form, selecting `LIFTING` + a port + container type +
   load state auto-fills `buyAmount` from `liftPricing` (seeded, via the
   forwarder-portal resolve endpoint — D9); the user can still override;
   the resolved-vs-actual delta is shown; rapid selector changes are
   race-safe (D13).
3. Running a trip through `updateTripFigures` for a customer with
   `fuelSurchargeSharePct=50`, `baseFuelPrice=20000`,
   `currentFuelPrice=25000`, `quotaLiters=100` produces
   `fuelSurchargeAmount = 2500` on the trip AND the same value appears in
   the debit-note render data via `buildTripRenderData` (D5 — no longer
   null).
4. Completing a trip with a chi-hộ `trip_expense` (`supplierId` set,
   `COMPANY_DIRECT`) posts exactly one new `VENDOR_EXPENSE` ledger row to
   `entityType='VENDOR', entityId=<supplierId>` (D2 — today: zero);
   populates `apCostHash`; reversal symmetry holds. `resolveExternalCarrierId`
   is unchanged (D1/D3 — phantom fix dropped).
5. AP capture failure does not abort completion (D11); AR+AP markDirty are
   atomic (D12); both AR + AP dirty-queue endpoints are live and
   `casbinAuthz('financial')`-gated (D8).
6. Every QA gate in `AGENTS.md` is green with artifacts saved under `qa/`:
   `pnpm lint`, `cd backend && npx tsc --noEmit && pnpm test`,
   `cd frontend && npx tsc -b && pnpm test`, `make build`,
   `cd e2e && ./run_all.sh` (E2E required — schema + RBAC + flow changed).

