# Customer Service to Finance Workflow

## Outcome

Implement the operating chain `Booking -> Customer Service -> Điều vận -> Phát sinh chi phí -> CUS kiểm tra chi phí -> Lập Debit Note -> Kế toán duyệt -> Xuất hóa đơn -> Theo dõi công nợ -> Thu tiền -> Báo cáo lợi nhuận` by reusing the repo's current authorities: `shipments` (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:2305`), `billingDocuments` (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:825`), `paymentReceipts` (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:2584`), `paymentAllocations` (`backend/src/db/schema.ts:2633`), and the existing customer receivable snapshot (`backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:133`).

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A["Booking"] --> B["Customer Service"]
  B --> C["Điều vận"]
  C --> D["Phát sinh chi phí"]
  D --> E["CUS kiểm tra chi phí"]
  E --> F["Debit Note"]
  F --> G["Kế toán duyệt"]
  G --> H["Hóa đơn / tham chiếu pháp lý"]
  H --> I["AR và nhắc nợ"]
  I --> J["Thu tiền và phân bổ"]
  J --> K["Lợi nhuận và dashboard"]
  D --> L["AP nhà cung cấp"]
  L --> M["Thanh toán AP"]
  J --> N["Treasury tiền mặt / ngân hàng"]
  M --> N
```

## Scope

- Re-baseline the workflow around current shipment, expense, billing-document, governance, receivable, payable, credit, allocation, reminder, profit, and dashboard services.
- Keep debit note, invoice, AR/AP, and cash reporting in one traceable chain with additive migrations only.
- Deliver customer-service coordination as auditable shipment interaction/state tracking, not a new chat platform.
- Keep executive reporting on existing `ADMIN` / `MANAGER` reach; do not introduce `Role.CEO`.

## Explicitly Out Of Scope

- A second ledger, parallel billing lifecycle, or direct-write finance workaround.
- Treating debit note and legal/tax invoice as the same thing before Phase 1 resolves the adapter boundary.
- Full two-way customer portal messaging, customer self-service shipment mutation, or customer-driven billing edits.
- Inventing treasury balances from AR/AP totals without an explicit company-cash authority.

## Authority Chain

- Booking and dossier authority starts on shipment create/update/quick-create (`backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:192`, `backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:235`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:433`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:557`).
- Dispatch handoff remains shipment-driven and idempotent (`backend/src/routes/shipments.ts:378`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:1523`, `backend/src/services/shipment.service.ts:1502`).
- Recoverable-cost and debit-note assembly stays inside `billing_documents` and its governance flow (`backend/src/services/billingDocument.service.ts:950`, `backend/src/services/billing-document-governance.service.ts:295`, `backend/src/services/debit-note-lifecycle.service.ts:40`).
- Customer receivables remain a snapshot over trips, service fees, billing documents, and debt offsets (`backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:7`, `backend/src/services/customer-receivable-authority.service.ts:133`).
- Cash application stays on payment receipts plus allocations, with explicit unapplied balance handling (`backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:1060`, `backend/src/services/payment-allocation.service.ts:1101`).
- Profitability stays on current P&L and distribution services; treasury KPI work cannot start until company-cash authority is explicit (`backend/src/services/pnl.service.ts:29`, `backend/src/services/dashboard-stats.service.ts:17`, `backend/src/services/dashboard-widgets.service.ts:44`, `backend/src/services/company-info.service.ts:21`, `backend/src/services/ledger.service.ts:40`).

## Phases

| Phase | Name | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Authority contracts and migration safety](./phase-01-authority-contracts-and-migration-safety.md) | Completed |
| 2 | [CUS shipment and customer coordination](./phase-02-cus-shipment-and-customer-coordination.md) | Completed |
| 3 | [Recoverable costs Debit Note and invoice handoff](./phase-03-recoverable-costs-debit-note-and-invoice-handoff.md) | Completed |
| 4 | [AR AP and treasury controls](./phase-04-ar-ap-and-treasury-controls.md) | Completed |
| 5 | [Profitability and CEO dashboard](./phase-05-profitability-and-ceo-dashboard.md) | Completed |
| 6 | [Role workspaces rollout and closed-loop QA](./phase-06-role-workspaces-rollout-and-closed-loop-qa.md) | In Progress |

## Dependency Graph

- Phase 1 blocks every other phase because it locks the invoice adapter boundary, treasury authority, migration order, and snapshot rules.
- Phases 2 and 3 both depend on Phase 1 and may proceed in parallel. Debit-note
  generation consumes stable existing shipment/customer/legal-entity IDs, not
  the new customer communication timeline.
- Phase 3 blocks Phase 4 because AR/AP and collection controls must read issued
  Debit Note / invoice-reference outcomes instead of draft shipment state.
- Phase 4 depends on Phase 3 and blocks Phase 5 because collections, offsets, payables, and treasury balances feed profitability and executive KPIs.
- Phase 5 depends on Phase 4 and blocks Phase 6 because dashboard assertions are only valid once the finance chain is settled.
- Phase 6 depends on all prior phases and owns final role-matrix QA, rollout sequencing, and rollback rehearsal.

## Cross-Plan Relationships

- `plans/260727-1230-approved-business-rules/plan.md` is the finance-rule baseline for debit-note lock, payment-date authority, governance, and due-date behavior.
- `plans/260729-1908-shipment-operations-workspace/plan.md` is the shipment baseline for dossier fields, dispatch, optimistic locking, and change requests.
- `plans/260729-1248-customer-portal-overhaul/plan.md` and `plans/260726-2145-customer-portal-repair/plan.md` are the customer portal UI and responsive baselines.
- `plans/silversea-prd-roadmap/plan.md` and its wave files are directional context only. They inform sequencing, but they are not hard blockers if this plan can prove a safer authority path.

## Acceptance Criteria

- Shipment remains the only source of truth for booking, dossier, dispatch-readiness inputs, and shipment-to-trip linkage.
- Debit-note, invoice, receivable, payable, payment, and profitability flows reuse the current billing/ledger stack instead of duplicating it.
- Draft shipments may stay partial, while dispatch-readiness remains advisory until mandatory dossier data is complete.
- Customer communication v1 is an auditable shipment interaction/update log plus notification and acknowledgement records, not a general chat inbox.
- Direct shipment, trip, container, customer, route, operator, and sales attribution is snapshotted for profitability; shared overhead stays visible and unallocated until policy exists.
- Accepted dispatcher, salesperson, and financial posting/version ownership are implemented before profitability activation; missing historical evidence remains explicit and is never guessed.
- All executive KPIs render full `vi-VN` digits. Cash/bank metrics use the
  explicit Phase 4 source-linked book-balance authority, preserve
  partial/unavailable state, and never imply statement reconciliation or infer
  balance from AR/AP.
- `CUSTOMER`, `CLERK`, `ACCOUNTANT`, `MANAGER`, and `ADMIN` capabilities stay consistent across backend RBAC, frontend routes, and visible nav.
- Each phase ends with targeted tests, then repo QA gates, with complete artifacts saved under `qa/` during implementation.

## Unresolved Decisions To Close Early

- **Blocking — legal invoice authority:** finance/legal must accept the reference-only model (Debit Note remains the sole AR posting) or approve a redesigned one-posting replacement/alias lifecycle before provider-specific Phase 3 work.
- **Blocking — treasury foundation and cutover:** approve explicit
  accounts/source-linked movements, per-account opening-balance watermark,
  pending-action and payment-contract versioning, physical transaction
  identity, governance/RBAC, and post-cutover rollback compatibility before
  payment mutation. Statement reconciliation, internal transfers, close/reopen,
  and a full treasury workspace are deferred to a separate approved plan.
- **Blocking — customer communication authority:** name how milestones, delivery logs, immutable customer-visible content, and acknowledgements compose before adding persistence.
- **Blocking — attribution:** approve the owning workflows for accepted dispatcher, versioned salesperson assignment, and the financial posting/version ID shared by P&L and profitability.
- **Blocking for each surface — role/action matrix:** resolve CUS/CLERK row scope, treasury read/operate/admin, and executive-reporting endpoint access before exposing the corresponding API/UI.
- **Non-blocking layout choice:** use the verified shipment register/detail shell first; add a dedicated CUS lane only if implementation evidence proves the shared workspace cannot remain bounded and role-clear.

## Rollout And Rollback Strategy

- Roll forward with additive schema and route changes first, then expose new UI slices behind role-aware reachability.
- Keep old shipment, debit-note, and reporting paths readable until the new workflow proves parity.
- Roll back by disabling the new workflow surfaces and reverting additive writes, without deleting core shipment, billing-document, or ledger data.
- After treasury cutover, never restore a build/mode that can post ledger money without the linked treasury movement. Gate direct-money actions as one unit unless the rollback build meets the treasury compatibility floor.
- Do not run destructive migrations, data rewrites, or ledger backfills without a separate, tested rollback script.

## QA Gates For Implementation

