# Customer Workflow Alignment and Data Cutover

## Outcome

Make the app follow the customer’s documented operating chain, then load only
approved customer data into local and staging while preserving every login,
credential, role, status, and usable access relationship.

This is not a blanket reset. The cutover has two distinct lanes:

1. **Preserved control plane:** user identities, credentials, roles, account
   status, every user-owned row, business-unit/customer access, user-linked
   driver identities, settings, governance, period locks, and audit evidence.
2. **Validated business data:** approved customer/vendor/factory/port/fleet
   master data and approved operational/financial rows, imported through a
   repeatable manifest after every source row is classified as authoritative,
   template-only, or rejected.

## Current Verdict

The app is **partially aligned, not yet cutover-ready**.

| Customer workflow area | Current state | Required before cutover |
|---|---|---|
| Booking, dossier, containers, documents, dispatch | Implemented on `shipments` and linked `trips` | Preserve this authority; fill only field/workspace gaps |
| Pricing, lift fees, recoverable costs | Implemented in separate authorities | Add the approved workbook fuel-adjustment/contract policy without a second calculator |
| Debit Note, AR/AP, receipts, allocation, aging, reminders | Strong existing financial authority | Resolve legal-invoice/treasury decisions in the blocking plan; never reload sample amounts as truth |
| P&L and dashboard | Implemented read models | Reconcile to imported authoritative transactions; no hardcoded workbook totals |
| CUS/dispatch workspace | Partial composition | Add the missing task-oriented view and role-safe actions |
| Contract timing and SLAs | Missing/partial | Versioned customer contract policy: payment, cutoff, detention, acceptance, force majeure |
| Factory/warehouse operating rules | Mostly free text | Approved first-class master/data contract or deliberate bounded text model |
| Customer tax-risk evaluation | Not verified as an implemented authority | Decide whether the workbook note is required; use an approved provider or keep an explicit unavailable state |
| Data replacement | Local demo seed/reset exists | New dry-run, preservation, import, reconciliation, and rollback contract |

## Evidence Baseline

Customer-source authority and field/formula inventory:

- `./research/customer-source-audit.md`
- `docs/BIẾU MẪU BÁO CÁO/29.7 - DATA PM.xlsx`
- `docs/BIẾU MẪU BÁO CÁO/29.7 - DEMO KẾ TOÁN.xlsx`
- `docs/BIẾU MẪU BÁO CÁO/BẢNG DEMO PHẦN MỀM 2026- CUS- ĐIỀU XE.xlsx`
- three contracts under
  `docs/BIẾU MẪU BÁO CÁO/FILE HỢP ĐỒNG MẪU UP PM/`

Current-code/data audit:

- `./research/app-data-audit.md`
- `plans/260730-2232-customer-service-finance-workflow/plan.md`
- `plans/260730-2232-customer-service-finance-workflow/reports/phase-01-decision-gates-and-authority-map.md`

The local baseline observed on 2026-07-31 is intentionally large:
3,621 users, 1,893 customers, 3,733 shipments, 892 trips, 942,358
`user_shipment_links`, and 5,687,108 notifications. These counts are evidence
of cutover risk, not constants; execution must recapture both environments.

## Authority Rules

- Contract text controls customer-specific acceptance, detention, payment, and
  reconciliation timing.
- Accepted rules in `docs/prd/business-logic-qa-proposals.md` apply when the
  contract is silent.
- Workbook layouts define field/report requirements, but example rows and
  amounts are not production truth without explicit row-level approval.
- Existing shipment, billing-document, payment-allocation, ledger, and P&L
  services remain the only authorities. No parallel spreadsheet-shaped ledger.
- Application/import code uses Drizzle. Infrastructure backup/restore uses
  `pg_dump`/`pg_restore`.

## Decision Gates

Implementation may audit and build dry-run tooling before these close, but no
business-data deletion or staging write may occur.

1. **Source rows:** which sheets/rows are approved master data, approved
   transactions, templates, or examples?
2. **Contract mapping:** which contract/version applies to each customer?
   The samples conflict on 30/60-day payment, 8/24-hour detention, and
   explicit/deemed acceptance.
3. **Account mapping:** how do the 228 active CUSTOMER accounts and 57 linked
   drivers map to imported customer/driver records?
4. **Accounting boundary:** preserve all finance history and the customer
   anchors referenced by it, import deltas, or intentionally create a fresh
   accounting sandbox? Default: preserve with stable customer IDs.
5. **User-owned data boundary:** notifications, push subscriptions, onboarding
   state, agent conversations/messages/metrics, actor-linked idempotency, audit
   history, and every other user-FK or semantic-user reference are preserved
   byte-for-byte by default. Any named exclusion requires separate explicit
   approval and its own retention/archival plan; it is not inferred from
   “clean up demo data.”
6. **Staging approval:** approve maintenance window, tested dump, restore
   rehearsal, staging-specific identity/mapping snapshot, dry-run report, and
   named rollback owner.

## Phases

| Phase | Name | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Customer source and workflow authority](./phase-01-customer-source-and-workflow-authority.md) | In Progress |
| 2 | [Application gap remediation](./phase-02-application-gap-remediation.md) | Pending |
| 3 | [Import and preservation tooling](./phase-03-import-and-preservation-tooling.md) | Pending |
| 4 | [Local dry run and cutover](./phase-04-local-dry-run-and-cutover.md) | Pending |
| 5 | [Staging cutover](./phase-05-staging-cutover.md) | Pending |
| 6 | [Closed loop verification](./phase-06-closed-loop-verification.md) | Pending |

## Dependencies

- Plan-level blocker:
  `plans/260730-2232-customer-service-finance-workflow/` must close its legal
  invoice, treasury, communication, and attribution decisions before this plan
  mutates finance or performs staging cutover.
- Plan-level blocker:
  `plans/260801-0942-end-to-end-dispatch-workflow/` must deliver the approved
  factory/warehouse authority, FCL/LCL fulfillment-task model, dispatch order,
  driver milestones, e-POD approval, aggregate shipment closure, and Debit
  Note template integration before customer workflow data is cut over.
- Phase 1 blocks Phases 2 and 3.
- Phase 3's schema-independent parser/validator may start after Phase 1, but its
  apply/reconciliation layer requires Phase 2 and the blocking finance plan.
- Phase 4 requires Phases 2 and 3 green.
- Phase 5 requires a green Phase 4, explicit staging approval, and a verified
  backup restore.
- Phase 6 runs after both environments are cut over and reconciled.

## Definition of Done

- A signed source manifest classifies every imported row and contract policy.
- No imported example transaction or workbook total is treated as real history.
- Every existing `users` row retains the same immutable identity/profile,
  credential hash, role, status, account type, timestamps, and deletion state.
  Only `customer_id` may change, and only through an approved old-to-new
  customer mapping; business-unit/driver access remains usable.
- Every user-owned row is accounted for in a complete FK and semantic-reference
  matrix and remains byte-for-byte unchanged unless a named exclusion is
  separately approved.
- Every environment has an approved default-deny disposition manifest with
  exact `PRESERVE | REMAP | REBUILD | DELETE` predicates and expected counts;
  unlisted tables or rows cannot be mutated.
- Preserved history has zero stale typed, polymorphic, JSON, snapshot, audit,
  notification, idempotency, finance, or governance entity references.
- Derived shipment scope is rebuilt against new shipment IDs and proves no
  cross-customer visibility.
- Local replay returns the already committed result for the same environment,
  manifest, sources, schema, and tool build; primary keys, timestamps,
  sequences, links, and counts remain unchanged.
- Staging dump restores successfully in isolation before the maintenance window.
- Master, operational, and finance reconciliations pass with zero unexplained
  deltas.
- Role/workflow QA passes on desktop and mobile for ADMIN, MANAGER,
  ACCOUNTANT, CLERK, DRIVER, FORWARDER, and CUSTOMER.
- Every affected automated/manual QA run is saved under `qa/`.

## Explicitly Out of Scope

- Production cutover or production data mutation.
- Importing unapproved personal, banking, tax, or sample financial data.
- Replacing the ledger, billing-document, shipment, or payment authorities.
- Creating a new legal-invoice or treasury model outside the blocking plan.
- Committing, pushing, or deploying without a separate user request.
