# End-to-End Dispatch Operations Workflow

## Outcome

Implement `Master data -> Lô hàng -> Tác vụ thực hiện -> Điều xe -> Tài xế -> e-POD -> Duyệt/khóa -> Debit Note` as one audited workflow. Reuse `shipments`, `trips`, driver progress, notifications, Debit Note templates, billing documents, and ledger authority; replace the current one-live-trip-per-shipment constraint with a clean fulfillment model suitable for this new product.

## Locked Decisions

- CUS is existing role `CLERK`; Điều vận is `MANAGER`/`ADMIN`; Kế toán is `ACCOUNTANT`.
- FCL creates exactly one fulfillment task per container. LCL v1 creates exactly one task/trip per shipment and cannot split across vehicles.
- Dispatcher explicitly selects carrier, plate/truck, and driver. Plate may suggest, never auto-authorize, a driver.
- Driver completion sets the owned trip to `COMPLETED`; scoped CUS or Điều vận first-winner approval sets it to `LOCKED`; ACCOUNTANT is read-only for operational approval.
- All active tasks must have accepted e-POD and `LOCKED` trips before the shipment becomes `CLOSED`.
- Notifications use durable in-app records and Web Push only.
- No backward-compatibility layer is required: there is no running production system.

## Scope Boundary

In scope: validated import from `docs/quytrinh/`; operational-site master; FCL/LCL intake; fulfillment decomposition; bounded dispatch workspace; driver milestones; e-POD; aggregate closure; Long Minh Debit preset; role/responsive/volume QA.

Out of scope: Zalo; GPS live map or continuous tracking; native app rewrite; route optimization; chat; legal-invoice provider; full treasury; production deployment; customer-data cutover execution.

## Phases

| Phase | Name | Status |
|-------|------|--------|
| 1 | [Authority and migration foundation](./phase-01-authority-and-migration-foundation.md) | Completed |
| 2 | [Master data and shipment intake](./phase-02-master-data-and-shipment-intake.md) | Completed |
| 3 | [Fulfillment tasks and dispatch](./phase-03-fulfillment-tasks-and-dispatch.md) | Completed |
| 4 | [Driver execution and app notifications](./phase-04-driver-execution-and-app-notifications.md) | Completed |
| 5 | [e-POD review and shipment closure](./phase-05-e-pod-review-and-shipment-closure.md) | Completed |
| 6 | [Debit Note export and closed-loop rollout](./phase-06-debit-note-export-and-closed-loop-rollout.md) | In Progress |

## Dependencies

- Phase 1 blocks all schema/API work. Phase 2 depends on Phase 1.
- Phase 3 depends on Phases 1-2. Phase 4 depends on Phase 3. Phase 5 depends on Phases 3-4.
- Phase 6 depends on Phases 2-5 and blocks `plans/260731-1631-customer-workflow-data-cutover/`.
- Existing `plans/260730-2232-customer-service-finance-workflow/` remains authoritative for broader finance, but its legal-invoice/treasury decisions do not block this operational scope.

## Acceptance Criteria

- Stage-0 import classifies every workbook row; blank/template/example rows never become master or financial data.
- FCL `N` containers produce `N` independently assignable tasks/trips; LCL produces one.
- No duplicate task/trip/order is created by retries or concurrent dispatchers.
- Driver milestones, e-POD submission, review, trip lock, shipment closure, and Debit export are traceable end to end.
- CLERK scope is enforced live; ACCOUNTANT cannot dispatch, approve e-POD, or lock trips.
- Dispatch caps task pages at 50 and fleet pages at 100; with 55 vehicles and 500+ tasks it renders only loaded rows, uses at most 8 queue-query statements, and meets the controlled warm-response budget of 1 second.
- Desktop, tablet, 390px, and 320px views have no page overflow, preserve actions, and use accessible controls.
- All affected gates in `AGENTS.md` are green with exact artifacts under `qa/`.

## Delivery Strategy

Use normal forward schema migrations, reset/reseed dev data when useful, then verify local and staging. No legacy dual-read, dual-write, shadow mode, compatibility floor, or production cutover is required. Roll back unreleased work through forward corrective migrations or a clean dev/staging reset; never fork billing or ledger authority.

## Open Questions

None. Business decisions are locked above.
